===Etymology===
{{lbor|tl|ceb|adlaw||sun}}, from Proto-Bisayan ''*qadlaw'', from Proto-Central Philippine ''*qaldaw'', from {{der|tl|phi-pro|*qaljaw}}, from {{der|tl|poz-pro|*qaləjaw}}. Proposed by Eusebio Daluz by the 20{{sup|th}} century to use the Visayan word instead of {{cog|tl|araw||sun; day}} to distinguish {{m-g|sun}} and {{m-g|day}} to have equivalents for {{ncog|es|sol||sun}} and {{ncog|es|día||day}}. {{doublet|tl|araw}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|adláw}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|adláw|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|neologism}}

# [[sun]]
#: {{syn|tl|araw|sol|q2=rare}}

====Derived terms====
