Page 664 Albay: Already saw {{tl-pr}}, skipping: {{tl-pr|Albáy|hmp=albay}}
Page 664 Albay: Skipped, no changes
Page 664 Albay: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
[[File:1602 map of Albay in southern Luzon province of the Philippines.jpg|thumb|Map of ''La Baye la baye'' ({{w|Albay}}) (1602) by {{w|Olivier van Noort}}]]
{{bor+|tl|es|Albay}}, as in {{compound|es|al|[[bahía|baye]]|t1=the|t2=bay|nocat=1}}, or in longer variant names, La Baye la baye ("The Bay of Baye") or Bay la Bay ("Bay of Bay") as in {{w|Olivier van Noort}}'s 1602 Map of ''La Baye la baye'' ({{w|Albay}}), where the first {{m|es|[[bahía|baye]]}} or {{m|es|[[bahía|bay]]}} is an old variant spelling of {{cog|es|bahía|t=[[bay]] (geographical feature)}}, but the second {{m|es|baye}} or {{m|es|bay}} refers to its previous derivation from {{der|tl|es|Al Baybay}}, which itself came from {{der|tl|es|al|t=the}} + {{der|tl|bcl|baybay|t=shore}}, where finally, it was simplified or shortened to just its present form to do away with any confusion. The name originally referred to the coastal settlement of ''Sawangan'', now the port district of {{w|Legazpi, Albay|Legazpi City}}. In April 3, 1574, the place used to also be called “[[Baybayon]]”, which became an encomienda assigned by Philippine Governor-General {{w|Guido de Lavezaris}} to Juan Guerra.<ref>{{cite-web|work=Official Government Website of Republic of the Philippines Province of Albay Region V - Bicol|title=About Albay|url=http://albay.gov.ph/about/|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20210722030347/http://albay.gov.ph/about/|archivedate=22 July 2021}}</ref> In time, the name was also later applied to the province over which the town of Albay (now Legazpi City) served as the capital.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|Albáy|hmp=albay}}

===Proper noun===
{{tl-proper noun|Albáy|b=+}}

# {{q|lalawigan/probinsiya ng ~}} {{place|tl|t=Albay|province|c/Philippines}}

====See also====
{{col3|tl|Camarines Norte|Camarines Sur|Catanduanes|Sorsogon|Masbate}}

===References===
<references/>
