Page 1149 ang: Already saw {{tl-pr}}, skipping: {{tl-pr|hmp=Ang}}
Page 1149 ang: Skipped, no changes
Page 1149 ang: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|'ng||contraction|informal|after words ending with vowel, usually in [[set phrase]]s}}

===Etymology===
From Proto-Central Philippine ''*aŋ''. Cognate with {{cog|bcl|an}}, {{cog|ceb|ang}}, {{cog|hil|ang}}, {{cog|war|an}}. See also {{cog|pam|ing}} and {{cog|tsg|in}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|hmp=Ang}}

===Article===
{{tl-head|article|b=+}}

# {{n-g|direct marker for all nouns other than personal proper nouns}}
#: {{ux|tl|[[tumakbo|Tumakbo]] '''ang [[lalaki]]'''.|'''The man''' ran.}}
#: {{ux|tl|Kinain ng pusa '''ang isda'''.|The cat ate '''the fish'''.}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''Ang kidlat''' ay gumuguhit ng mga ugat sa taniman ng langit.|('''The''') '''lightning''' sketches roots under the soil of the sky.}}
# {{n-g|used with a quality for emphasis and to give it an adjectival meaning}}
#: {{syn|tl|bang|q1=Rizal|dang|q2=Cavite|budang|q3=Nueva Ecija}}
#: {{uxi|tl|'''Ang''' ganda!|'''How''' pretty!|lit='''The''' beauty!}}
#: {{uxi|tl|'''Ang''' tapang!|'''How''' audacious!|lit='''The''' audacity!}}

====Usage notes====
* This particle is analyzed as the definite article (i.e., ''the'') when used alone, and the indefinite article (i.e., ''a'' or ''an'') when used with the numeral {{m|tl|isa||one}}.
*: {{uxi|tl|'''ang''' araw|'''the''' sun}}
*: {{uxi|tl|'''ang isang''' tao|'''a''' person}}
* Direct personal proper nouns (''primarily names'') are marked with {{m|tl|si}}.

====See also====
{{tl-markers}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:KWF Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:CEDOF|1|18}}
* {{cite-journal|author=Robert Blust|title=The Proto—Malayo-Polynesian Multiplicative Ligature *ŋa: A Reply to Reid|work=Oceanic Linguistics|page=538–566|year=2012|url=https://www.jstor.org/stable/23321867|volume=51|issue=2|issn=0029-8115}}

-------- end text --------
