Page 1169 anghang: Skipped, no changes
Page 1169 anghang: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|hanghang}}

===Etymology===
{{glossary|Apheresis}} of {{IPAchar|/h/}} from variant {{m|tl|hanghang}}. Exact etymology is unknown but possibilities are:
* From Central {{inh|tl|phi-pro|*haŋhaŋ}}
* {{rdp|tl|}} of {{m|tl|halang||spiciness; pungence}} with elision of {{IPAchar|/l/}}.

Compare {{cog|pag|hanghang}}, {{cog|ceb|hang}}/{{m|ceb|halang}}, and {{cog|hil|kahang}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|angháng}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|angháng|b=+}}

# [[spiciness]]; [[hotness]] of [[flavor]]; [[sharpness]] in [[taste]] or [[smell]]
#: {{syn|tl|hanghang|q1=of taste|sangsang|q2=of smell|halang|q3=dialectal|paras|q4=Bataan|askad|q5=obsolete}}
#: {{ux|tl|Ang '''anghang''' naman!|So '''spicy'''!|lit=[That's] really the '''spice'''!}}
# [[pungency]]; [[piquancy]]

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|maanghang|kaanghangan|anghangan}}

====See also====
{{col3|tl|pahang}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:map:ACD|haŋhaŋ}}
