[[Image:Large bonfire.jpg|thumb|225px|apoy]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|ipoy||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|tl|poz-pro|*hapuy}} (compare {{cog|ch|guåfi}}, {{cog|haw|ahi}}, {{cog|ms|api}}, {{cog|mi|ahi}}, and {{cog|sm|afi}}), from {{inh|tl|map-pro|*Sapuy}} (compare {{cog|pwn|sapuy}}), possibly through a borrowing from Dumagat, Sambal, etc., since evidence indicates that one would expect ''*hapoy'' in Tagalog, according to Zorc.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|apóy}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|apóy|b=+}}

# [[fire]] {{gl|oxidation reaction}}
#: {{syn|tl|puwego}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|apuyan|apuyin|mag-apoy|kinakain ng apoy|maapoy|magpaapoy|mainapoy|pag-apuyin|pamatay-apoy|apuybilos|takaw-apoy|may apoy sa tuktok|magsaapoy|dagat-dagatang apoy}}

====See also====
{{col3|tl|sunog}}

