===Etymology 2===
{{bor+|tl|hil|asindero}}, from {{suffix|hil|asin|dero|t1=salt}}, coined as a [[pun]] to the above sense of a [[hacienda]] [[owner]] to bring pride upon the [[occupation]].<ref>{{cite-web|work=Asinderos de Miag-ao: Part II - The Art of Farming Budbud Salt|url=http://sulugarden.com/articles/blog/asinderos-de-miag-ao-part-2/|last=Matias|first=Jonathan R.|last2=Posecion|first2=Norman|last3=Sucgang|first3=Coleen P.|year=2015}}</ref>

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# [[salt]] [[farmer]]; [[saltmaker]]
#: {{syn|tl|mag-aasin|mag-iiras}}
#* {{quote-web
|tl
|url=http://nanovio.blogspot.com/2008/04/asin-dero.html
|date=April 10, 2008
|title='''Asin-dero'''
|author=Norman Novio
|work=Minding Mindoro and Beyond
|passage=''Ang mga tinawag nating “'''Asin-dero'''”,.. ang mag-aasin na siyang kumakayod, naghahakot at nagmi-maintain ng banigan ang dehado dahil sa hindi makatarungang partihan (70/30) pabor sa may-ari ng asinan!''}}
#* {{quote-web
|tl
|url=https://issuu.com/the.pillar.ursb/docs/le_pilier_2018-2019_final_low_reso/s/11617940
|year=2018/2019
|title=SI DOM, ANG '''ASINDERO'''
|author=Dominic Rapal; Shan Rencel Vitor
|work=Le Pilier A.Y 2018-2019
|publisher=The Pillar URSB
|passage=''Ako si Dom, ang '''asindero''', at ito ang maalat kong kwento, Pinalaki ako ng aking mga magulang sa tabing-dagat kung saan namana ko ang aming “family business” – pag-aasin.''}}

=====Alternative forms=====
* {{alt|tl|asin-dero}}

