===Etymology===
From a {{syncopic form|tl|nocap=1}} of {{m|tl|ayawan}}, from Proto-Central-Philippine ''*áyaw'' (“to leave (behind)”) + ''-an'', with semantic shift originally meaning “it leaves (me)” according to Zorc (1983). Blust & Trussel also posit {{der|tl|poz-pro|*away}}, with {{glossary|metathesis}} (c.f. {{cog|pag|awey}}). See also {{m|tl|ayaw}}. {{doublet|tl|iwan}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|aywán,ewan<q:colloquial>}}

===Interjection===
{{tl-head|interjection|aywán|b=+}}

# [[I don't know]]!; [[I]] [[forgot]]!
#: {{syn|tl|malay|ilam|q2=Mindoro}}
# [[whatever]]

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|aywan ko|aywan ko sa iyo}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|aywán|b=+}}

# [[ignorant]]; [[not]] [[known]] {{q|only used with indirect pronouns or with ''kay'' or ''ng''}}
#: {{syn|tl|di-malaman}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|aywán|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|colloquial}}

# something or someone which cannot even be [[understand|understood]], [[describe]]d, or [[explain]]ed
#: {{ux|tl|Kausapin mo na nga yang '''aywan''' na iyon.|Please talk right now with that '''person I can't even describe'''}}
#: {{ux|tl|Itong mabigat na '''aywan''', pano ko dadalhin diyan?|This heavy '''thing I can't even explain''', how am I bringing it there?}}
# [[idiot]]; [[moron]]
#: {{ux|tl|Alam mo, parang '''aywan''' na naman si Jejomar.|You know, Jejomar is acting like an '''idiot'''.|lit=Jejomar is like '''something I can't understand'''}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|tl|parang aywan}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:KWF Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1860}}
* {{R:CEDOF|1|30}}
* {{R:map:ACD|away₃}}
* {{cite-book|author=Constantino Lendoyro|title=The Tagalog Language: A Comprehensive Grammatical Treatise Adapted to Self-instruction and Particularly Designed for Use of Those Engaged in Government Service, Or in Business Or Trade in the Philippines|year=1909|publisher=J. Fajardo|url=https://books.google.com.ph/books?id=ScGPq7i8s4YC&pg=315#v=onepage&q&f=false}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1613}}
** page 446: “Noſe) Ayavan (pc) L. negando ſauer lo”
** page 446: “Noſe) Ayevan (pc) lo que te diçes”
** page 446: “Noſe) Avan (pc) T. eſo que ſea”
** page 507: “Queſe yo) Ayavan (pc) [o no lo ſe]”
