===Etymology 1===
From {{der-lite|tl|poz-pro|sc=Latn|*ba}}, or shortened form of {{m-lite|tl|baga}}. Cognate with {{cog-lite|ceb|ba}} and {{cog-lite|mg|va}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr}}

====Particle====
{{tl-head|particle|b=+}}

# {{n-g|marks a sentence as interrogative}}
#: {{syn|tl|ga|baga|q1=dialectal|q2=dialectal|kaya|q3=obsolete}}
#: {{ux|tl|Mayroon ka '''ba'''ng pera?|Do you have money?}}

=====Usage notes=====
* The particle sometimes disappears in informal contexts and the sentence can be inferred as interrogative depending on the tone of the speaker.
*: {{ux|tl|Mayroon kang pera?|You have money?}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|ano ba}}

===Etymology 2===
Influenced by Baybayin character {{m-lite|tl|ᜊ|sc=Tglg|tr=ba}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# {{tl-letter name|B|b|alph=abak}}
#: {{syn|tl|bi|be|q1=in the Filipino alphabet|q2=in the Abecedario}}

=====See also=====
* {{l|tl|baba}}

===Etymology 3===

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr}}

====Interjection====
{{tl-head|interjection|b=+}}

# {{clipping of|tl|aba}}

===Etymology 4===

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|bâ}}

====Interjection====
{{tl-head|interjection|bâ|b=+}}

# [[boo]] {{qual|used in play-scare with babies}}
#: {{syn|tl|ga|bulaga}}

===Etymology 5===

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|bâ}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|bâ|b=+}}

# {{clipping of|tl|amba}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:map:ACD|ba5}}

