===Etymology===
{{bor+|tl|sa|भार|t=[[burden]]; [[load]]; [[weight]]}}.<ref>{{R:tl:Potet|TBC|page=276}}</ref> Compare {{cog|pam|bala}}, {{cog|ceb|bala|alt=bála / baláha|t=to carry something on the back, not tied}},<ref>{{R:Wolff 1972}}</ref> {{cog|ms|bahara|t=weight}},<ref>{{R:PRPM|bahara}}</ref><ref>{{cite-book|author=Jose G. Kuizon|title=The Sanskrit Loan-Words in the Cebuano-Bisayan Language|url=https://nirc.nanzan-u.ac.jp/nfile/646|publisher=University of San Carlos|location=Cebu City|page=118|year=1964}}</ref> and {{cog|jv|ꦧꦫ||hundred million}}. Otherwise, it may also possibly be from {{m|tl|Bathala}}, which was from {{der|tl|sa|भट्टार|t=[[revered]], [[worshipful]]}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|bahalà}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|bahalà|b=+}}

# [[responsibility]]
# ː {{syn|tl|responsabilidad}}
