Page 1853 bahala ka: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{m|tl|bahala||responsibility}} and {{m|tl|ka||you}}. {{lit|you (are with) [[burden]]}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|bahala7 ka}}

===Interjection===
{{tl-head|interjection|[[bahalà]] [[ka]]|b=+}}

# {{n-g|expresses the desire to not be involved, and to leave the situation to the second person}}: it's up to you; you're on your own; do what you want
#: {{ux|tl|''Tulungan mo naman ako. — '''Bahala ka'''!''|''Help me, please. — '''You're on your own'''!''}}
#: {{ux|tl|''Anong oras ba dapat ako dadating sa party mo? — '''Bahala ka'''.''|''What time do I have to come to your party? — '''It's up to you'''.''}}

====Related terms====
{{rel3|tl|bahala|bahala na}}

====See also====
* {{l|tl|bathala}}
-------- end text --------
Page 1854 bahala na: WARNING: Non-default pronunciation bahala7 na and specified syllabification ba.ha.la.na not equal to respelling/pagetitle auto-syllabification ba.ha.la na, adding explicitly: {{hyph|tl|ba|ha|la|na}}
