===Etymology===
From a {{blend|tl|badya|t1=speak; notify|dila|t2=tongue|nocap=1}} or a {{blend|tl|babala|t1=speak; warn; order|dila|t2=tongue|nocap=1}}, coined by the ''Samahan ng mga Mananagalog'' (Association of Tagalog Writers) around 1905–1906. An alternative etymology posits it to be a {{blend|tl|[[balana]]|[[dila]]||t1=anyone; people|t2=tongue|lit=the people's tongue|nocap=1}} but {{w|Lope K. Santos}} disagrees as {{m|tl|balana}} was also a coinage even later than {{m|tl|balarila}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|balarilà}}

===Noun===
