Page 2028 Balatik: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|Balatic||obsolete|Abecedario}}

===Etymology===
From {{m|tl|balatik||spring-set spear trap}}, due to its resemblance with the constellation [[Orion]], particularly the [[Orion's Belt]] and [[Orion|Orion's]] [[Sword]]. Compare {{cog|bcl|Balatik}}, {{cog|ceb|Balatik}}, {{cog|hil|Balatik}}, {{cog|mry|Bayatik}}, {{cog|mbb|Belatik}}, {{cog|syb|Belatik}}, {{cog|sml|Batik}}, and {{cog|ms|Belantik}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|astronomy}} [[Orion]] {{q|particularly around the region of the [[Orion's Belt]] that looks like a {{m|tl|balatik}}}}
# {{lb|tl|astronomy}} [[Sagittarius]]
#: {{syn|tl|Sahitaryo|Mamamana}}

====See also====
{{col3|tl|Tres Marias|Tatlong Maria|Balais|balyestero}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1860|29|'''BALATIC'''. pp. {{m|es|ballestón}}, las {{m|es|estrella}}s llamadas {{m|es|Tres Marías|tres Marías}}.}}
* {{cite-journal|author=Dante L. Ambrosio|title=BALATIK: Katutubong Bituin ng mga Pilipino|url=https://journals.upd.edu.ph/index.php/pssr/article/view/1287/1833|journal=Philippine Social Sciences Review|location=Quezon City|publisher=University of the Philippines-Diliman College of Social Sciences and Philosophy|year=2005|volume=57|pages=1-27}}

{{C|tl|Constellations}}
