Page 2030 balato: Would save with comment = convert {{tl-IPA}} to {{tl-pr}}; remove {{hyph}} same as respelling auto-syllabification
Page 2030 balato: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Borrowed from Early Modern {{bor|tl|es|barato}}. {{doublet|tl|barat|barato}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|gambling}} [[share]] of [[money]] or [[kind]] given away as [[goodwill]] by the [[winner]] {{q|in gambling, a business deal, etc., especially in a game of {{m|tl|balikutsa}}}}
#: {{syn|tl|salap|tobalats|q2=slang}}
#* {{quote-text|tl|year=2003|author=Ligaya Tiamson-Rubin|title=Angono, Rizal: Bukal ng sining
|passage=Minsan, nilapitan niya ako at binigyan ng '''balato''' na kung ilang libong piso. Masayang masaya ako, hindi ako tumaya pero para akong nanalo, hinalikan ko siya sa batok kasabay ang biro kong, “Ito lang ba?”
|translation=At one time, he approached me and gave me a '''consolation''' of around some thousand pesos. I'm very happy, I didn't made a bet but I felt like I won, that I kissed him on the neck along with a chuckle, "Is this it?"}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|pabalato|balatuhan|balatuhin|bumalato|magbalato|magpabalato|pabalatuhin|tobalats}}

