Page 2373 barok: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
From comic character created by Filipino cartoonist Bert Sarile in 1973, {{w|Barok}}, who was depicted as a “pre-historic caveman”. Possibly influenced by {{der|tl|en|baroque}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|barók}}

====Adjective====
{{tl-adj|barók|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|colloquial|slightly|_|derogatory}}

# [[speak]]ing a [[language]] in a [[broken]] or [[unfluent]] [[manner]] {{q|especially by a non-native speaker or someone with a speech disorder}}
#: {{ux|tl|Ang '''barok''' ng Tagalog mo!|You're speaking '''broken''' Tagalog!}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=1997|author=Virgilio S. Almario|title=Tradisyon at Wikang Filipino|publisher=Sentro Ng Wikang Filipino Sistemang Unibersidad Ng Pilipinas|isbn=9789718781692
|passage=Halatang tinamad sapagkat hindi idinulot ang iba pang makulay na kahulugan  sa Ingles na &quot;joker.&quot; Ang totoo, kung may sobra ... Ngunit ang mas mabigat na  pagkaligta ay ang hindi pagpapasok sa katu- tubong &quot;'''barok'''.&quot; Ni hindi man  lamang&nbsp;...}}
#* {{quote-text|tl|year=1982|author=Reynaldo Arquero Duque|title=Bagani Ubbog
|passage=At inilibing namin ang mga buto ni Apong Ibang sa hukay sa isang sulok ng  bakuran ni Apong Isis na walang tinawag na ... May Tagalog, may Sebuwano,  may Kapampangan, may Iluko, may Ingles, may Espanyol, may Pangasinense.  ... &#39;Yan ang bilin niya, '''barok''', paliwanag ng Amang nang magtanong ako sa  kanya.}}
#* {{quote-text|tl|year=2000|author=Riza Faith C. Ybañez|title=Labor Migration & HIV/AIDS: Vulnerability of Filipino Migrant Workers
|passage=Like Mel, Grace no longer has plans of working abroad since she has vowed to &quot; prioritize my child and my family. ... naging problema ko pa ay yung salita, kasi  bibihira naman ang Hapon na marunong mag-Ingles. So, nag-aral kami ng  konting Niponggo at medyo kahit '''barok''' na '''barok''' kaming magsalita ay nagka- kaintindihan na naman kaming mga Hapon [Perhaps, another problem I faced (at  the start)&nbsp;...}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|barók|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|slang|dated}}

# [[drug addict]]
#: {{syn|tl|adik}}

===Etymology 2===

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# [[small]] [[pillow]]
#: {{syn|tl|almohadilya}}

===Etymology 3===
{{bor+|tl|en|baroque}}, from {{der|tl|fr|baroque}}, from {{der|tl|pt|barroco||irregular pearl}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|barók}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|barók|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|art}}

# [[Baroque]]

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
