Page 2408 basahan: Removing explicit syllabification same as auto-syllabification: {{hyph|tl|ba|sa|han}}
Page 2408 basahan: Replaced {{tl-IPA}} with {{tl-pr}}
Page 2408 basahan: Would save with comment = convert {{tl-IPA}} to {{tl-pr}}; remove {{hyph}} same as respelling auto-syllabification
Page 2408 basahan: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Etymology 1===
Either from the following:
* From {{der|tl|ms|basahan||daily used items or clothes}}, from {{der|tl|poz-pro|*basəq-an||thing that gets wet}}. Can also be analyzed as {{m|ms|basah||wet}} + {{m|ms|-an}}.
* From {{m|tl|basa||wet}} + {{m|tl|-han}}. However, the expected conjugation would be ''*basaan'' since {{m|tl|basa}} ends with a glottal stop, and the root being {{m|tl|basa||reading}} is unlikely. Possibly an irregular conjugation.

Compare {{cog|pam|basan||rag}}, {{cog|mrw|basa'an||bathing suit}}, and {{cog|kaw|basahan||piece of cloth which is not taken off while bathing}}.

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# [[cleaning]] [[rag]]; [[waste]] [[piece]] of [[cloth]] {{q|used for cleaning, dusting, etc.}}
#: {{syn|tl|pamunas|trapo}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|basanhin|basahanin|magbasahan|mamasahan|pagbabasahan|manyikang-basahan}}

=====See also=====
* {{l|tl|gulanit}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{suffix|tl|basa|han|t1=reading}}.

====Verb====
{{tl-verb|+|binasahan|binabasahan|babasahan|b=+}}

# to [[read]] something for [[someone]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{tl-conj|mag|b|a|sa|b|a|sah|o=in|d=an}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|tl|basahan ng sakdal}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1613}}
** page 599: “Veſtido) Baſahan (pp) de cada dia que ſe pone para trabajar con el”
** page 600: “Viejo) Baſahan (pp) vestido”
-------- end text --------
