===Etymology===
{{bor+|tl|pam|bayani}}, from {{der|tl|phi-pro|*baʀani}}, from {{der|tl|poz-pro|*baʀani||brave, bold; dare to do}}. Cognate with {{cog|ceb|bagani}}, {{cog|mrw|bagani}}, {{cog|ms|berani}}, and {{cog|mh|peran}}. {{doublet|tl|balani}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# [[hero]]
# [[mutual]] [[aid]]; [[cooperative]] [[endeavor]]
#: {{syn|tl|tulungan|usungan|damayan}}
# [[person]] who [[offer]]s [[free]] [[service]] in a [[cooperative]] [[endeavor]]
#: {{syn|tl|kasaknong|kausong|katulong}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|kabayanihan|Araw ng mga Bayani|bayanihan|bayanihin|pagkabayani|magpakabayani|mamayani|mambayani|nakapamamayani|pabayani|pamamayani|matang-bayani|magbayani|pagbayanihan}}

====See also====
{{col3|tl|kisig|tapang|balyente}}

