Page 2885 binyag: Already saw {{tl-pr}}, skipping: {{tl-pr|binyág}}
Page 2885 binyag: Skipped, no changes
Page 2885 binyag: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|biniyag||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
According to the ''Vocabulario de la lengua tagala'' (1860), this word is from Brunei, perhaps {{bor|tl|kxd|-}}, which originally meant {{m-g|to pour water from above}}, which was an ablution ceremony (c.f. {{m|en|wudu}}) done by an imam  while teaching Islam, and was possibly later applied to Christian baptism. Blust & Trussel also posit {{inh|tl|phi-pro|*buniag}}. Compare {{cog|ilo|buniag}}, {{cog|pam|biniag}}, {{cog|bcl|bunyag}}, {{cog|ceb|bunyag}}, {{cog|hil|bunyag}}, and {{cog|mrw|boniyag}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|binyág}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|binyág|b=+}} 

# {{lb|tl|Christianity}} [[baptism]]
#: {{syn|tl|bawtismo|pagbibinyag}}
# {{lb|tl|Islam|obsolete}} [[wetting]] with a [[specific]] [[wash]] {{defdate|16th|17th c.}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|binyagan|magbinyag|Binyagan|mabinyagan|magpabinyag|pabinyagan|maminyagan|ninang sa binyag|ninong sa binyag|pagbibinyag|buminyag}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|bor=1|tsg|binyag}}

====See also====
{{col3|tl|sawan|sutmondilaw|wudu}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:KWF Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1860}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1613}}
** page 102: {{m-g|Baptiſmo) Binyag (pc) rejeneraçion eſpiritual}}
** page 106: {{m-g|Bautiſmo) Binyag (pc) rrejeneraçion eſpiritual}}
** page 427: {{m-g|Mojar) Binyag (pc) con cierto lauatorio. Eſte bocablo no es Tagalo ſino Burney, q̃ venia vn Miniſtro de aquella tierra a eſta a enſeñar la ley de Mahoma, y enſabiẽdola les hacia çierto lauatorio y llamauan le binyag, y alos tales mang̃a binyagan .{{!}}. los purificados [y renouados] en ley}}
* {{R:map:ACD|buniag}}
-------- end text --------
