===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|boliyos||obsolete|Abecedario}}
* {{alt|tl|buliyos||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From earlier variant {{m|tl|buliyos}}, possibly from an early borrowing of {{bor|tl|es|buríos}} / {{m|es|burillos}}, plural of {{m|es|burío}} / {{m|es|burillo}}, a generic name for various species of trees whose bark material is obtained to make cords. Compare {{cog|pam|burilius}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|bulyós}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|bulyós|b=+}}

# [[whip]] consisting of [[cylindrical]] [[bamboo]] [[stick]]s bundled and tied into a [[sturdy]] [[cord]] commonly used by [[flagellant]]s during [[Holy Week]]

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|pagbubulyos|magbulyos|bulyusin|bulyusan}}

====See also====
{{col3|tl|pagtatatak|penitensiya|panata|pasang-krus}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1613|511|Randas) Boliyos (pp) C. que haçen [con palillos]}}

