Page 3429 bunot: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|tl|phi-pro|*bunút}}, from {{inh|tl|poz-pro|*bunut}}. Compare {{cog|bcl|bunot}}, {{cog|ceb|bunot}}, {{cog|hil|bunot}}, and {{cog|tsg|bunut}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|bunót}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|bunót|b=+}}

# [[coconut]] [[husk]]
# [[act]] of [[polish]]ing the [[floor]] using a [[coconut]] [[husk]]
#: {{syn|tl|pagbubunot}}
# [[coir]] {{gl|coconut husk fibers}}
# [[fibrous]] [[portion]] of [[nut]]s or [[seed]]s

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|bunutin|magbunot|pagbubunot|makasipol-bunot|himunot|manghimunot|himunutan|himunutin}}

===Etymology 2===
From Proto-Central Philippine ''*bugnut''  (“pull out”) or {{inh|tl|phi-pro|*búnut||pulling out, uprooting}}. Compare {{cog|ilo|bunot}}, {{cog|bcl|bugnot}}, {{cog|ceb|bunot}}, and {{cog|hil|bugnot}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|+<n^>|bunót<a^>}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# [[act]] of [[pull]]ing out something [[elongated]]
# [[tooth]] [[extraction]]; [[removal]] of [[teeth]]
# [[uprooting]] {{q|of a plant}}
# [[drawing]] {{q|in a lottery}}
# [[unsheathing]]; [[drawing]] {{q|of a weapon from its sheath or holster}}
# [[unplugging]] {{q|of an electronic device}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|bumunot|mamunot|bunutan|bunutin|mabunot|makabunot|magbunot|magpabunot|mabunutan|mabunutan ng tinik|sabunot|pagsabunot|magsabunutan|sabunutan|pagsasabunutan|sabunutin|manabunot|sumabunot}}

====Adjective====
{{tl-adj|bunót|b=+}}

# [[pulled]] [[out]] {{q|of something elongated}}
# [[extracted]]; [[removed]] {{q|of teeth}}
# [[uprooted]] {{q|of plants}}
# [[drawn]] {{q|of a number in a lottery}}
# [[unsheathed]]; [[drawn]] {{q|of a weapon from its sheath or holster}}
# [[unplugged]] {{q|of an electronic device}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
