Page 3586 buwena mano: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|buena mano}}
* {{alt|tl|buwenamano}}
* {{alt|tl|bwenamano}}

===Etymology===
{{bor+|tl|es|[[buena]] [[mano]]||good hand}}, due to the supposed [[good]] [[pick]] or [[fine]] [[hand]] of the [[first]] [[customer]] of the [[day]]. It is said that the concept originally came from the {{w|Sangley|Sangley Chinese}} who are believed to be good at running a [[business]].

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|{{l|es|buena|buwena}} [[mano]]|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|business}}

# [[first]] [[customer]] of the [[day]]
# [[first]] [[sale]] of the [[day]]

====Usage notes====
* In the [[Philippines]], it is believed that usage of this term invites [[luck]] into the [[business]] throughout the [[day]], so [[business owner]]s tend to [[welcome]] the first customer with a [[bigger]] [[smile]].

====Related terms====
{{rel3|tl|buweno|mano}}

====See also====
{{col3|tl|manigo|pasinaya}}

