===Etymology 1===
{{bor+|tl|sa|धरति||to hold}}<ref>{{R:tl:Potet|TBC|page=278}}</ref> with the root {{m|sa|धृ}} but without the {{m|sa|-ति}} suffix, from {{der|tl|inc-pro|*dʰárati}}, from {{der|tl|iir-pro|*dʰárati}} with the root {{m|iir-pro|*dʰar-}}, from {{der|tl|ine-pro||*dʰér-e-ti}}, thematic present of {{m|ine-pro|*dʰer-||to hold}}. Compare {{cog|pam|dala}}, {{cog|bcl|dara}}, {{cog|ceb|dala}},<ref>{{cite-book|author=Jose G. Kuizon|title=The Sanskrit Loan-Words in the Cebuano-Bisayan Language|url=https://nirc.nanzan-u.ac.jp/nfile/646|publisher=University of San Carlos|location=Cebu City|page=120|year=1964}}</ref> {{cog|tsg|dā}}, {{cog|as|ধৰা}}, {{cog|bn|ধরা}}, {{cog|or|ଧରିବା}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|dalá}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|dalá|b=+}}

# [[load]]; something [[carried]]; something [[brought]]
#: {{syn|tl|karga|lulan|kargada}}
# [[carrying]]; [[bringing]] {{q|of something}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|dala-dala|dala-dalahan|dala-dalahin|dalang-galit|dalang-hiya|dalhan|dalhin|ipadala|ipagdala|madala|magdala|magpadala|nagdadalang-tao|padala|padalahang-liham|padalhan|pagdadala|pagdadalang-tao|pagdadalhan|pagpapadala|tagadala|tagapagdala|dalang-sabi|dalang-tao|magdalang-tao}}

====Adjective====
{{tl-adj|dalá|b=+}}

# [[carried]] along; [[brought]]; [[take away|taken away]]
#: {{syn|tl|dinala|inilulan|kinarga|taglay}}
# {{lb|tl|figurative}} [[brought about]]; [[caused]] {{q|by something aforementioned}}

