{{bor+|tl|es|dela}}, from {{m|es|[[de]] [[la]]}}. Its use as a contraction of ''de los'' in Spanish-origin surnames is from the American colonial era, possibly by influence of Italian {{m|it|della}}, {{m|it|delle}} and {{m|it|degli}}.

