Page 4606 dilawan: Already saw {{tl-pr}}, skipping: {{tl-pr|dilawán<v^>|+,dilawán<n,a^>}}
Page 4606 dilawan: Skipped, no changes
Page 4606 dilawan: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|tl|dilaw|an|t1=yellow}}. The political senses are from the yellow color associated with the {{w|Liberal Party (Philippines)|Liberal Party of the Philippines}} and [[liberalism]] itself locally. Originally used by both left-wing and right-wing politicians to attack members of the Liberal Party back in the 1980s, but its usage has been revived under the Aquino III and Duterte administrations.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|dilawán<v^>|+,dilawán<n,a^>}}

===Verb===
{{tl-verb|dilawán|dinilawan|dinidilawan|didilawan|b=+}}

# to be [[made]] [[yellow]]
# to be [[add]]ed some [[turmeric]] {{q|in food}}

====Conjugation====
{{tl-infl-in-an|d|i|law|law|object}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|dilawán|head2=+|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|Philippine politics|slang|sometimes|derogatory}} {{w|Liberal Party (Philippines)|Liberal Party}} [[supporter]] {{q|especially the Aquino administrations}}

====Derived terms====
{{col3|tl|pinklawan}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|dilawán|head2=+|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|Philippine politics|slang|sometimes|derogatory}} [[liberal]]; of the {{w|:Liberal Party (Philippines)|Liberal Party}}
-------- end text --------
