===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|rin}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|tl|phi-pro|*dən|pos=completive particle}}. Compare {{cog|akl|eon}}, {{cog|ceb|ron}}, and {{cog|mrw|den}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|+,den<q:colloquial>}}

===Adverb===
{{tl-adv|b=+}}

# [[too]]; [[also]]
#: {{syn|tl|saka|man}}

====Usage notes====
* When the preceding word ends with a vowel, {{angbr|w}}, or {{angbr|y}}, {{m|tl|rin}} is used instead, but the distinction isn't always made. Other words with this phenomenon include {{m|tl|dito}}, {{m|tl|diyan}}, {{m|tl|doon}}, and {{m|tl|daw}}.

