Page 4654 dini: Would save with comment = convert {{tl-IPA}} to {{tl-pr}}; remove {{rhymes}} same as auto-generated rhyme and syllable count; remove {{hyph}} same as respelling auto-syllabification
Page 4654 dini: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|dine}}
* {{alt|tl|rini|rine}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|tl|map-pro|*di-ni||here}}. The latter half of the word is possibly related to {{m|tl|iri}}/{{m|tl|ire}}/{{m|tl|idi}}. See also {{m|tl|ganiri}} and other Tagalog demonstrative pronouns. Meanwhile, the former half is possibly related to {{cog|ms|di}} and {{cog|id|di}} as a likely cognate. Compare {{cog|ceb|ini}}, {{cog|tsg|dī}}, and {{cog|ms|ini}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|+|dine<qq:colloquial>}}

===Adverb===
{{tl-adv|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|dialectal}}

# [[here]] {{gl|near the speaker}}
#: {{syn|tl|dito}}

====Usage notes====
* Used in most dialects except standard or Manila Tagalog.
* When the preceding word ends with a vowel, {{angbr|w}}, or {{angbr|y}}, {{l|tl|rini}} is used instead.

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|parini|narini|naririni|pumarini|pagparini|nandini|dumini|garini|parika}}

====See also====
{{tl-dem pronouns}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:map:ACD|-ni|di-ni}}

