From Proto-Central-Philippine ''*dúlaʔ'' (“to play; amuse oneself”). Compare {{cog|ceb|dula}}, {{cog|kyk|duwa}}, and {{cog|mg|dola|alt=dôla}}. The sense “drama” was introduced in the early 20th century.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|dulâ,dulà}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|dulâ|head2=dulà|b=+}}

# [[drama]]; [[stage]] [[play]]
#: {{syn|tl|drama}}
# {{lb|tl|obsolete}} [[joy]]
#: {{syn|tl|galak|tuwa}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|dulaan|dulain|isadula|magsadula|madula|madulain|mandudula|pagsasadula|pandudula|pandula|dulambuhay|dula-dulaan|lakandula}}

====See also====
{{col3|tl|sarsuwela|parsa}}

===Further reading===
