Page 5129 eme: Removing explicit syllabification same as auto-syllabification: {{hyph|tl|e|me}}
Page 5129 eme: Replaced {{tl-IPA}} with {{tl-pr}}
Page 5129 eme: Would save with comment = convert {{tl-IPA}} to {{tl-pr}}; remove {{hyph}} same as respelling auto-syllabification
Page 5129 eme: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Etymology 1===
{{bor+|tl|es|eme}}, the Spanish name of the letter {{m|es|M}}/{{m|es|m}}.

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|historical}} {{tl-letter name|M|m|alph=abec}}
#: {{syn-lite|tl|em|q1=in the Filipino alphabet|ma|q2=in the Abakada alphabet}}

===Etymology 2===
Possibly from {{cog|es|eme||M}}, euphemism of {{m|es|mierda||shit; crap}} by taking its first letter. Compare {{m|tl|kiyeme}}. See also {{m|tl|lamyerda}}, {{m|tl|lakwatsa}}.

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|women's speech|gay slang}}

# [[nonsense]]
#: {{syn|tl|kiyeme|kemerut|echos|kalokohan|sagimuymoy}}
# {{n-g|term used for any object whose actual name the speaker does not know or cannot remember}}: [[thingamajig]]; [[whatchamacallit]]; [[thingy]]; [[dingus]]
#: {{syn|tl|ano|kuwan}}
# [[excuses]]; [[pretenses]]

=====Usage notes=====
* The word is typically used by [[women]], and may sound [[effeminate]] when used by [[men]].

=====Alternative forms=====
* {{alt|tl|ems}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|eme-eme|umeme-eme}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* [https://www.tagaloglang.com/eme/ “EME” in ''Tagalog-English Dictionary'', TAGALOG LANG, 2007.]
* {{R:es:DRAE}}

