Page 5723 gayuma: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|gayoma||obsolete|Abecedario}}

===Etymology===
From Southern Luzon axis ''*gayúma'' ({{m-g|love-charm}}). Compare {{cog|pam|gayuma}}. See also {{ncog|ceb|gugma||love}}. The sense of {{m-g|magnet}} is coined in the 1960s as an allusion to the effect of the magical potion.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# [[charming]] [[quality]]
#: {{syn|tl|panghalina|pang-akit|lumay|q3=dialectal}}
# {{lb|tl|folklore|magic}} [[love]] [[charm]]; [[philter]] {{gl|charm or potion to cause a person to fall in love}}
# {{lb|tl|obsolete}} [[magnet]]
