===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|G.I.}}

===Etymology===
Initialism originally from {{bor|tl|en|GI|t=nickname for [[USA|U.S.]] military personnel}}. The words to the {{initialism|tl||nocap=1}} was later jokingly perceived as {{m|en|"[[genuine#English|'''G'''enuine]] [[Intsik#Tagalog|'''I'''ntsik]]"}}, from {{compound|en|genuine|lang1=en|Intsik|t2=[[Chinese]]|lang2=tl|nocat=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|dyí7ay}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=dyi ay}} {{tlb|tl|Chinese Filipino|humorous|slang}}

# {{initialism of|tl|[[genuine|Genuine]] {{l|tl|Intsik}}|nodot=1}} ([[Chinese]]) {{gl|any [[ethnic]] [[Chinese]] person in the [[Philippines]] described to be profoundly [[Chinese]] in [[behavior]], [[speech]], [[demeanor]], or [[likeness]], especially those [[born]] and [[raise]]d in [[China]] or [[Taiwan]].}}
#: {{ux|tl|Ang lalim ng Chinese (vocabulary) ng '''GI''' na nakilala ko, at di kami nagkaintindihan kahit sabay kaming gumagamit ng Mandarin.|The Chinese (vocabulary), used by the '''GI''' I met, was quite deep, and we couldn't understand each other even though we were both using Mandarin.}}

