Page 5801 ginoo: Already saw {{tl-pr}}, skipping: {{tl-pr|gino7ó|gino7o<qq:archaic, now dialectal>}}
Page 5801 ginoo: Skipped, no changes
Page 5801 ginoo: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|guinoo||obsolete|Abecedario}}
* {{alt|tl|Ginoo||capitalized}}
* {{alt|tl|G.||abbreviation}}

===Etymology===
Possibly from Proto-Bisayan ''*gin-'' (c.f. {{cog|ceb|gi-}} and {{cog|hil|gin-}} prefixes) + Greater Central Philippine ''*túʔuh'' ({{m-g|believe; give credence to}}) (c.f. {{cog|tl|totoo}}, {{cog|ceb|tuo}}), from {{der|tl|poz-pro|*tuqu||true}}. Compare {{cog|pam|ginu}}, {{cog|bcl|ginoo}}, {{cog|ceb|ginoo}}. Also possibly related to {{noncog|sa|नु||praise}}, or {{m|tl|noo|t=forehead}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|gino7ó|gino7o<qq:archaic, now dialectal>}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|ginoó|b=+}}

# [[gentleman]]; [[well-bred]] [[man]]
#: {{syn|tl|maginoo|kabalyero}}
#: {{ux|tl|Bigay ng isang '''ginoo'''.|Given by a '''mister'''.}}
# {{lb|tl|archaic}} [[lady]] of [[rank]]
# {{lb|tl|historical}} [[lord]]; [[noble]] from the [[ruling]] [[class]]

====Usage notes====
* According to Fr. Juan de Noceda and Fr. Pedro del San Lucar who compiled the ''Vocabulario de la lengua tagala'' in 1754, '''''ginoo''''' referred to a lady of rank while '''''maginoo''''' referred to a gentleman of rank, whereas today, both refer to men, while '''{{m|tl|ginang}}''', '''{{m|tl|gining}}''', or '''{{m|tl|binibini}}''' are used for women today.

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|kaginoohan|maginoo|maginoohin|pagkamaginoo|Aba Ginoong Maria|lawing-ginoo}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|tl|Ginoo}}
* {{l|tl|Guino-o}} {{q|surname}}

====See also====
{{col3|tl|ginang|gining|dayang|don|donya|senyor|senyorita|lakan|lakambini}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1860}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1613}}
** page 444: “Noble) Ginoo (pp) por linaje y parentela”
** page 497: “Prinçipala) Ginoo (pp) o ſeñora”
** page 552: “Señora) Ginoo (pp) para con mugeres”
-------- end text --------
