From {{w|Philippine Spanish|Philippine}} {{bor|tl|es|guerra|guierra}}, variant of {{der|tl|es|guerra}}, from {{der|tl|la-eme|werra}}, from {{der|tl|frk|*werru|t=confusion; quarrel}}. The insertion of {{angbr|-i-}} / {{angbr|-iy-}} ({{IPAchar|/{{w|{{IPAsym|j}}|j}}/}}) after {{IPAchar|/ɡ/}}, in {{w|Philippine Spanish}} is possibly due to {{glossary|palatalization}} of {{IPAchar|/ɡ/}} before [[front vowel]] {{IPAchar|/e/}} in some Spanish dialects. Compare {{w|Chilean Spanish|Chilean}} {{cog|es|guierra}}, {{cog|an|guierra}}, and {{cog|ist|guiera}}.

