===Etymology===
{{bor+|tl|es|grave}}, from {{der|tl|la|gravis}}. See also {{m|tl|bruto}}, {{m|tl|gulo}}, and {{m|tl|guro}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|informal}} [[outrageous]]; [[intense]]
#: {{syn|tl|matindi|yano|q2=Quezon}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''Grabe''' 'yong nangyaring lindol sa Hapon!|The earthquake that happened in Japan was '''outrageous'''!}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''Grabe''' na talaga ang krimen dito sa Maynila!|The crimes here in Manila are really '''getting out of control'''!}}
# [[grave]]; [[serious]]
#: {{syn|tl|matindi|malubha}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''Grabe''' ang kanyang kondisyon, at kailangan niyang magpahinga.|His condition is '''grave''', and he needs to rest.}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|tl|grumabe}}

===Interjection===
{{tl-head|interjection|b=+}}

# {{n-g|expression of [[astonishment]] at the [[gravity]] or [[outrageousness]] of the situation}}: [[whoa]]! [[wow]]!
#: {{ux|tl|'''Grabe'''! Nanalo ka ulit sa lotto?|'''Wow'''! You won again in the lottery?}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''Grabe'''! Wala ka talagang kuwenta!|'''Wow'''! You're definitely worthless!}}

