===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|hao siao}}
* {{alt|tl|hao-siao}}
* {{alt|tl|hao-shiao}}
* {{alt|tl|hawshaw}}
* {{alt|tl|hawsiyaw}}

===Etymology===
{{bor+|tl|nan-hbl|嘐潲|tr=hau-siâu|t=fake}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|derogatory|slang}}

# [[bogus]]; [[phony]]; [[fake]]

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|napakahawsyaw|hawsyawin}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}} {{lb|tl|derogatory|slang}}

# [[something]] or [[someone]] [[bogus]]
#* {{quote-web|tl|url=https://pcoo.gov.ph/april-12-2017-speech-of-president-rodrigo-roa-duterte-during-his-meeting-with-the-filipino-community-in-riyadh-saudi-arabia/|date=April 12, 2017|work=Speech of President Rodrigo Roa Duterte during his meeting with the Filipino community in Riyadh, Saudi Arabia|author=Rodrigo Roa Duterte|publisher=Presidential Communications Operations Office
|passage=''Sa harap naman, ako pati si Yasay. So Yasay studied UP sa padre Faura, sila sa Ateneo, ako San Beda. But we mixed each other very well. Hanggang lumaki na kami, kilala ko na ‘yung characters nila. Kaya ‘yung pinili ko talaga, garantisado ako. Ngayon, walang '''hao-siao''' ‘yang mga tao. Kasi puro na mayayaman. Totoo. Si Bebot islanded estate ito o. Ako lang ang mahirap diyan sa — kaya I never signed anything. Andyan man in front of the public eh. Hindi ako nakapirma na mangolekta ako ng allowance extra except my salary, 130,000. Tapos dalawa ang pamilya ko. Eh papano ko...''}}
#* {{quote-web|tl|url=http://www.pcaf.da.gov.ph/index.php/2019/05/14/2019-farmers-and-fisherfolks-month-fetes-the-filipino-agri-fishery-worker/|date=May 14, 2019|work=2019 Farmers’ and Fisherfolk’s Month fetes the Filipino Agri-Fishery Worker|publisher=The Philippine Council for Agriculture and Fisheries (PCAF)
|passage=''Ito ay para nakikita nila na walang hocus-pocus, walang '''hao-siao''' ‘yung ating Procurement process. Kasi dito nagsisimula ‘yung pagkawala ng tiwala ng ating mga magsasaka at mangingisda sa ating Procurement process kapag ang natatanggap nila ay service commodity or equipment ay hindi nila gusto.''}}
#* {{quote-web|tl|url=https://www.abante.com.ph/hao-siao-bidder-yari-kay-digong/|date=Oct 20, 2020|work='''Hao siao''' bidder yari kay Digong|author=Aileen Taliping|publisher=Abante News
|passage=''Sa ganitong paraan aniya ay makikita kung sino ang mga tunay na bidder at kung sino ang mga '''hao-shiao''' na nagbababa ng husto ng sa presyo ng isang proyekto para manalo.''}}
# [[pseudojournalist]] {{q|especially those who cash in on payoffs and bribes made by news sources, particularly during elections}}<ref>{{cite-book|title=A Values Approach to News Media Ethics: The CMFR Ethics Manual|url=https://books.google.com.ph/books?id=UhBlAAAAMAAJ&q=hao+siao&dq=hao+siao&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwjvp-qvo9n0AhXlyIsBHY-GAzkQ6AF6BAgIEAI|year=2007|publisher=Center for Media Freedom and Responsibility|pages=48}}</ref><ref>{{cite-web|work=A glossary of media corruption|url=http://www.hotmanila.ph/content/media/glossary-media-corruption|date=October 12, 2004|publisher=HotManila.ph}}</ref>
#* {{quote-web|tl|url=https://wwwmortzcortigoza.blogspot.com/2011/09/|date=September 26, 2011|work=Ibalik ang integridad ng BOC|author=Mortz Ortigoza|publisher=P'Nan News
|passage=''Tama si Customs Commissioner Rozzano Rufino Biazon na palayasin mula sa kanilang tanggapan ang mga “'''hao siao'''” o fake na mediamen.''}}

===References===
<references />

===Further reading===
* {{R:Tagalog Slang Dictionary|57}}
-------- end text --------
