===Etymology===
Said to be {{bor+|tl|nan-hbl|-|nocap=1}}, either:
* {{m|nan-hbl|[[欣]][[眠]]|tr=him bîn / herm bîn|lit=happy sleep|pos={{IPAchar|/him³³ bin²⁴/}} or {{IPAchar|/həm³³ bin²⁴/}}}}, according to Manuel (1948).
* {{m|nan-hbl|[[陷眠]] / [[含眠]]|tr=hâm-bîn / hām-bîn|t=to talk in one's sleep; to [[sleeptalk]]}} or "sound sleep" according to Manuel (1948).
See also {{ncog|nan-hbl|[[噤]] / [[含]]|tr=hīm / hām|t=to keep mouth shut; to be silent}} & {{m|nan-hbl|含|tr=hâm / hām|t=to keep mouth shut}} as per Douglas (1873/1899). Furthermore, see also {{ncog|tl|him-|pos=[[historical]] [[stative]] [[prefix]], now [[unproductive]]}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|himbíng}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|himbíng|b=+}}

# [[deep]] [[sleep]]; [[profound]] [[sleep]]
# [[proper]] and [[comfortable]] [[temperature]] of [[water]] or [[weather]]

