Page 6552 -hin: Replaced {{tl-IPA}} with {{tl-pr}}
Page 6552 -hin: Would save with comment = convert {{tl-IPA}} to {{tl-pr}}
Page 6552 -hin: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Suffix===
{{tl-verb|b=+|addlpos=adjective,noun}}

# {{alt form|tl|-in|nodot=1}}
#: {{suffixusex|tl|intindi|t1=to understand|intindihin|t2={{lb|tl|transitive}} understand}}
#: {{suffixusex|tl|basa|t1=to read|babasahin|t2=reading material}}
#: {{suffixusex|tl|pang-una|t1=the first|pangunahin|t2=primary}}
# {{lb|tl|Tayabas}} {{ngd|nature and origin suffix}}
#: {{suffixusex|tl|Lucena|t1=city|Lucenahin|t2=a native of Lucena, Quezon}}
#: {{suffixusex|tl|Infanta|t1=municipality|Infantahin|t2=a native of Infanta, Quezon}}
#: {{suffixusex|tl|Aurora|t1=municipality of San Francisco|Aurorahin|t2=a native of San Francisco (Aurora), Quezon}}
#: {{suffixusex|tl|ilaya|t1=upper part|ilayahin|t2=a native or local from [[northern]] or [[upper]] [[part]] of a [[town]] or [[community]]}}

====Usage notes====
* Normally, {{IPAchar|/h/}} is inserted before -in when the root word ends with a vowel that is not followed by a glottal stop. In some cases, phoneme change can occur and {{IPAchar|/h/}} becomes {{IPAchar|/n/}} or {{IPAchar|/r/}}.
*: {{suffixusex|tl|sabi|altsuf=-'''h'''in|sabihin}}
*: {{suffixusex|tl|talo|altsuf=-'''n'''in|talunin}}
*: {{suffixusex|tl|sala|altsuf=-'''r'''in|salarin}}

* Sometimes, the final vowel of the root word disappears when the suffix is added.
*: {{suffixusex|tl|bili|bilhin}}
*: {{suffixusex|tl|dala|dalhin}}

====Derived terms====
{{suffixsee|tl}}
-------- end text --------
