===Etymology===
From {{inh|tl|poz-pro|*ibəʀ||saliva in the mouth; drool; desire; crave; lust for}}. Cognates with {{cog|pag|ibeg||covet, desire, fall in love with}}, {{cog|pam|ibug||corporal desires; appetite}}, {{cog|ceb|ibog||attracted, craving for}}, {{cog|tbl|iwol||saliva, drool over, desire}}, {{cog|tsg|ibug||envy}}, {{cog|mg|ivy||saliva}}, and {{cog|to|ifo||saliva, tasty}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# [[want]]; [[desire]]; [[like]]; [[wish]]
#: {{syn|tl|gusto|nais|nasa|hangad|mithi}}
# [[choice]]; [[preference]]
#: {{syn|tl|kagustuhan}}
# [[purpose]]; [[objective]]
#: {{syn|tl|layon|layunin|mithi|mithiin|adhika|adhikain}}
#: {{ux|tl|Ang '''ibig''' ko lang sa pagparito ay magdala ng pagkain.|My only '''purpose''' of coming here is to bring food.}}
# [[love]]d one; [[beloved]]; [[darling]]; [[sweetheart]]
#: {{syn|tl|sinta|mahal|irog|giliw}}
# [[love]]; [[attraction]]; [[fondness]] {{q|especially in {{m|tl|pag-ibig}}}}
#: {{syn|tl|pag-ibig|mahal|pagmamahal|sinta|pagsinta|irog|pag-irog|giliw|paggiliw|pagkasi|pagsuyo|pagliyag}}

===Verb===
{{tl-verb|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|pseudoverb}} to [[want]]; to [[like]]
#: {{syn|tl|gusto|nais}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''Ibig''' kong malaman kung saan nakatira si G. Dela Cruz.|I '''want''' to know where Mr. Dela Cruz lives.}}
#: {{ux|tl|Ano ang '''ibig''' mong sabihin?|What do you mean?|lit=What do you '''want''' to say?}}

====Derived terms====
