Page 6950 ika-: Skipped, no changes
Page 6950 ika-: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|tl|map-pro|*Sika-}}.

====Prefix====
{{tl-head|prefix|iká-|b=+}}

# {{ngd|used to form ordinal numbers}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|dalawa|t1=two|ikalawa|t2=second}}
# {{ngd|used to express {{m|en|o'clock}}}}
#: {{syn|tl|alas}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|lima|t1=five|ikalima|t2=five o'clock}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Tagalog ordinal numbers prefixed with '''''ika-''''' are usually more formal compared to those prefixed with {{m|tl|pang-}}, but '''''ika-''''' is also preferred in temporal rankings.

===Etymology 2===

====Prefix====
{{tl-head|prefix|iká-|b=+}}

# {{ngd|used to form verbs with causative focus}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|galit|t1=anger|ikagalit|t2=to cause one's anger}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{prefixsee|tl}}
