Page 7118 Imus: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Ph locator cavite imus.png|thumb|Location of Imus]]

===Etymology===
From {{m|tl|imos|imus, imos|land between the tributary of two rivers}}, a reference to the original townsite at Toclong, around the confluence of Imus and Julian rivers. Alternative origins and {{glossary|folk etymologies}} include derivation from {{der|tl|la|infimus}} and {{der|tl|es|céntimo|céntimos}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Proper noun===
{{tl-proper noun|b=+}}

# {{place|tl|<<city>> and {{m|en|de jure}} <<provincial capital>> in <<p/Cavite>>, <<c/Philippines>>|t=Imus}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=1992|author=Santiago V. Alvarez|title=The Katipunan and the Revolution: Memoirs of a General : with the Original Tagalog Text|publisher=Ateneo University Press|isbn=9789715500777
|passage=Nang makuha na ng mga kastila ang Perez Dasmarinas, ay hindi naluwatan sa kanilang pamamalagi at pag-aayos doon, at muling gumayak ng paglusob sa '''Imus'''.}}
