Page 7119 -in: Already saw {{tl-pr}}, skipping: {{tl-pr|+<a:Standard Tagalog>|-en<a:colloquial>}}
Page 7119 -in: Skipped, no changes
Page 7119 -in: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|-hin}}
* {{alt|tl|-nin}}
* {{alt|tl|-rin}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|tl|phi-pro|*-ən}}, from {{inh|tl|poz-pro|*-ən}}, from {{inh|tl|map-pro|*-ən}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|+<a:Standard Tagalog>|-en<a:colloquial>}}

===Suffix===
{{tl-verb|b=+|b2=in}}

# {{non-gloss definition|object trigger}}: to perform the action of the verb to someone or something
#: {{ux|tl|Lulutu'''in''' ko ang isda.|inline=1|I will cook the fish|lit=The fish will be cooked by me.}} {{q|'''The fish''' is focused.}}
# {{non-gloss definition|directional trigger}}: to do something in the (physical or psychological) direction of
#: {{ux|tl|D'''in'''alaw namin ang lola ni Olivia.|inline=1|We visited the grandmother of Olivia.|lit=Olivia's grandmother was visited by us.}} {{q|'''The grandmother''' is focused.}}
# {{non-gloss definition|actor trigger}}: to be affected or overtaken by a condition, feeling or phenomenon
#: {{ux|tl|B'''in'''abaha ang bahay niya.|inline=1|His house gets flooded.}} {{q|'''His house''' is focused.}}
# {{non-gloss definition|object trigger}}: {{q|with root word reduplication}} to do something occasionally, at random, a little, a bit, now and then or here and there
#: {{ux|tl|'''Iniisip''' ko minsan ang nakaraan ko.|inline=1|I sometimes think about my past.|lit=My past is sometimes thought about by me.}} {{q|'''My past''' is focused.}}

===Suffix===
{{tl-adj|b=+|b2=in}}

# [[prone]] to, [[susceptible]] to
#: {{suffixusex|tl|lagnat|t1=fever|lagnatin|t2=prone to fever}}
#: {{suffixusex|tl|sakit|t1=illness|sakitin|t2=prone to illness}}

===Suffix===
{{tl-noun|b=+|b2=in}}

# {{non-gloss definition|an object of the action expressed by the root}}
#: {{suffixusex|tl|awit|t1=singing, song|awitin|t2=song}}
#: {{suffixusex|tl|aral|t1=lesson, studying|aralin|t2=studies}}
# {{lb|tl|Tayabas}} {{ngd|nature and origin suffix}}
#: {{suffixusex|tl|Quezon|t1=province|Quezonin|t2=a native of Quezon}}
#: {{suffixusex|tl|Sampaloc|t1=municipality|Sampalukin|t2=a native of Sampaloc, Quezon}}
#: {{suffixusex|tl|bayan|t1=town center or poblacion|bayanin|t2=a local from the town center}}
#: {{suffixusex|tl|linang|t1=farm or remote area|linangin|t2=a local from the farm}}

====Usage notes====
* Normally, {{IPAchar|/h/}} is inserted before -in when the root word ends with a vowel that is not followed by a glottal stop. In some cases, phoneme change can occur and {{IPAchar|/h/}} becomes {{IPAchar|/n/}} or {{IPAchar|/r/}}.
*: {{suffixusex|tl|sabi|altsuf=-'''h'''in|sabihin}}
*: {{suffixusex|tl|talo|altsuf=-'''n'''in|talunin}}
*: {{suffixusex|tl|sala|altsuf=-'''r'''in|salarin}}

* Sometimes, the final vowel of the root word disappears when the suffix is added.
*: {{suffixusex|tl|sunod|sundin}}
*: {{suffixusex|tl|kamit|kamtin}}

* Due to [[allophony]], {{IPAchar|/d/}} turns into {{IPAchar|/r/}} when inserted before ''-in''.
*: {{suffixusex|tl|hangad|[[hangarin|hanga'''r'''in]]}}
*: {{suffixusex|tl|baligtad|[[baligtarin|baligta'''r'''in]]}}
*: {{suffixusex|tl|bayad|[[bayarin|baya'''r'''in]]}}

====Derived terms====
{{suffixsee|tl}}

-------- end text --------
