Page 7500 isko: Already saw {{tl-pr}}, skipping: {{tl-pr|iskó}}
Page 7500 isko: Skipped, no changes
Page 7500 isko: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{clipping|tl|iskolar||scholar}}, from the phrase {{m-g|''iskolar ng bayan''}}, {{lit|scholar of the people|nocap=1}}. The scholarship of the students given the label is subsidized by the government, which is in turn funded by the citizens' taxes. Thus, in effect, the people pays for the students' education.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|iskó}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|iskó|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|education|university slang}}

# [[student]] with [[education]] [[subsidize]]d by the [[government]] {{q|especially from [[state]] [[universities]] such as the {{w|University of the Philippines}}}}

====Usage notes====
* The term is not gender-specific. However, since the word ends with ''-o'' (Spanish-derived masculine suffix, see {{ncog|es|-o}}), the word is sometimes assumed to be masculine. The term {{m|tl|iska}} is used to specify a female state university student.
-------- end text --------
