Page 7622 iwan: Already saw {{tl-pr}}, skipping: {{tl-pr}}
Page 7622 iwan: Skipped, no changes
Page 7622 iwan: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From Proto-Central-Philippine ''*áyaw'' ("to leave, redistribute") + ''-an'' (''ayawan'' → ''aywan'' → ''ewan'' → ''iwan''). Cognates with {{cog|msk|ayaw||to leave}} and {{cog|ceb|ayaw||to cry (as a child) when left behind}}. See also {{m|tl|ayaw}}. {{doublet|tl|aywan}}. An alternate etymology from Panganiban (1972) posits it theoretically to be from {{suf|tl|iwi|an|t1=taking care of a domestic animal in behalf of the owner}}.

Attested in the ''{{w|Doctrina Christiana}}'' as ''œvan'', written in [[Baybayin]] as {{tl-bay sc|iwan|trad=1|disp=1|tr=1}}, most likely reflecting ''ewan'' or ''eywan''. In the book, the {{angbr|œ}} character (possibly an {{angbr|æ}} character) was sometimes written in Baybayin as {{tl-bay sc|ay|trad=1|disp=1|tr=1}}. Hence, the word can also reflect ''aywan''.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Verb===
{{tl-verb|+|iniwan|iniiwan|iiwan|b=+}}

# to [[leave behind]] (a person or thing)
#: {{syn|tl|di-isama|di-dalhin}}
# to [[abandon]]; to [[forsake]]; to [[let alone]]
#: {{syn|tl|bayaan|pabayaan|layasan}}
# to [[get away]] from
#: {{syn|tl|lisanan|layuan}}

====Conjugation====
{{tl-infl-in-an||i|w|iwan|object}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|iwanan|mag-iwan|magpaiwan|maiwan|maiwanan|mang-iwan|mapag-iwanan|paiwan|iwan sa eyre}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:CEDOF|4|189}}
* {{R:Diksyunaryo tesauro Pilipino-Ingles 1973|page=573}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1860}}

-------- end text --------
