Page 7721 k: Replaced {{tl-IPA|key}} with {{tl-pr|key}}
Page 7721 k: Replaced {{tl-IPA|ka}} with {{tl-pr|ka}}
Page 7721 k: Would save with comment = convert {{tl-IPA}} to {{tl-pr}} (2)
Page 7721 k: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{bor+|tl|es|k}}. Each pronunciation has a different source:
* Filipino alphabet pronunciation is influenced by {{der-lite|tl|en|k}}.
* Abakada alphabet pronunciation is influenced by Baybayin character {{m-lite|tl|ᜃ|sc=Tglg|tr=ka}}.
* Abecedario pronunciation is from {{der-lite|tl|es|k}}.

The use of {{angbr|k}} instead of using the Spanish-based {{angbr|c}} and {{angbr|q}} was promoted in the late 19th century primarily by the educated (such as {{w|José Rizal}} and {{w|Trinidad Pardo de Tavera}}) because of the Baybayin character primarily being applicable to all vowels, as well as the ease of usage with Tagalog grammar rules. Its order in the Abakada alphabet was due to the order of the similar sounding {{angbr|c}} in the Spanish alphabet.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr
|kéy<qq:letter name, Filipino alphabet>
|ká<qq:letter name, Abakada alphabet, Abecedario>
|+<qq:phoneme>
|raw:/k/ [x]<qq:phoneme, intervocalic>
}}

====Letter====
{{tl-letter|b=key}}

# {{tl-letter-def|11|key|alph=fil}}

=====See also=====
* {{list:Latin script letters/tl}}

====Letter====
{{tl-letter|b=ka}}

# {{tl-letter-def|3|ka|alph=abak}}
# {{lb|tl|historical}} {{tl-letter-def|12|ka|alph=abec}}

===Etymology 2===

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|key}}

====Interjection====
{{tl-head|interjection|b=key}}

# {{lb|tl|Internet slang|text messaging}} [[OK]]

===Etymology 3===

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|ka}}

====Pronoun====
{{tl-pron|b=ka}}

# {{lb|tl|Internet slang|text messaging}} {{alt form of|tl|ka}} {{q|in text messaging and Internet conversations}}: [[you]]; [[u]]
#: {{ux|tl|Nasan '''k''' na?|Where are '''u'''?}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{cite-journal|first=Megan C.|last=Thomas|title=K Is for De-Kolonization: Anti-Colonial Nationalism and Orthographic Reform|work=Comparative Studies in Society and History|page=938–967|year=2007|url=https://www.jstor.org/stable/4497712|volume=49|issue=4|issn=0010-4175}}

-------- end text --------
