Page 7772 kaban: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|caban||obsolete|Abecedario spelling}}

===Etymology===
According to Blust (2010–), it is listed as a [[loan]] distributed among many Philippine languages, such as {{cog|ilo|kaban}}, {{cog|kne|kaban}}, {{cog|pag|kaban}}, {{cog|ksn|kaban}}, {{cog|bcl|kaban}}, {{cog|ceb|kaban}}, {{cog|agn|kaban}}, and many more,<ref>{{R:map:ACD|id=30049|type=lo|dry measure for grain}}</ref> which may possibly be from {{inh|tl|poz-pro|*kaban||dry measure for grain etc.}}. Compare {{cog|ja|-}} {{ja-r|鞄|かばん|t=bag}}, {{cog|nan-hbl|合萬|tr=kap-bān|t=[[cashbox]]; [[till]]}}, {{cog|nan-tws|合萬|tr=kap buāng|t=[[safebox]]}}, {{cog|yue|夾萬|tr=gaap<sup>3</sup> maan<sup>6</sup>|t=[[safebox]]}}

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|kabán}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|kabán|b=+}}

# [[chest]]; [[trunk]] {{q|especially one for clothes}}
#: {{syn|tl|baul}}
# {{lb|tl|Christianity|Islam}} [[ark]]
# [[cavan]] {{gl|a measurement of around 75 liters}}
## a [[sack]] {{q|e.g. of rice}}
##: {{syn|tl|sako}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|Kaban ng Tipan}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|es|caván|bor=1}}

===References===
<references/>

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}

{{C|tl|Units of measure}}

