Page 7793 kabayo: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|cabayo||obsolete|Abecedario orthography}}

===Etymology===
Earlier (c. 16th-18th century) borrowing from {{bor|tl|es|caballo}} (then spelled as {{m|es|cavallo}}), from {{der|tl|LL.|caballus}}. {{doublet|tl|kabalyo}}. During time of borrowing, {{cog|es|''⟨[[ll]]⟩''}} ({{IPAchar|/ʝ/}}) still corresponds to {{noncog|tl|-}} {{IPAchar|/j/}}, as per [[yeísmo]]. Compare {{cog|ceb|kabayo}} and {{cog|ilo|kabalio}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# [[horse]]
# [[ironing board]]
#: {{syn|tl|plantsahan}}
# {{lb|tl|chess}} [[knight]]
# {{lb|tl|card games}} [[jack]]
#: {{syn|tl|sota}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|kabayong-dagat|kabayong pangarera|mangabayo|mangangabayo|kabayuhan|kabayuhin|karera ng kabayo|kiling ng kabayo|nakakabayo|palahing kabayo|pangangabayo|magkabayo|ay kabayo}}

====Related terms====
{{rel3|tl|kabalyerisa|kabalyeriya|kabalyero|kabalyerosidad|kabalyete|kabalyo}}

====See also====
{{table:chess pieces/tl}}
{{table:playing cards/tl}}

