Page 7987 kalabaw: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=tl}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|karabaw||Marinduque}}

===Etymology===
{{bor+|tl|es|carabao}}, from {{der|tl|war|karabaw}},<ref>Roberts, E. A. (2014). A Comprehensive Etymological Dictionary of the Spanish Language with Families of Words based on Indo-European Roots. Volume I (A–G). XLibris LLC. p. 311. {{ISBN|9781493191109}}.</ref> from {{der|tl|ms|kerbau}}, from {{der|tl|poz-mly-pro|*kAr(ə)baw}}, ultimately from {{der|tl|mkh-pro|*krpiʔ|*krpiʔ ~ *krpiiw ~ *krpuʔ ~ *(kr)puh|buffalo}}.<ref>{{R:map:ACD|type=lo|carabao}}</ref> Cognate with Modern {{cog|km|ក្របី}}, {{cog|hal|kơpùa}}, {{cog|ms|kerbau}}, {{cog|jv|ꦏꦼꦧꦺꦴ}}, {{cog|th|กระบือ}}.  Before the coming of the Spaniards, the native Tagalog term used to refer to the animal is {{m|tl|anwang}}. The word {{m|tl|kalabaw}} itself does not appear in the earliest Tagalog dictionaries.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|kalabáw}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|kalabáw|b=+}}

# [[carabao]]; [[water buffalo]] {{gloss|large ungulate}}
#: {{syn|tl|damulag|anwang|q2=archaic}}
# [[carabeef]]
# {{lb|tl|informal}} [[neckerchief]] [[slide]] in the Philippine [[Boy Scout]] [[uniform]], which is the likeness of the head of a carabao

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|balat-kalabaw|pakong-kalabaw|kayod-kalabaw}}

====See also====
{{col3|tl|kalakian|malatandok|panleeg|pinak|pugik|sikwat|kubaw|malatundok|unga}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|kalabáw|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|figurative|colloquial}} [[lazy]]
#: {{syn|tl|tamad}}

===References===
<references/>

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}

{{C|tl|Bovines}}
