Page 8141 kaluluwa: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|caloloua||obsolete|Abecedario orthography}}
* {{alt|tl|kalulowa}}
* {{alt|tl|kalulwa}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|tl|phi-pro|*ka-du-duha||soul, spirit of a living person}}, from {{prefix|tl|ka|}} {{m|phi-pro|*duha|t=two|pos=fossilized form of {{m|tl|dalawa}}}}, with {{rdp|tl||nocap=1}} of the first syllable of the root, and {{IPAchar|/d/}} sound-shifted to {{IPAchar|/l/}}. Compare {{cog|ilo|kararua}}, {{cog|pag|kamarerua}}, {{cog|duo|kaliduwa}}, {{cog|ibg|ikakarwa}}, {{cog|pam|kaladdua}}, {{cog|tbw|kiyarulwa}}, {{cog|mrw|ikadowa}}, {{cog|msk|kallowa}}, {{cog|tsg|aluwa}}, and {{cog|dtp|koduduo}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|kaluluwá,káluluwá}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|kaluluwá|head2=káluluwá|b=+}}

# [[soul]]; [[spirit]]; [[essence]]
#: {{syn|tl|espiritu|diwa|buhay|alma|anima}}
# {{lb|tl|obsolete}} [[rational]] [[soul]]

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|Araw ng mga Kaluluwa|pangkaluluwa|halang ang kaluluwa|walang kaluluwa|kaluluwahin|mangaluluwa|may-kaluluwa|kumaluluwa|magkaluluwa|buong kaluluwa|makaluluwa|pangangaluluwa|kaluluwahan}}

====Related terms====
{{rel3|tl|dalawa}}

====See also====
{{col3|tl|hilagyo|lakas ng loob|kakambal}}

