Page 8221 kamote: Already saw {{tl-pr}}, skipping: {{tl-pr}}
Page 8221 kamote: Skipped, no changes
Page 8221 kamote: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{bor+|tl|es|camote||sweet potato}}, from {{der|tl|nci|camohtli||}}. Senses about performing badly is possibly an expression about students should instead plant potatoes, or a play on the word {{m|tl|kamot||scrach}}, about scratching one's heads when unable to know what to do. However, some sources state that the senses already exist as part of Spanish slang to mean that way. See also {{cog|nan-hbl|大番薯|tr=[[tōa-han-chî]]}}, {{cog|yue|大番薯|tr=daai{{sup|6}} faan{{sup|1}} syu{{sup|4-2}}}}, {{cog|hak|大番薯}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# [[sweet potato]] {{gl|{{taxfmt|Ipomoea batatas|species}}}}
# the [[tuber]] of this [[plant]]
# {{lb|tl|slang}} act of [[perform]]ing badly on a [[task]]
# {{lb|tl|slang|by extension}} a [[driver]] with little or no regard for the [[rules of the road]]

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|kamoteng-kahoy}}

====See also====
* {{l|tl|patatas}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|slang}} [[puzzled]]; [[unable]] to [[figure out]] how to [[resolve]] a [[problem]] or a [[task]]

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|kamote ang ulo|anak ng kamote|mangamote|pangangamote|makamote}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|nan-hbl|ka-mú-tī|bor=1}}

====See also====
* {{l|tl|loko}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:Tagalog Slang Dictionary}}
* {{R:tl:Hispanismos 1972|page=104|q=kamote}}

{{C|tl|Vegetables|Root vegetables|Morning glory family plants}}
