Page 8228 kampante: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{bor+|tl|es|campante}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|b=+}}

# acting as if nothing happens; [[ignorant]]; [[indifferent]]
# [[smug]]; [[complacent]]
#: {{ux|tl|Tila '''kampante''' siya na wala na siyang kailangang tapusin.|He seemed '''complacent''' that he doesn't have anything needed to finish.}}
#* year unknown, ''Sigay Ii' 2005 Ed.'', Rex Bookstore, Inc. ({{ISBN|9789712340536}}), page 6:
#*: '''Kampante''' tayo noon sa lakas ng mga mananakop na Americano na hindi kailanman makakalmot man lang ng mga “mababang-uri” na Hapones.
#*:: We felt smug under the power of the American occupants who have not received a single scratch from the "lower than [human]" Japanese.
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=2003|author=Isagani R. Cruz; David Jonathan Bayot|title=Bukod na bukod: mga piling sanaysay|isbn=9789715423281
|passage=Huwag tayong pumayag na maging '''kampante''' tayo dahil nabasa na natin sina Derrida o Foucault o Lacan o Jameson o Eagleton o Ashcroft o Soyinka o Ngugi  o Murthy; lagi nating isipin na marami pa tayong hindi nababasa.
|t=We should not allow ourselves to become complacent because we have read Derrida or Foucault or Lacan or Jameson or Eagleton or Ashcroft or Soyinka or Ngugi or Murthy; we should always think that we have a lot we have not read.}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
