Page 8324 kanto boy: Removing explicit syllabification same as auto-syllabification: {{hyph|tl|kan|to boy}}
Page 8324 kanto boy: Replaced {{tl-IPA}} with {{tl-pr}}
Page 8324 kanto boy: Would save with comment = convert {{tl-IPA}} to {{tl-pr}}; remove {{hyph}} same as respelling auto-syllabification
Page 8324 kanto boy: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{bor+|tl|en|kanto boy}}, from {{compound|en|kanto|t1=corner, especially of two streets|lang1=tl|boy|nocat=1}}. According to Potet (2016), the former term ''*kanto'' was originally from {{der|tl|ja|-}} {{ja-r|官庁|かんちょう|t=government office}}, borrowed in during [[WW2]]. The word was reinterpreted to mean {{m-g|office corner}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|vulgar|slang}}

# [[bum]]; [[deadbeat]]; [[loafer]]; [[idler]]
#: {{syn|tl|palaboy|tambay}}
# {{lb|tl|humorous}} [[office boy]]

====Related terms====
{{rel3|tl|kanto girl}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:tl:Potet|TBC|page=343}}
* {{R:Tagalog Slang Dictionary|72}}
