Page 8518 karinderya: Skipped, no changes
Page 8518 karinderya: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|karinderiya|karinderia}}
* {{alt|tl|carinderia|carenderia}}

===Etymology===
From {{w|Philippine Spanish|Philippine}} {{bor|tl|es|carindería}}, where the root itself is from {{der|tl|es|carí}} which itself is from {{der|tl|tl|kari|t=curry}}, according to {{w|Wenceslao Retana}} (1920). The {{w|Philippine Spanish}} term was coined by analogy with {{cog|tl|karihan|t=place where [[curry]] is sold}} and {{noncog|es|cafetería}}, according to Zorc (1981). {{surf|tl|karindero|-erya}}. Compare {{noncog|es|panadería}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|karinderyá,+}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|karinderyá|head2=+|b=+}}

# [[carinderia]] {{gl|a small restaurant or eatery selling local food}}

====See also====
{{col3|tl|turo-turo}}

===References===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:CEDOF|2|79}}
* {{cite-book|en|author=Santa María Sta María|title=The Governor-general's Kitchen: Philippine Culinary Vignettes and Period Recipes, 1521-1935|year=2006|publisher=Published and exclusively distributed by Anvil|url=https://www.google.com.ph/books/edition/The_Governor_general_s_Kitchen/gdPgAAAAMAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&bsq=carinderia|isbn=978-971-27-1696-6}}
