===Etymology===
{{bor+|tl|es|[[carne]] [[norte]]|lit=north meat}} likely referring to {{noncog|es|norteamericano|t=North American}} as in {{m-g|North American meat}} since it was brought in during the 20th century in {{w|History of the Philippines (1898–1946)|American colonial times}}. Compare {{cog|en|carne norte}}. Polistico (2017) mentions that it was probably a brand name. {{gentrade|tl|notext=1}} {{surf|tl|karne|norte}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|karné nórte}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|[[karné]] [[nórte]]|b=+}}

# [[corned beef]]

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|ginisang karne norte|tortang karne norte}}

