Page 8695 katay: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Possibly related to {{cog|map-pro|*aCay||death}} (compare {{noncog|tl|matay}}, {{m|tl|patay}}, and {{m|tl|bitay}}), or from {{noncog|nan-hbl|[[共]][[伊]][[刣]]|tr=kā i thâi|lit=have it/him/her slaughtered}} according to Chan-Yap (1980).<ref name="Chan-Yap"/><ref name="Zorc"/> See more at {{cog|nan-hbl|刣|tr=thâi}} where the second element may simply be a substrate cognate word comparable to {{cog|map-pro|*aCay||death}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|+<n^>|katáy<a^>}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# [[act]] of [[kill]]ing or [[butcher]]ing an [[animal]] for [[food]]
#: {{syn|tl|pagkatay|pagkakatay}}
# [[act]] of [[cut]]ting a [[butcher]]ed [[animal]] into [[piece]]s
#: {{syn|tl|lapa|paglapa|paglalapa}}
# [[big]] [[slice]] or [[cut]] of [[meat]]
# {{lb|tl|by extension}} [[fish]], [[small]] [[piece]]s of [[meat]], etc. tied or strung together in a [[bundle]]
#: {{syn|tl|tali|bungkos|tuhog}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|katayan|katayin|kumatay|magkatay|pagkatay|kinatay|sangkatay}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|katáy|b=+}}

# [[slaughter]]ed or [[butcher]]ed for [[food]], [[refer]]ring to an [[animal]]
# [[cut]] into [[big]] [[piece]]s, [[refer]]ring to a [[butcher]]ed [[animal]]
#: {{syn|tl|lapa|nilapa}}

===References===
<references>
<ref name="Chan-Yap">{{R:tl:Chan-Yap 1980|page=145}}</ref>
<ref name="Zorc">{{R:CEDOF|2|82}}</ref>
</references>

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}

