Page 8768 katutubo: Would save with comment = convert {{tl-IPA}} to {{tl-pr}}; remove {{hyph}} same as respelling auto-syllabification
Page 8768 katutubo: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|catotobo|catutubo||obsolete|Abecedario orthography}}.

===Etymology===
From {{prefix|tl|ka-|tubo|t2=sprout}} with {{rdp|tl||nocap=1}} of the first syllable of the root.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|katutubò}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|katutubò|b=+}}

# [[native]]; [[indigenous]]
#: {{syn|tl|taal}}
# [[natural]]; [[inborn]]
#: {{syn|tl|likas|natural}}
# [[share|sharing]] the same [[age]]

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|katutubò|b=+}}

# [[native]]; [[aborigine]]
# {{lb|tl|obsolete}} [[guardian]] [[angel]]
#: {{syn|tl|anghel na tagatanod}}
#: {{ux|tl|Ano'ng bati mo sa ansilis na '''katutubo''' mo bago ka mahiga kung gabi?|What salutation do you say to your '''guardian angel''' before you go to bed at night?}}

====Usage notes====
* According to Fr. Pedro de San Buena Ventura (1613) and Fr. Domingo de los Santos (1835), a '''''katutubo''''' ({{lit|someone  sprouted with|someone with the same age|nocap=1}}) is a guardian angel believed long ago to be given to each man at the time of their birth by {{m|tl|Bathala|Bathalang}} {{m|tl|Maykapal}} or born with the person for the person's protection, of which they call {{m|tl|bathalang katutubo}} (or {{m|tl|badhalang katutubo}} in Noceda & Sanlucar (1860)).

====See also====
{{col3|tl|kerubin|ansilis}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1860}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1613|57|Angel) Catutubo (pp) de guarda, antiguamente creyan eſtos que en naçiendo el hombre, luego el bathalang maycapal, q̃ es. D. N. S. le daua otro como Dios q̃ le guarda ſe, al qual llamauan, bathalang catutubo, o q̃ naçia con el, de ſuerte q̃ creyan tener quiẽ los guardaſe de parte de Dios.}}
* {{R:tl:Potet|ABCT|page=167}}
