===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|tl|poz-pro|*kaya||able, capable, strong, wealthy}}. Compare {{cog|ms|kaya||wealth; power}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|+<audio:Tl-PH-kaya.ogg>}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# [[ability]]; [[capability]]; [[competence]]
#: {{syn|tl|kakayahan}}
# [[means]]; [[resources]]; [[wealth]]; [[wherewithal]]

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|kakayahan|may-kaya|[[kayahin]] ([[kayanin]])|makaya|kawalang-kaya|ubos-kaya|bigay-kaya|abot-kaya}}

====Adjective====
{{tl-adj|b=+}}

# [[able]] to do; [[capable]] to do
#: {{syn|tl|magagawa}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''Kaya''' natin ito!|We '''can''' do this!}}

====Adverb====
{{tl-adv|b=+}}

# [[ably]]; in an able [[manner]]
#: {{syn|tl|makakaya}}

===Etymology 2===

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|tl|kaya't}}
* {{alt|tl|kung kaya}}
* {{alt|tl|kanya}}

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|kayâ}}

====Conjunction====
{{tl-head|conjunction|kayâ|b=+}}

# [[so]]; [[therefore]]; [[hence]]
#: {{syn|tl|dahil doon|dahil diyan|sa gayon}}
#: {{ux|tl|Marami siyang ginawang trabaho, '''kaya''' pag-uwi niya'y nakatulog siya agad.|He'd done a lot of work, so as soon as he got home, he fell asleep instantly.}}
# [[as a result]]; [[consequently]]
#: {{syn|tl|samakatwid|anupa't}}

====Adverb====
{{tl-adv|kayâ|b=+}}

# {{n-g|expression to indicate an uncertainty or doubt}}; [[perhaps]]; I [[wonder]]
#: {{syn|tl|kali|q1=Bataan}}
#: {{ux|tl|Ano '''kaya''' ang nangyari?|What could have happened?}}
# {{n-g|used with {{m|tl|o}} to connect choices being considered with uncertainty}}
#: {{ux|tl|Bumili ka ng karne o '''kaya''' ay isda para sa hapunan natin.|Buy meat or perhaps fish for our dinner.}}
# {{lb|tl|informal}} {{n-g|expression for [[emphasis]]}}
#: {{ux|tl|Lagi mong iniisip na pangit ka. Maganda ka '''kaya'''.|You always think you're ugly. You're very pretty, indeed!
}}

