===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|kay sa}}
* {{alt|tl|kaysasa|kaysa sa}}
* {{alt|tl|kesa||colloquial}}

===Etymology===
Possibly {{univerbation|tl|kay|sa|nocap=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|kaysá|kesa<qq:relaxed>}}

===Conjunction===
{{tl-head|conjunction|kaysá|b=+}}

# [[than]]
#: {{ux|tl|Mas maganda ako '''kaysa''' sa'yo.|I'm more beautiful '''than''' you.}}

====Usage notes====
* When the second term compared is a person, use {{m|tl|kaysa kay}}. For multiple persons, use {{m|tl|kaysa kina}}.
* In colloquial Manila Tagalog, {{m|tl|kaysa}} is always followed by {{m|tl|sa}} or {{m|tl|kay}} when used to mean "than". 

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|kaysa sa|kaysa kay|kaunti kaysa|kaysa kina|mas matimbang ang dugo kaysa tubig}}

===Preposition===
{{tl-head|preposition|kaysá|b=+}}

# [[rather than]]; [[instead of]]

