Page 8980 kina: WARNING: For spelling '', rhyme a not same as pronunciation-based rhyme ina: {{rhymes|tl|a}}
Page 8980 kina: Would save with comment = convert {{tl-IPA}} to {{tl-pr}}; remove {{rhymes}} same as auto-generated rhyme; remove {{hyph}} same as respelling auto-syllabification
Page 8980 kina: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|kiná}}

====Preposition====
{{tl-prep|kiná|b=+}}

# {{ngd|Used to mark [[oblique case]]s of personal nouns}}
#: {{ux|tl|Ang awiting ito ay para '''kina''' papa at mama.|This song is '''for''' (my) father and (my) mother.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* This is used where there is more than one addressee, as a simpler way of saying ''kay'' [1st referrent] … ''at kay'' [last referrent] (e.g. ''kina Pedro at Juan'').
* Where it precedes one name, this refers to the person and others surrounding them (e.g. ''Kina Pedro'' refers to Pedro and anyone other around him, usually unspecified).

=====Alternative forms=====
* {{alt|tl|kana|kila|kinda|kanila}}

=====See also=====
{{tl-markers}}

===Etymology 2===
{{bor+|tl|es|quina}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# [[cinchona]]
#: {{syn|tl|singkona}}

=====Alternative forms=====
* {{alt|tl|kino}}

=====See also=====
{{col3|tl|dita|kinina}}

-------- end text --------
