===Etymology 1===
From {{der|tl|poz-pro|*(i-)kita}}, from {{der|tl|map-pro|*(i-)kita}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|kitá<audio:tl-ph-kita-pronoun.ogg>}}

====Pronoun====
{{tl-pron|kitá|b=+}}

# {{n-g|Replaces '''{{m|tl|ko}} {{m|tl|ka}}''' or '''{{m|tl|ko}} {{m|tl|ikaw}}''' ([[I]] or [[my]] and [[you]]). Used when speaking directly to the receiver of a verb.}}
#: {{ux|tl|Mahal ko siya, mahal ko sila, mahal ko tayong lahat—at ikaw, mahal '''kita'''.|I love him, I love them, I love all of us—and you, '''I''' love '''you'''.}}
#: {{ux|tl|Anak '''kita'''.|'''You''' are '''my''' child.}}
# {{lb|tl|now|_|dialectal|Batangas|Marinduque|uncommon|_|in|_|Bulacan}} [[we]]; the two of us; [[you]] and [[I]]
#: {{syn|tl|kata|[[tayo]]ng [[dalawa]]}}
#: {{ux|tl|Magkaibigan '''kita'''.|'''You and I''' are friends.}}

====See also====
{{tl-personal pronouns}}
* {{l|tl|mahal kita}}
* {{l|tl|gusto kita}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|tl|phi-pro|*kitaʔ}}, from {{inh|tl|poz-pro|*kita}}, from {{inh|tl|map-pro|*kita}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|+|kità<audio:tl-ph-kita-noun.ogg>}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|+|head2=kità|b=+}}

# state or quality of being [[seen]]; [[visibility]]
# [[observation]]
#: {{syn|tl|pagkakita}}

====Adjective====
{{tl-adj|+|head2=kità|b=+}}

# [[seen]]; [[visible]]
#: {{syn|tl|nakikita|litaw|nakalitaw|hayag|nakahayag|tanaw|natatanaw}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''Kita''' ang bahay namin mula rito.|Our house can be '''seen''' from here.|lit=Our house is '''visible''' from here.}}
# [[obvious]]; easily [[seen]] or [[understood]]

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|ipakita|kinikita|kitain|kitang-kita|kumita|magkita|magpakita|magpangita|makakita|makini-kinita|makipagkita|makita|mapakita|pagkakita|pagkikita|pagpapakita|pakikipagkita|pakita|pakitaan|pakitang-gilas|pakitang-tao|pangita|pangitain|kini-kinita|kitakits}}

