Page 9378 kuha: Skipped, no changes
Page 9378 kuha: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From Proto-Central Philippine ''*kúha(ʔ)'' (“to get; to take”). Compare {{cog|bcl|kua}}, {{cog|ceb|kuha}}, {{cog|pam|kua}}, {{cog|mrw|kowa}}, and {{cog|tsg|kawaꞌ}}. According to Zorc (2021), it might be from {{inh|tl|map-pro|*kuSa||work}} with semantic reassignment. Compare {{cog|ckv|kuway||to work in the field}} and {{cog|isd|kuwa||to work}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr
|+,kuhà<n^(act of) taking, catching, grabbing, etc.; catch, shot; adaptation><a^taken/adapted from; having gotten the hang of; having inherited><int^got it>
|kuhá<a^similar to the original; successfully taken>
}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|+|head2=kuhà|b=+}}

# [[take]]; [[grab]]; [[act]] of [[get]]ting {{q|as with one's hand}}
#: {{syn|tl|pagkuha|getlak|q2=gay slang}}
# [[act]] of [[obtain]]ing or [[receive|receiving]]
#: {{syn|tl|pagkuha|tanggap|pagtanggap|tamo|pagtatamo|kamit|pagkakamit}}
# [[capture]]; [[shot]]; [[snap]]; [[taking]] {{q|of a picture}}
#: {{syn|tl|pagkuha|pagkakuha}}
#: {{ux|tl|Maganda ang '''kuha''' mo sa akin.|Your '''shot''' of my picture is nice.}}
# [[capture]]; [[catch]] {{q|of fish, etc.}}
# [[act]] of [[hire|hiring]] (someone to work)
# [[adaptation]] {{q|of something from another}}
#: {{syn|tl|hango|paghango|batay|pagbabatay}}
# [[helping]]; [[portion]] {{q|of food}}
#: {{syn|tl|bulos|q=dialectal}}
# {{lb|tl|by extension}} [[act]] of [[steal]]ing something
#: {{syn|tl|umit|pag-umit|kupit|pagkupit|nakaw|pagnakaw}}
# {{lb|tl|by extension}} [[abortion]]; [[miscarriage]]

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|kunin|kumuha|ipakuha|ipangkuha|ikakuha|ikuha|manguha|kunan|makuha|makakuha|kuhaan|magpakuha|hinuha|hinguha|nenok|makuha sa tingin|kukunan|kukunang-yaman|makunan|magkuhanan|pagkukunan|pagkuhananan|pagkunan|pagkakuha|pagkuha|panguhanin|pangunin|kuhanan|panguha|paghihinguha|hinguhahin|mapaghinguha|hingunin|hingunan|panghinguha|manghinguha|ipanghinguha|mapanghinguha|panghihinguhaan|mahinuha|maghinuha|hinuhain|paghihinuha}}

====See also====
{{col3|tl|abot|dampot|pulot|pitas}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|+|head2=kuhà|b=+}}

# [[get the hang of|gotten the hang of]] something; [[managed]] to [[learn]] to [[handle]] something
# [[taken]] from; [[adapted]] from
#: {{syn|tl|hango|hinango|batay|ibinatay}}
# having [[inherited]] certain [[feature]]s {{q|as from one's parents}}
#: {{syn|tl|mana}}

===Interjection===
{{tl-head|interjection|+|head2=kuhà|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|informal}} [[got it]]; [[understood]]
#: {{syn|tl|gets|q1=slang|getlak|q2=gay slang}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|kuhá|b=+}}

# [[similar]] to the [[original]] {{q|as of a picture or drawing}}
#: {{syn|tl|kamukha}}
# [[successfully]] [[taken]] or [[obtained]]
#: {{syn|tl|nakuha|natamo}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{cite-journal|author=Zorc, R. D., & Almarines, A.|title=Axis Relationships in the Philippines–When Traditional Subgrouping Falls Short|url=https://upd.edu.ph/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/AXIS-relationshipsZorc-Presentation.pdf?fbclid=IwAR0rPKUUopCxoxDmo8ZyWbtG8fs5l1dIMt50W1LvXuR5fTerVsDhUM4tkfc|journal=14th Philippine Linguistics Congress|date=August 2021|volume=24|format=PDF}}

