{{unc|tl}}, but it can be literally "scraping a fish's snout" (from {{m|tl|kuskos||to scrape; to rub}} and {{m|tl|balungos||fish's snout}}), or a borrowing from {{bor|tl|ceb|kuskos balungos|lit=scratching one's pubic hair}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|kuskós-balungos}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|kuskós-balungos|b=+}}

# [[fuss]]; [[excessive]] [[activity]], [[worry]], [[talk]], [[complaint]], or [[detail]]s about something {{gl|that causes delay}}
#: {{syn|tl|kuntil-butil|rekobeko|kesyo-kesyo}}
#* {{quote-text|tl|year=1998|author=Rogelio L. Ordoñez|title=Saan papunta ang mga putok ?
|passage=Inaasahan naming pagdating sa bahaging ito ay “napagsaluhan” na natin ang “ piging” - isang masaganang hapag ng mga putaheng pampanitikan na handog sa  atin ni Ka Roger. Nang wala nang marami pang pasakalye at '''kuskos-balungos'''.
|translation=We expect at this part, we will "share" the "feast" - a lavish table of literary recipes out brother Roger provided us. [But], without lots of introductory ceremonies and fuss.}}
-------- end text --------
