Page 9714 kuwan: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|coan|couan||obsolete|Abecedario}}

===Etymology===
Possibly either from the following:
* From {{inh|tl|poz-pro|*kuan||to speak, talk}}, or derived from {{der|tl|poz-pro|*kua||whatchamacallit}}. Cognate with {{cog|ilo|[[kua]]}}, {{cog|ceb|kuan}}, {{cog|tsg|kuwan}}, {{cog|btx|er-kuan||to speak}}, and {{cog|tnt|kuan||what is said or thought}}.
* From {{der|tl|sa|क्व||somewhere}}, according to Potet (2016).
* From a corruption of {{der|tl|es|cuál||what}}, according to Panganiban (1973).

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|kuwán}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|kuwán|b=+}}

# [[so-and-so]], [[whatchamacallit]] {{gl|placeholder name for a person or thing}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|magkuwan|kumuwan|makikuwan|magpakuwan}}

====See also====
{{col3|tl|ano}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:tl:Potet|TBC|page=286}}
* {{R:Diksyunaryo tesauro Pilipino-Ingles 1973|page=327}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1613}}
** page 327: “Fulano) Covan [(pc)] bordonçillo que tienen eſtos como en eſpañol como [ſe llama], pero eſtos ncada paſo lo diçen como noſe acuerden del nombre propio, vt. [ſi covan] [ſi caſambil], ſulano caſambil.”
** page 358: “Hulano) Covan [(pc)] bordonçillo vſado entre eſtos ſiao ſe acuerdan de lo quee van a deçir, vt. covã dico naalala, como ſe diço a que nome acuerdo, ſi covan, hulano”
