Page 9755 kuya: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|coya|cuya||obsolete|Abecedario orthography}}
* {{alt|tl|koya||now|colloquial}}

===Etymology===
{{bor+|tl|nan-hbl|哥仔|tr=*ko-iá}} as per Chan-Yap (1980)<ref>{{R:tl:Chan-Yap 1980|page=141}}</ref> and Manuel (1948)<ref>{{R:tl:Manuel 1948|page=33}}</ref> with an older obsolete form of the diminutive suffix<ref>{{R:Dictionario Hispanico Sinicum|344/366}}</ref><ref>{{cite-book|last=Medhurst|first=Walter Henry|authorlink=Walter Henry Medhurst|publisher=East India Press|location=Macau|title=A Dictionary of the Hok-këèn Dialect of the Chinese Language: According to the Reading and Colloquial Idioms: Containing about 12,000 Characters|url=https://archive.org/details/dictionaryofhokk00medhrich|year=1832|worklang=en, nan-hbl|page=736}}</ref> as a weak form of {{zh-l|囝|tr=kiáⁿ, káⁿ}}. Cognate with {{cog|ceb|kuya}} and {{cog|pam|koya}}. Compare {{m|tl|guya}} and {{m|tl|piaya}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# [[elder brother]]; [[big brother]]
#: {{syn|tl|kuyang|q1=Nueva Ecija}}
#: {{ux|tl|Tumutulong si '''kuya''' sa aming mga magulang sa mga gawaing bahay.|Our '''big brother''' helps our parents do housework.}}
# {{lb|tl|informal}} {{n-g|[[term of address]] for a [[male]] [[senior]]}} {{q|in school, work, etc.}}
#: {{syn|tl|kuyang|q1=Nueva Ecija}}
#: {{ux|tl|Tinanong ko ang '''kuya''' sa hayskul, "'''Kuya''', ano po ang mga gawain niyo sa hayskul".|I asked my '''senior''' from high school, "'''Bro''', What activities do you do in high school?"}}
# {{lb|tl|informal}} {{n-g|[[term of address]] for any [[young]] [[male]]}}: [[mister]]; [[bro]]
#: {{syn|tl|kuyang|q1=Nueva Ecija|kuys|q2=slang}}
#: {{ux|tl|Bumili ako ng sorbetes kay '''kuya'''.|I bought ice cream from the '''mister'''.}}
# {{lb|tl|Bulacan|informal}} [[eldest]] [[male]] [[cousin]]
# {{lb|tl|Laguna|Tayabas|informal}} [[uncle]]

====Coordinate terms====
* {{l|tl|ate}}

