Page 9826 labi: Already saw {{tl-pr}}, skipping: {{tl-pr|labì}}
Page 9826 labi: Already saw {{tl-pr}}, skipping: {{tl-pr|labî,labí}}
Page 9826 labi: Skipped, no changes
Page 9826 labi: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
Compare {{cog|pam|labi}} and {{cog|xsb|labi}}, and possibly related to {{cog|bcl|ngabil}} and {{cog|ceb|ngabil}}. Possibly derived from {{noncog|es|labio||lips}}, according to Lopez (1965). See also {{ncog|fa|لبی|tr=labi||labial}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|labì}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|labì|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|anatomy}} [[lip]]
# [[rim]]; [[edge]] of a [[container]] {{q|as of a bowl, glass, cup, pitcher, etc.}}
# [[brink]]; [[edge]] {{q|of a ravine, etc.}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{col-auto|tl|katlabi|kagat-labi|labian|katlabian|lumabi|paglabi|may gatas pa sa labi}}

=====See also=====
{{col-auto|tl|nguso|bibig}}

===Etymology 2===
Ultimately from {{inh|tl|map-pro|*labiq}}. Compare {{cog|ilo|labi||remnant}}, {{cog|pam|labi||excess}}, and {{cog|ms|lebih||excess}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|labî,labí}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|labî|head2=labí|b=+}}

# [[remains]]; [[remnant]]; [[leftover]]
#: {{syn|tl|tira}}
# [[surplus]]; [[excess]]
#: {{syn|tl|sobra|labis}}
# [[corpse]]; [[cadaver]]; [[dead]] [[body]]
#: {{syn|tl|bangkay}}
# [[debris]]; [[ruin]]s
#: {{syn|tl|guho}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{col-auto|tl|malabi|nalalabi|labing-|labi ng aso|labimpito|labindalawa|labing-anim|labing-apat|labing-isa|labingwalo|labinlima|labinsiyam|labintatlo}}

