===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|tl|phi-pro|*laŋsa||odor of fish, blood}}, possibly from {{inh|tl|poz-pro|*laŋ(ə)si||fishy smell}}, from {{inh|tl|map-pro|*laŋ(ə)si||unpleasant odor}}. Compare {{cog|bcl|langsi}}, {{cog|akl|eangsa}}, {{cog|ceb|langsa}}, and {{cog|mrw|langensa}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|lansá}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|lansá|b=+}}

# [[characteristic]] [[fishy]] [[odor]] or [[taste]]
#: {{syn|tl|amoy-isda}}
# [[viscous]] [[substance]] covering the [[fish]]
# [[characteristic]] [[smell]] of [[blood]] {{gl|perceived as similar to a fishy smell}}
# {{lb|tl|figurative}} [[obscenity]]
#: {{syn|tl|laswa|kalaswaan|kabastusan}}

=====Alternative forms=====
* {{alt|tl|langsa||obsolete}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|kalansahan|malansa}}

