Page 10273 laya: Skipped, no changes
Page 10273 laya: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
Possibly from a {{blend|tl|layaw|haya|t1=satisfaction of one's needs and desires|t2=at ease; allow; tolerate|nocap=1}}, according to {{w|Virgilio S. Almario}} (1992). However, historian {{w|Zeus A. Salazar}} (1999) argued that the word was a standalone word and was already part of the Tagalog vocabulary by mid-19th century despite not being included in Fr. Noceda and Sanlucar's ''{{w|Vocabulario de la lengua tagala}}''. In addition, {{m|tl|malaya||free}} was listed as a surname in the ''{{w|Catálogo alfabético de apellidos}}'' which was first published 1849.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|layà,+<q:obsolete><n^>|layâ<a^>}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|layà|b=+}}

# [[freedom]]; [[liberty]]
#: {{syn|tl|kalayaan|pagsasarili}}
# [[ease]] of [[movement]] or [[performance]]; [[facility]]
#: {{syn|tl|luwag|kaluwagan}}
# {{lb|tl|colloquial}} [[right]]; [[privilege]]
#: {{syn|tl|karapatan}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|kalayaan|lumaya|magpalaya|palayain|malaya|nakalalaya|pagkakapalaya|pagkamalaya|pagkapalaya|paglaya|pagpapalaya|ibong malaya|malayang loob|ilaya|ikalaya|Araw ng Kalayaan}}

====Adjective====
{{tl-adj|layâ|b=+}}

# [[free]]; [[emancipated]]
#: {{syn|tl|libre|malaya}}
# [[pampered]]; [[given]] too much [[freedom]]
#: {{syn|tl|layaw}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|pagkalaya|kalayaan}}

===Etymology 2===

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

