===Etymology 1===
{{bor+|tl|ms|ribu}}, from {{der|tl|poz-pro|*ʀibu}}. (cf. {{cog|bcl|ribo}}, {{cog|ceb|libo}}, {{cog|cyo|ribo}}, {{cog|hil|libo}}, {{cog|isd|ribu}}, {{cog|jv|ꦲꦺꦮꦸ|tr=èwu}}, {{cog|knb|libu}}, {{cog|mg|arivo}}, {{cog|ms|ribu}}, {{cog|mrw|nggibo}}, {{cog|tsg|ibu}}, {{cog|tet|rihun}}, {{cog|wlo|rewu}}, and {{cog|yog|ribu}}). Also theorized to be late enough to be borrowed from {{w|Arabic language|Arabic}} {{m|ar|رِبْوَة}}, which meant “myriad” in reference to currency.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr}}

====Numeral====
{{tl-num|b=+}}

# {{cln|tl|cardinal numbers}} [[thousand]]
#: {{syn|tl|mil}}

=====Derived terms=====
