Page 10560 Linggo: Would save with comment = convert {{tl-IPA}} to {{tl-pr}}; remove {{hyph}} same as respelling auto-syllabification
Page 10560 Linggo: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|Ling.||abbreviation}}
* {{alt|tl|Lingo||proscribed|archaic|Abecedario orthography}}
* {{alt|tl|Dingo||obsolete|Abecedario orthography}}
* {{alt|tl|Dinggo||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
Zorc (1985) surmises it to possibly be from {{bor|tl|es|domingo||Sunday}}, which was possibly mistakenly analyzed as {{m|tl|luminggo}} (e.g. ''Luminggo na'', "It's Sunday", which could have been taken to mean "It's been a week"), from which the word is derived by removing the seeming infix {{m|tl|-um-}} and early change from {{IPAchar|/d/}} to {{IPAchar|/l/}}. However, according to Wolff (1976), it could also be from {{bor|tl|ms|minggu||week}}, which is from {{der|tl|pt|domingo||Sunday}}. Wolff argues that the change in initial nasal to {{IPAchar|/l/}} is also attested for {{w|Tagalog language|Tagalog}} {{m|tl|langka}} and {{w|Malay language|Malay}} {{m|ms|nangka}}. Ultimately from {{der|tl|LL.|diēs Dominicus|t=Sunday|lit=day of the Lord}}. {{doublet|tl|Dominggo}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|Linggó}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|Linggó|b=+}}

# [[Sunday]]
#: {{syn|tl|Dominggo|q1=archaic}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|Linggo de Ramos|Linggo ng Pagkabuhay|Linggo ng Palaspas|Linggo ng Paghihirap|Linggo ng Pentekostes}}

====Related terms====
{{rel3|tl|linggo|domino}}

===See also===
* {{list:days of the week/tl}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1613|260|Domingo) Lingo[(pc)] C. dia ſancto}}
* {{cite-book|year=1976|last=Wolff|first=John U.|chapter=Malay borrowings in Tagalog|title=Southeast Asian History and Historiography: Essays Presented to D. G. E. Hall|editors=C.D. Cowan & O.W. Wolters|location=Ithaca|publisher=Cornell University Press|url=https://zorc.net/RDZorc/TAGALOG/Wolff-1976-MalayBorrowingsInTagalog.pdf|page=351}}
* {{R:CEDOF|4|217}}
-------- end text --------
