===Etymology===
{{bor+|tl|es|lírica}}, feminine of {{m|es|lírico}}, from {{der|tl|la|lyricus}}, from {{der|tl|grc|λυρικός}}. Sense meaning "words to a song" is a {{sl|tl|en|lyrics|nocap=1}}. Correct Spanish term would be {{m|es|[[letras]] [[de]] [[canciones]]}}. {{doublet|tl|liriks}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|lírika}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|líriká|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|music}} [[lyrics]] {{gl|words to a song}}
#: {{syn|tl|liriks|titik|letra}}
# {{lb|tl|poetry}} [[lyric poetry]]

====Related terms====
{{rel3|tl|lira|liriko}}

====See also====
{{col3|tl|awitin}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
