Possibly from a {{rdp|tl||nocap=1}} of the last syllable of {{der|tl|es|abuelo}}, possibly also influenced by mimicking other likewise reduplicated syllable direct family terms like {{m|tl|nana}}, {{m|tl|tata}}, {{m|tl|mama}}, {{m|tl|papa}}, {{m|tl|kaka}}, {{m|tl|nene}}, etc. Compare {{m|tl|lelong}}, {{m|tl|lola}}, {{m|tl|lelang}}, {{m|tl|ninong}}, {{m|tl|ninang}}, etc.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|f=lola|b=+}}

# [[grandfather]]
#: {{syn|tl|lelong|ingkong|mamay|apo|nuno|amama<q:dialectal>|abwelo<q:archaic>|agwelo<q:archaic>}}
#: {{ux|tl|Masaya ang lola kahapon dahil dumating ang '''lolo'''.|Grandmother was happy yesterday because '''Grandfather''' came.}}
# {{lb|tl|colloquial}} {{n-g|term of address for an old man}}
#: {{syn|tl|tatay|ingkong}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|lolo sa tuhod|lolo sa talampakan|lolo sa sakong|maglolo}}

====Related terms====
