Page 11009 ma-: Replaced {{tl-IPA}} with {{tl-pr}}
Page 11009 ma-: Would save with comment = convert {{tl-IPA}} to {{tl-pr}}
Page 11009 ma-: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|tl|poz-pro|*ma-}}, from {{inh|tl|map-pro|*ma-}}. Compare {{m|tl|may|pos=existential marker}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Prefix===
{{tl-head|prefix|b=+}}

# {{n-g|used to form adjectives indicating a quality}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|linis|t1=cleanliness|malinis|t2=clean}}
# {{n-g|actor III trigger infinitive verb prefix}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|ligo|t1=bath|maligo|t2=to take a bath; to bathe}}
# {{n-g|object IV trigger infinitive verb prefix}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|basa|t1=wet|mabasa|t2=to become wet}}
# {{n-g|object trigger to have done something; to be able to do something}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|tapos|t1=finish|matapos|t2=to be able to finish something}}
#: {{uxi|tl|'''Natapos''' kong basahin ang libro kagabi.|I was able to finish reading the book last night.}}
# {{n-g|object trigger to perform the action of the verb unintentionally}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|basag|t1=break, crack|mabasag|t2=to break something unintentionally}}
#: {{uxi|tl|'''Nabasag''' ko ang salamin.|I '''unintentionally broke''' the mirror.}} {{n-g|Compare it when used with the suffix '''-in''':}}
#: {{m|tl|basag|t=break, crack}} + {{m|tl|-in}} → {{m|tl|basagin|t=to break something on purpose}}
#: {{uxi|tl|'''Binasag''' ko ang salamin.|I '''broke''' the mirror on purpose.}}
# {{lb|tl|dialectal}} {{n-g|used to form contemplative aspects of verbs prefixed with {{m|tl|um-}} or infixed with {{m|tl|-um-}}}}

====Derived terms====
{{prefixsee|tl}}

-------- end text --------
