===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|mabig-at||now|dialectal|Southern Tagalog}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|tl|poz-pro|*(ma-)bəʀəqat}}, or analyzed as {{af|tl|ma-|bigat}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|mabigát}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|mabigát|pl=mabibigat|b=+}}

# [[heavy]] {{gl|having great weight}}
#: {{uxi|tl|Sabay-sabay nilang itinulak ang '''''mabigat''''' na dyip nang 'di na ito makatakbo.
|They pushed the '''heavy''' jeepney together when it could no longer start up.}}
#: {{uxi|tl|'''Mabigat''' ang krisis ng gutom sa mahihirap na sektor ng bansa.
|The hunger crisis is heavy onto the poorest sectors of the country}}
#: {{uxi|tl|'''Mabigat''' ang porsiyento ng mga exam sa klaseng ito kumpara sa mga proyekto.
|The percentage of the exam has more weight as against the projects.}}
# [[deep]]; [[profound]]; [[weighty]]
#: {{ux|tl|Nasasabaw ako sa '''mabibigat''' na mga teoriya ni Marx.
|I can't understand fully Marx's '''profound''' theories.}}
# [[serious]]; [[critical]]; [[grave]]; [[grievous]]
#: {{syn|tl|malubha|malala}}
# [[formidable]]; [[hard]] to [[accomplish]] or [[tackle]]

====Inflection====
{{tl-infl-adj|b|i|gat|partial}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|mabigat ang paa|mabigat ang salapi|mabigat panimbangan}}
