Page 11232 mag-: Skipped, no changes
Page 11232 mag-: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|tl|map-pro|*maʀ-}}, likely a portmanteau of the original actor trigger affix {{m|poz-pro|*-um-}} (inherited as Tagalog {{m|tl|-um-}}) and {{m|poz-pro|*paʀ-}} (Tagalog {{m|tl|pag-}}), as is the case in other actor trigger affixes ({{m|tl|mang}} from ''pang-'' + ''-um-'', and {{m|tl|ma-}} from ''pa-/ka-'' + ''-um-'').

===Prefix===
{{tl-head|prefix|b=+}}

# {{n-g|actor trigger verb prefix, used to express:}}
## {{n-g|an action}}
##: {{uxi|tl|'''Maglu'''luto ako ng pagkain.|I will cook food.}}
## {{n-g|the taking up of an occupation}}
##: {{uxi|tl|Nagplanong '''mag'''doktor si Mary noong 1987.|Mary planned to become a doctor in 1987.}}
## {{n-g|the use or wearing of something}}
##: {{uxi|tl|Hindi siya marunong '''mag'''-Ingles.|He doesn't know how to speak (use) English.}}
##: {{uxi|tl|'''Mag'''-amerikana ka at malamig sa labas.|Wear a coat because it's cold outside.}}
## {{n-g|a reciprocal action (for some verbs)}}
##: {{uxi|tl|'''Mag'''-usap muna tayo.|Let's talk to each other first.}}
## {{q|with CV reduplication}}: {{n-g|an action that will be done repeatedly, continually, or intensely}}
##: {{uxi|tl|'''Magsisi'''sigaw ang mga bata kapag ginawa mo iyan.|The children would be screaming so much once you do that.}}
## {{q|with root word reduplication}}: {{n-g|a reciprocal action involving three or more doers}}
##: {{uxi|tl|'''Magkikita'''-kita tayo sa susunod na linggo.|We will see one another next week.}}
## {{q|with root word reduplication}}: {{n-g|an action to be done occasionally, at random, a little, a bit, now and then, or here and there}}
##: {{uxi|tl|'''Maglakad'''-lakad si Pedro sa mall.|Pedro will walk a bit in the mall.}}
# {{n-g|verb prefix with no trigger/focus used to express being, occurrence, or existence}}
#: {{uxi|tl|'''Magpa'''-Pasko na bukas!|It will be Christmas tomorrow!}}
#: {{uxi|tl|'''Magha'''hating-gabi na.|It is almost midnight.}}
# {{n-g|noun prefix used to indicate:}}
## {{n-g|relationship between two persons}}
##: {{prefex|tl|ama|mag-ama|t1=father|t2=father and child}}
##: {{prefex|tl|asawa|mag-asawa|t1=spouse|t2=married couple}}
## {{q|with CV reduplication}}: {{n-g|relationship among three or more persons}}
##: {{prefex|tl|mag-|!CV-|ina|mag-iina|t3=mother|t4=mother and children}}
##: {{prefex|tl|mag-|!CV-|kapatid|magkakapatid|t3=sibling|t4=brothers and sisters, siblings}}
## {{q|with CV reduplication}}: {{n-g|occupation}}
##: {{prefex|tl|mag-|!CV-|saka|magsasaka|t3=farming|t4=farmer}}
##: {{prefex|tl|mag-|!CV-|nakaw|magnanakaw|t3=something stolen|t4=thief, robber}}

====Usage notes====
* If the root word begins with a vowel or the root word is a proper noun, insert a hyphen after the prefix.
:* {{prefixusex|tl|aral|mag-aral}}
:* {{prefixusex|tl|Pasko|mag-Pasko}}
* Also see usage notes at {{m|tl|-um-}}.

====Derived terms====
{{prefixsee|tl}}

====Related terms====
{{col-auto|tl|mag- -an|magka-|magkanda-|magkang-|magma-|magpa-|magpaka-|magpa-|magsi-|magsipag-|um-|-um-|nag-|pag-}}
-------- end text --------
