Page 11472 maging: Already saw {{tl-pr}}, skipping: {{tl-pr|magíng<a:Standard Tagalog>|+<a:Quezon,alternative>}}
Page 11472 maging: Skipped, no changes
Page 11472 maging: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|maguing|maguin||obsolete|Abecedario orthography}}
* {{alt|tl|magin||rare}}

===Etymology===
Possibly from obsolete root {{m|phi-pro|*ging}} (also possible to be {{m|phi-pro|*gi}}/{{m|phi-pro|*giq}}/{{m|phi-pro|*gin}} + {{m|tl|-ng}} suffix).<ref>{{cite-journal|title=Tagalog Monosyllabic Roots|work=Oceanic Linguistics|page=345–374|year=1995|url=https://www.jstor.org/stable/3623048|volume=34|issue=2|issn=0029-8115|doi=10.2307/3623048|last=Potet|first=Jean-Paul G.}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|magíng<a:Standard Tagalog>|+<a:Quezon,alternative>}}

===Verb===
{{tl-verb|magíng|naging|nagiging|magiging|b=+}}

# to [[become]]
#: {{ux|tl|'''Naging''' asul ang langit.|The sky '''became''' blue.}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''Magiging''' maganda siya.|He will '''become''' beautiful.}}
# to [[be]]
#: {{ux|tl|Mahirap '''maging''' bulag.|It's hard '''to be''' blind.}}

====Usage notes====
* Enclitics follow the word or phrase (e.g. names, dates, addresses, times of day) after maging and its inflected form.

====Related terms====
{{rel3|tl|paging|paging-|pagiging-|ma-}}

