Page 11513 magkumahog: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{prefix|tl|mag|kumahog}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|magkumahóg}}

===Verb===
{{tl-verb|magkumahóg|nagkumahog|nagkukumahog|magkukumahog|type=actor II|b=+}}

# to [[hurry]] to [[finish]] something; to [[rush]]
#* {{quote-text|tl|year=1988|title=National Mid-week
|passage=Dahil isang buwan nang sira ang lumang TV kaya&#39;t hindi na  magawa ang kinaugaliang panonood ng balita kung gabi, at dahil kung umaga&#39; y '''nagkukumahog''' sa pagpasok sa eskuwela bukod pa sa silid-aklatan naman nakikibasa ng diyaryo, sa eskuwela na lang nabalitaan ni Agnes ang nangyari sa Mendiola noong hapon.
|translation=Since their old TV has been damaged a month ago, she can no longer watch news every night as it used to be, and because she rushes to school every morning and to the library where she can read a newspaper with somebody, Agnes only knew what happened in Mendiola that afternoon at school.}}
#* {{quote-text|tl|year=2000|author=Bienvenido Lumbera|title=Pag-akda Ng Bansa
|passage=Sa pelikula ni Emmanuel A. Reyes, may isang estudyante na ang mga magulang ay nasa U.S. '''Nagkukumahog''' siyang makatapos para makarating siya sa lupaing kinaroroonan ng kanyang mga magulang.
|translation=In a movie by Emmanuel A. Reyes, there is a student whose parents are in the U.S. He is rushing to graduate to reach the lands where his parents went to.}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=2014|author=Marlene Legaspi-Munar|title=How to Keep Your Hubby Happy: at iba pang Tips para kay Misis|publisher=OMF Literature|isbn=9789710092956
|passage=Kaya ang kawawang dalaga, '''nagkukumahog''' na makapagasawa. Nang ligawan siya, tumibok agad ang puso niya, hindi na nagdalawang isip nang yayaing pakasalan ng boyfriend.
|t=So the poor girl is rushing to have a wife. When someone courted her, her heart suddenly beat, that she didn't hesitate to propose a marriage for her boyfriend.}}

====Inflection====
{{tl-infl-mag|k|u|mahog}}
-------- end text --------
