Page 11883 maka-: Would save with comment = convert {{tl-IPA}} to {{tl-pr}}; remove {{hyph}} same as respelling auto-syllabification
Page 11883 maka-: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Prefix===
{{tl-head|prefix|maká-|b=+}}

# '''Actor trigger''' refers to things that have been done [[unintentionally]]
#: {{prefex|tl|maka-|basag|t2=to break|makabasag|t3=break something unintentionally}}
#: {{uxi|tl|'''Naka'''basag ang anak ko sa mall.|My son broke something in the mall '''(unintentionally)'''.}}
# '''Object trigger''' when paired with {{m|tl|kailangan||necessary}}, it usually refers to actions that have to be done or performed
#: {{uxi|tl|Kailangan mong '''maka'''tapos ng pag-aaral.|You '''have to''' finish your studies.}}
# '''Actor trigger''' refers to things that happen by chance
#: {{prefex|tl|maka-|kita|t2=see|makakita|t3=to happen to see something}}
#: {{uxi|tl|'''Naka'''kita ako ng artista nung nasa mall ako.|I '''happened to''' see an actor while I was in the mall.}}
# being in favor of or being inclined towards something
#: {{uxi|tl|Bakit ka '''maka'''-Amerika?|Why are you '''in favor of''' America?}}

====Derived terms====
{{prefixsee|tl}}

====See also====
