#* {{quote-text|tl|year=1969|title=Katas
|passage=Kinailangan niya ang mas malaking allowance para siya makalimot. Kung kaunti lamang, talagang nangungulila siya. (Pagkatapos ni Herbie, sumunod na dumating sa buhay ni Hazel si Ed...)<br>She needs more allowance so she can forget. If few, she'll long for someone. (After Herbie, Ed soon came to Hazel's life...)}}
#* {{quote-text|tl|year=1997|author=Jaime L. An Lim; Christine Godinez-Ortega|title=Worsmiths & Archipelagoes: The Third Iligan National Writers Workshop and Literature Teachers Conference
|passage=Andres : Kay dali ninyong makalimot sa kasaysayan. kay dali ninyong makalimot sa dakilang plebeyo, sa sigaw ng Balintawak, sa ama ng Katipunan, kay- Lahat :  ANDRES BONIFACIO? Katahimikan.
|translation=Andres : You easily forget history. You easily forget the great plebeian, the cry of Balintawak, the father of the Katipunan, and ALL: ANDRES BONIFACIO? Silence.}}

