Page 11910 makan: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|macan||obsolete|Abecedario orthography}}

===Etymology===
{{bor+|tl|es|macan|t=bruised}}, an [[inflection]] of {{m|es|macar|t=to bruise}}, although according to Manuel (1948), it is supposedly from {{m|tl|Macao}}, due to Noceda & Sanlucar (1860) defining it as ''"Arroz de tubigan, bueno y oloroso, uno es blanco y otro colorado. Vino la semilla de Macan."'' and an early account of Fr. {{w|Domingo de Salazar}} (1583) saying that they have located it at ''"la ysla de Macan, donde viven los Portugueses que estan junto a la ciudad de Cantón, en la China,..."''.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|makán}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|makán|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|botany}} a type of [[aromatic]] [[rice]] ({{taxfmt|Oryza sativa|species}}, sometimes subspecies {{taxlink|Oryza sativa indica|subspecies|O. s. indica}}) grown across the [[Philippines]] with a variety of [[white rice]] and [[red rice]], often considered as a [[second-class]] [[rice]]
# {{lb|tl|zoology}} a [[species]] of [[pig]] with a [[savory]] [[meat]] when [[cooked]]

====Related terms====
{{rel3|tl|Makaw|sinandomeng|dinorado}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:KWF Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:tl:Manuel 1948|q=Makán|page=40}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1860}}

