Page 11938 Makaw: Removing explicit syllabification same as auto-syllabification: {{hyph|tl|Ma|kaw}}
Page 11938 Makaw: Replaced {{tl-IPA|makáw}} with {{tl-pr|makáw}}
Page 11938 Makaw: Would save with comment = convert {{tl-IPA}} to {{tl-pr}}; remove {{hyph}} same as respelling auto-syllabification
Page 11938 Makaw: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=tl}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|Macao}}
* {{alt|tl|Macau}}

===Etymology===
{{bor+|tl|es|Macau}}, from {{der|tl|pt|Macau}}, from {{der|tl|yue|[[阿媽]][[港]]|t=[[Mazu]] [[harbor|Harbor]]}}.<br>
The ''"good cook"'' sense is due to historically cooks and chefs across [[Manila]] and large towns across the [[Philippines]], especially [[Luzon]] such as in [[Pampanga]] and [[Baguio]], were usually ethnic Chinese people from [[Macau]] or [[Canton]] and their descendants, as per Manuel (1948).

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|makáw}}

===Proper noun===
{{tl-proper noun|Makáw|b=+}}

# {{place|tl|city/and/special administrative region|c/China|t=Macau}}
#* {{quote-text|tl|year=1998|author=Mariano Ponce; Jaime Carlos de Veyra|title=Efemérides filipinas
|passage=Sa pagkakawalay ng Portugal sa korona ng España noong 1640 ay napasama rin ang Goa, Molukas, '''Makaw''', atbp. Ang mga iyon ay itinuturing ng mga pag-aaring Portugés, bago naisanib ang kahariang ito sa Imperyong Kastila noong 1580.}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|Makáw|b=+}}

# [[Macao]] [[Chinese]]; [[Macanese]]; [[Cantonese]] {{gl|a [[Chinese]] person from [[Macau]] or [[Canton]]}}
# {{lb|tl|by extension}} a [[good]] [[cook]]

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|lumpiyang makaw|lutong makaw}}

====Related terms====
{{rel3|tl|makan|Intsik|Fukien}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:tl:Manuel 1948|q=Makáw|page=40}}
