Page 12106 maldita: Would save with comment = convert {{tl-IPA}} to {{tl-pr}}; remove {{hyph}} same as respelling auto-syllabification
Page 12106 maldita: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{bor+|tl|es|maldita}}, from {{der|tl|la|maledicta}}, feminine of {{m|la|maledictus}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|b=+|m=maldito}}

# [[mean]]; [[cruel]]
#* '''2014''', J. Corcinto, ''Teka, Wait...Di Ako Prepared'', Arcenciel Publishing
#*: {{quote|tl|Parang lahat na lang ng sinasabi niya na tatabunan nung malalalim na paghinga niya saka paghihikbi. Na imagine ko noon sa siguro maganda yung babae. Ang '''maldita''' din kasi nung matapobreng Mamma nung babae sa radyo! Oo. Mamma!}}
# [[mischievous]]
# {{lb|tl|derogatory|of a girl}} [[spoiled]]

====Related terms====
{{rel3|tl|dikta}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+|m=maldito}}

# {{lb|tl|derogatory}} [[spoiled]] [[girl]]
#: {{syn|tl|bruha}}
#* {{quote-text|tl|year=1988|author=Ricardo Lee|title=Si tatang at mga himala ng ating panahon: koleksyon ng mga akda
|passage=&quot;Say hello to them, anak, say hello,&quot; ani Yvonne nang lumapit ang anak. &quot;Ay walang dila.&quot; Ang bata ang inspirasyon niya sa buhay. “Nang ipanganak ko &#39;to&#39;y na-meet ko si Bernal. Kaya ayan, spoiled. '''Maldita'''!"
|translation="Say hello to them", Yvonne said to her daughter. "Oh, you're shy." Her child is her inspiration. "When I gave birth to her, I met Bernal. So, she's spoiled. Spoiled brat!"}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=2007|author=Fanny A. Garcia|title=Sandaang damit: 16 na maikling kuwento|publisher=UP Press|isbn=9789715425384
|passage=Kung hapon, habang nagluluto si Inay, mangangalumbaba ako sa aming bintana&#39;t matatanaw ko si Mayet, ang '''malditang''' si Mayet, sa pag-aabang sa kanyang ama.
|t=If it's afternoon, while Mother cooks, I put my elbows on the window and I see Mayet, that spoiled brat, waiting for her father.}}
-------- end text --------
