===Etymology===
From {{compound|tl|malik|mata}}. The word {{m|tl|malik}} is an archaic apheretic form of {{m|tl|bumalik}}, from {{m|tl|balik}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|malíkmatá,malikmatà}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|malíkmatá|head2=malikmatà|b=+}}

# someone or something [[perceived]] to be someone or something but on the contrary; someone or something [[mistaken]] for someone or something
#: {{syn|tl|transpigurasyon}}
# [[phantasm]]; [[illusion]]; [[visual]] [[deception]]
#: {{syn|tl|kini-kinita|ilusyon|pantasmagorya}}
# anything that has [[properties]] to [[morph]] or [[change]] [[form]]
#: {{syn|tl|transpigurasyon}}
# an [[amulet]] that gives [[invisibility]]
#: {{syn|tl|tagabulag|tagibulag}}
# [[sleight of hand]]
#: {{syn|tl|salamangka}}
# {{lb|tl|obsolete}} act of [[concealment]] or [[disguise|disgusing]] oneself {{defdate|16th|17th c.}}

