Page 12204 maluto: Skipped, no changes
Page 12204 maluto: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|maloto||obsolete|Abecedario}}

===Etymology===
From {{prefix|tl|ma|luto||t2=cook}}. Compare {{cog|pam|malutu||red}} and {{cog|mrw|maloto'||dark in color}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|malutô<a^cooked>|malutò<v^to be cooked><n^food brought when traveling><a^fine, well-dyed {{q|of color}}>}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|malutô|b=+}}

# [[cooked]]

===Verb===
{{tl-verb|malutò|naluto|naluluto|maluluto|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|intransitive}} to be [[cooked]]

====Conjugation====
{{tl-conj|ma|l|u|to|l|u|tu|o=ipa|d=an|a=none|rpl-loc-ka-an=yes}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|malutò|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|dialectal|Rizal|Laguna|Quezon}} [[food]] brought when [[travel]]ling
#: {{syn|tl|baon|binalot|q2=Batangas, Laguna, Quezon|bugong|q3=Cavite, Batangas}}
# {{lb|tl|obsolete}} [[rice]] brought when [[travel]]ling
#: {{syn|tl|kanin|sinaing|morisketa}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|magmaluto}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|malutò|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|obsolete}} [[fine]]; [[well]]-[[dye]]d {{q|of color}}
#: {{ux|tl|Hindi '''maluto''' ang pagkapula nitong suga.|The coloration of this incarnadine is not '''fine'''.}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1860}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1613}}
** page 320: “Finacoſa) Loto (pp) de color bien teñida, maloto, ad) color fina y bien teñida”
** page 432: “Moriſqueta) Maloto (pp) o arroz guiſado”
-------- end text --------
