Page 12253 mamaya: Already saw {{tl-pr}}, skipping: {{tl-pr|mamayâ,mámaya7}}
Page 12253 mamaya: Skipped, no changes
Page 12253 mamaya: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|mimiya||Cavite}}

===Etymology===
Possibly from the following:
* Initial {{rdp|tl|nocap=1}} of obsolescent root {{m|tl|maya||after a short period}}.
* From {{prefix|tl|mam|baya|t2=toleration}}, according to Panganiban (1972). 
* From {{der|tl|sa|समय}} with the first syllable mistaken as the {{m|tl|sa-}} prefix, then {{rdp|tl|nocap=1}} into {{m|tl|maya-maya}}, then inflected as {{m|tl|mamaya-maya}}, then underwent {{clipping|tl|nocap=1}}, according to Pardo de Tavera (1887). Compare {{cog|jv|ꦱꦼꦩꦪ|t=to postpone; to delay}}, {{cog|kaw|samaya}}, {{cog|id|semaya}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|mamayâ,mámaya7}}

===Adverb===
{{tl-adv|mamayâ|head2=mámayâ|b=+}}

# [[later]]; [[shortly]]
#: {{ux|tl|Gagawin niya ito '''mamaya'''.|''S/he'll do it '''later'''.''}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''Mamaya''' pa magsisimula ang programa.|''The program will start '''shortly'''.''}}

====Related terms====
{{rel3|tl|maya-maya|mamaya-maya|maya't maya|magmamaya-maya|pamaya-maya|ipagpamaya-maya|ipagpamaya't maya}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:Diksyunaryo tesauro Pilipino-Ingles 1973|page=689}}
* {{R:Diccionario tagálog-hispano|827}}
* {{R:Diccionario hispano-tagalog|208}}
* {{cite-book|es|author=Trinidad Hermenegildo Pardo de Tavera|title=El sanscrito en la lengua tagalog|year=1887|publisher=Imprimerie de la Faculté de Médecine, A. Davy|location=Paris|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=JYdBAAAAYAAJ&newbks=0|page=37}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1860}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1613}}

