===Etymology===
{{bor+|tl|es|mahón||[[nankeen]], especially the [[blue]] [[cloth]]; [[jeans]]}}, named after {{m|es|Mahón}}, capital city of [[Minorca]], [[Balearic Islands]], where in the 18th century English ships transshipped cargo destined for Spanish ports in the Levant. The city name is then from {{der|tl|la|[[portus|Portus]] [[Magōnis]]}}, from {{m|la|Magō}}, from {{der|tl|xpu|𐤌𐤂‬𐤍}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|ma7óng}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|maóng|b=+}}

# [[denim]] [[cloth]]; [[jean]]

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:tl:Hispanismos 1972|page=379|q=maong}}

{{C|tl|Fabrics}}
