Page 12656 Mapulon: Would save with comment = convert {{tl-IPA}} to {{tl-pr}}; remove {{hyph}} same as respelling auto-syllabification
Page 12656 Mapulon: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|Apolon|Apulon}}
* {{alt|tl|Mapolon|Mapolong||archaic|Abecedario orthography}}
* {{alt|tl|Mapulong}}

===Etymology===
{{unc|tl}}. Possibilities are:
* From {{m|tl|ma-}} + {{m|tl|pulong||meeting}}, because the seven animals of the constellation seem to meet together
* From ''Mapulon'', god of seasons in Tagalog mythology.
* Possibly from or related to {{der|tl|ivv|mapolon}}, an authority in the barangays of [[Batanes]] during the pre-historic period. The souls of the social upper class after death were said to enter the heavens and become stars.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Proper noun===
{{tl-proper noun|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|astronomy}} the [[star cluster]] [[Pleiades]], reckoned as a [[constellation]] of [[seven]] [[goats]]
#: {{syn|tl|Pulon-Pulon|Supot ni Hudas|Rosaryo}}

===References===
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1860}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1613|130|Cabrillas) Mapolon ([pp]) ſiete eſtrellas [en el] çielo, metaf) de polon que es jũta por q̃ andan juntas.}}
* {{R:Diccionario tagálog-hispano|48|'''Apulon.''' astron. Cabrillas. f. pl.}}
* {{cite-journal|author=Dante L. Ambrosio|title=BALATIK: Katutubong Bituin ng mga Pilipino|work=Philippine Social Sciences Review|year=2005|url=https://journals.upd.edu.ph/index.php/pssr/article/view/1287|volume=57|issue=1}}
