* {{alt|tl|madhuya|marhuya||chiefly|Laguna|Quezon}}
* {{alt|tl|maduya}}
* {{alt|tl|marahuya||chiefly|Batangas}}

===Etymology===
From earlier {{m|tl|madhuya}} / {{m|tl|marhuya}}, from an unknown source. Possible etymologies include:
* From {{der|tl|sa|माधुर्य||sweetness}}, from {{af|sa|मधुर|t1=sweet|-य<id:-ness>|nocat=1}}, according to Pardo de Tavera (1887). See also {{ncog|ms|madu}}.
* From {{der|tl|es-MX|alt=*marjuya}}, according to Panganiban (1973).

Compare {{cog|pam|baruya}}, {{cog|bcl|baduya}}, and {{cog|ceb|maruya}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|maruyà}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|maruyà|b=+}}

# {{w|banana fritter}}
#: {{syn|tl|pinaypay}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|pagmaruyaan|magmamaruya|magmaruya|pagmaruyain}}

====See also====
{{col3|tl|torta|kumbo|saging|turon}}

