Page 13262 Mindoro: Would save with comment = convert {{tl-IPA}} to {{tl-pr}}; remove {{hyph}} same as respelling auto-syllabification
Page 13262 Mindoro: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Usually attributed by folk etymologies to {{ncog|es|[[mina de oro]]||[[gold mine]]}}. However, there is little evidence of gold mining activities on the island. Furthermore, old Tagalog documents name the island ''Minolo''. ''Minolo'' may be related to ''minuro'', an old Visayan term meaning "place of abundance", from ''duro'', "abundance".

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Proper noun===
{{tl-proper noun|b=+}}

# {{place|tl|island|c/Philippines|t=Mindoro}}
# {{lb|tl|historical}} {{place|tl|province|c/Philippines|modern=[[Occidental Mindoro]] and [[Oriental Mindoro]]|t=Mindoro}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|Occidental Mindoro|Oriental Mindoro|Kanlurang Mindoro|Silangang Mindoro}}

====Related terms====
{{rel3|tl|Mindoreño|Mindoreña}}
