Page 13460 mulat: Would save with comment = convert {{tl-IPA}} to {{tl-pr}}; remove {{hyph}} same as respelling auto-syllabification
Page 13460 mulat: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
From Proto-Central Philippine ''*muklat'' ({{m-g|to open eyes}}). Compare {{cog|ilo|buragat||eyes opened wide}} / {{m|ilo|mulagat||wide-eyed}}, {{cog|pam|mulikat||open one's eyes}}, {{cog|pam|mulat||open the eyes}}, {{cog|bno|mukyat||to open eyes}}, {{cog|msb|muklat||open the eyes}}, {{cog|bcl|buklat||opening one's eyes}}, {{cog|akl|mukeat||to realize}}, {{cog|ceb|buklat||for the eyes to open}}, {{cog|hil|muklat||to open the eyes}}, {{cog|mrw|borarat||open eyes wide}}, {{cog|tsg|bulat||eyes open}}, and {{cog|jv|ꦩꦸꦭꦠ꧀||to look at; to see}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|+<n^>|mulát<a^>}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# act of [[open]]ing the [[eye]]s
#: {{syn|tl|dilat|hilat|q2=obsolete}}
# {{lb|tl|figuratively}} act of [[enlighten]]ing or [[educate|educating]] someone
#: {{syn|tl|pagturo}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|imulat|ipagmulat|ipagmulatan|ipamulat|magpamulat|pagmulatan|mamulat|pamulatan|pagmulat|kinamulatan|pagmumulat|mapamulat|mulatan|pamulatin}}

=====See also=====
{{col3|tl|mulagat|pukaw|bisaklat|buklat}}

====Adjective====
{{tl-adj|mulát|b=+}}

# [[open]] {{q|of the eyes}}
#: {{syn|tl|dilat|dulak|q2=obsolete}}
# {{lb|tl|figurative}} [[enlightened]]; [[educated]]; [[trained]]; [[conscious]]; [[awakened]]
#: {{syn|tl|sanay|gising|pinalaki|tinuruan|sanay|pinasuso}}

===Etymology 2===

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|obsolete}}

# act of [[own]]ing something to be one's [[property]]
#: {{syn|tl|ari|sarili|angkin}}
#: {{ux|tl|Aking '''mumulat-mulat''', at kinuha mo.|'''Something of''' my '''own''', and you took it.}}

=====Alternative forms=====
* {{alt|tl|molat||obsolete|Abecedario}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:KWF Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1860}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1613|8|Abrir) Mulat (pp) los ojos mucho, o abrillos el q̃ los tiene cerrados adrede}}
-------- end text --------
