Page 13548 na: Already saw {{tl-pr}}, skipping: {{tl-pr}}
Page 13548 na: Skipped, no changes
Page 13548 na: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Etymology 1===
Influenced by Baybayin character {{m|tl|{{tl-bay sc}}}}.

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# {{tl-letter name|N|n|alph=abak}}
#: {{syn|tl|en|q1=in the Filipino alphabet|ene|q2=in the Abecedario}}

=====See also=====
* {{l|tl|nana}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|tl|phi-pro|*na||now; already}}. Compare {{cog|bcl|na}}, {{cog|ceb|na}}, {{cog|hil|na}}, and {{cog|tsg|na}}.

====Adverb====
{{tl-adv|b=+}}

# [[already]]; [[now]]; [[anymore]] ({{n-g|expresses the [[event]] when following a [[verb]]}})
#: {{ux|tl|Tapos '''na'''.|Finished '''already'''.}}
#: {{ux|tl|Yari '''na''' tayo.|We've '''now been''' made.}}
# [[already]]; [[now]] ({{n-g|declares the [[event]] of [[action]] when following a [[verb]] in the [[past]] [[tense]]}})
#: {{ux|tl|Natulog '''na'''.|Slept '''already'''.}}
#: {{ux|tl|Bumili '''na'''.|Bought '''already'''.}}
# [[already]]; [[now]] ({{n-g|suggests [[immediate]] or [[quick]] [[action]] when following the [[infinitive]] form and [[future]] [[tense]] of the [[verb]]}})
#: {{ux|tl|Pumasok '''na''' tayo.|Let's go in '''already'''.}}
#: {{ux|tl|Ipinabibili ko '''na''' ang gamot.|I'm having someone buy the medicine '''now'''.}}

====Adjective====
{{tl-adj|b=+}}

# [[already]]; [[now]] ({{n-g|expresses the [[event]] when following a [[noun]]}})
#: {{ux|tl|Bagsak '''na'''.|Failure '''already'''.}}
#: {{ux|tl|Abogado '''na''' siya.|He/She is '''now''' a lawyer.}}
# [[now]]; [[already]] ({{n-g|expresses a [[shift]] or [[change]] in the [[performance]] of a [[task]] when following a [[personal pronoun]]}})
#: {{ux|tl|Ako '''na'''.|lit=Me '''now'''.|My '''turn'''.}}
#: {{ux|tl|Ikaw '''na'''.|lit=You '''now'''.|Your '''turn'''.}}
#: {{ux|tl|Siya '''na'''.|lit=Him/her '''now'''.|His/her '''turn'''.}}

=====See also=====
* {{l|tl|na-}}

===Etymology 3===
From {{inh|tl|map-pro|*na||linker marking emphatic attribution}}.

====Ligature====
{{tl-head|ligature|b=+}}

# {{n-g|Connects words, phrases, and sentences}}: [[which]] is; [[that]] is; [[who]] is
## {{n-g|Connects [[adjective]]s to [[noun]]s.}}
##: {{ux|tl|May matinis '''na''' boses siya.|He/she has a piercing voice.}}
##: {{ux|tl|Mahilig ako sa mga matatangkad na lalaki|I like tall boys.}}
## {{n-g|Connects [[adverb]]s to [[verb]]s.}}
##: {{ux|tl|Siya ay mabilis '''na''' tumakbo.|He/she ran fast.}}
##: {{ux|tl|Malugod ka nami'''ng''' tinatanggap.|We welcome you.}}
## {{n-g|Connects clauses}}: [[that]]; [[to]]
##: {{ux|tl|Masaya ka lang '''na''' meron kang pera.|You're only happy '''that''' you have money.}}
##: {{ux|tl|Maganda'''ng''' ipanggawa ng saranggola.|Good '''to''' use to make a kite.}}
## {{n-g|Connects [[quantifier]]s}} {{q|{{m|tl|mayroon}} and {{m|tl|wala}} only uses {{m|tl|-ng}}}}
##: {{ux|inline=1|tl|Tana'''ng''' Pilipino|Every Filipino.}}
##: {{ux|tl|Mayroon ka'''ng''' kanin sa pisngi mo|You have rice on your cheeks.}}
##: {{ux|inline=1|tl|Apat '''na''' palo.|Four sticks.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* ''na'' becomes the {{m|tl|-ng}} [[suffix]] if the preceding word ends in a [[vowel]].
*: {{ux|tl|Maganda'''ng''' bulaklak|Pretty flower}}
*: {{ux|tl|Bigla siya'''ng''' nagsalita.|He/She suddenly spoke.}}

* Words ending in -n will become -ng ({{m|tl|-g}})
*: {{ux|tl|Dayuhan'''g''' turista|Foreign tourist}}
*: {{ux|tl|Siya ay dahan-dahan'''g''' pumunta doon.|He/She carefully went there.}}

* It becomes the {{m|tl|-ng-}} [[interfix]] in [[compound word]]s, if the preceding [[stem]] ends in a [[vowel]].
*: {{affixusex|tl|haba|-ng-|buhay|[[habang-buhay|haba'''ng-'''buhay]]}}
*: {{affixusex|tl|bunga|-ng-|kahoy|[[bungangkahoy|bunga'''ng'''kahoy]]}}

* It becomes the {{m|tl|-m-}} [[interfix]] in [[compound word]]s, where the next [[stem]] starts with a ([[b]]) or ([[p]]).
*: {{affixusex|tl|haba|-m-|buhay|[[habambuhay|haba'''m'''buhay]]}}
*: {{affixusex|tl|ganti|-m-|pala|[[gantimpala|ganti'''m'''pala]]}}

* It becomes the {{m|tl|-n-}} [[interfix]] in [[compound word]]s, where the next [[stem]] starts with a ([[d]]), ([[s]]), or ([[t]]).
*: {{affixusex|tl|isa|-n-|daan|[[sandaan|sa'''n'''daan]]}}
*: {{affixusex|tl|bago|-n-|sakop|-in|[[bagunsakupin|bagu'''n'''sakupin]]}}
*: {{affixusex|tl|libo|-n-|taon|[[libuntaon|libu'''n'''taon]]}}

* Words ending with -n inside compounds ending will become -ng- ({{m|tl|-g-}})
*: {{affixusex|tl|daan|-g-|bakal|[[daang-bakal|daan'''g-'''bakal]]}}
*: {{affixusex|tl|kababaan|-g-|loob|[[kababaang-loob|kababaan'''g-'''loob]]}}
*: {{affixusex|tl|kabungguan|-g-|balikat|[[kabungguang-balikat|kabungguan'''g-'''balikat]]}}

=====See also=====
* {{l|tl|nang}}
* {{l|tl|ng}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}

