Page 13550 na-: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|na-<qq:complete aspect prefix>|ná-<qq:progressive aspect prefix>}}

===Prefix===
{{tl-head|prefix|b=+}}

# {{ngd|used to form complete aspects of verbs prefixed with {{m|tl|ma-}}}}

===Prefix===
{{tl-head|prefix|ná-|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|dialectal}} {{ngd|used to form progressive aspects of verbs prefixed with {{m|tl|um-}} or infixed with {{m|tl|-um-}}}}

====Usage notes====
* The dialectal prefix, when written, is generally a source of confusion and mockery for the majority of Tagalog speakers, but the two actually differ by pronunciation. The ''na-'', where it indicates a perfective aspect, is pronounced without stress, while the ''na-'' prefix, where it indicates a progressive aspect in some dialects, is pronounced with stress.
*: {{ux|tl|'''Na'''kain siya ng isda.|He/She was happened to be eaten by the fish.}}
*: {{ux|tl|'''Ná'''kain siya ng isda.|He/She is eating fish.}}

====Derived terms====
{{prefixsee|tl}}

