Page 13767 -nin: Replaced {{tl-IPA}} with {{tl-pr}}
Page 13767 -nin: Would save with comment = convert {{tl-IPA}} to {{tl-pr}}
Page 13767 -nin: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Suffix===
{{tl-verb|b=+|addlpos=adjective,noun}}

# {{alt form|tl|-in|nodot=1}}
#: {{suffixusex|tl|talo|t1=defeat|talunin|t2={{lb|tl|transitive}} to defeat}}
#: {{suffixusex|tl|kuha|t1=take|kunin|t2={{lb|tl|transitive}} to get}}

====Usage notes====
* Normally, {{IPAchar|/h/}} is inserted before -in when the root word ends with a vowel that is not followed by a glottal stop. In some cases, phoneme change can occur and {{IPAchar|/h/}} becomes {{IPAchar|/n/}}.
*: {{suffixusex|tl|sabi|altsuf=-'''h'''in|sabihin}}
*: {{suffixusex|tl|talo|altsuf=-'''n'''in|talunin}}

* Sometimes, the final vowel of the root word disappears when the suffix is added.
*: {{suffixusex|tl|kuha|kunin}}

====Derived terms====
{{suffixsee|tl}}
-------- end text --------
Page 13768 nina: Removing explicit syllabification same as auto-syllabification: {{hyph|tl|ni|na}}
Page 13768 nina: Replaced {{tl-IPA|niná}} with {{tl-pr|niná}}
Page 13768 nina: Would save with comment = convert {{tl-IPA}} to {{tl-pr}}; remove {{hyph}} same as respelling auto-syllabification
Page 13768 nina: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|niná}}

===Article===
{{tl-head|article|niná|b=+}}

# {{n-g|possessive particle, used only with personal names}}
#: {{syn|tl|nila|q1=colloquial}}
#: {{uxi|tl|mga [[bisikleta]] '''nina''' Juan at Juana|Juan and Juana's bicycles}}
# {{n-g|ergative marker used with personal names, equivalent of {{m|tl|ng}} {{m|tl|mga}} used with common nouns.}}

====Usage notes====
* This is used where there is more than one addressee, as a simpler way of saying ''ni'' [1st referrent] … ''at ni'' [last referrent] (e.g. ''nina Pedro at Juan'').
* Where it precedes one name, this refers to the person and others surrounding them (e.g. ''nina Pedro'' refers to Pedro and anyone other around him, usually unspecified).

===See also===
{{tl-markers}}

