===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|dingas-kugon}}
* {{alt|tl|lingas-kugon}}
* {{alt|tl|ningas kugon}}

===Etymology===
From {{compound|tl|ningas|t1=[[ignition]]|kugon|t2=[[cogon grass]]|lit=burns like cogon}}. Dried [[cogon grass]] is [[highly]] [[flammable]] & [[ignite]]s easily, but likewise, [[burns out]] quickly or does not last long.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|+,ningas-kugón}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|[[ningas]]-[[kugon]]|head2=[[ningas]]-[[kugón]]|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|idiom}} [[fleetingly]] [[enthusiastic]]; [[hardworking]], [[nice]], or [[great]] at [[first]], but eventually, no longer continues what was started

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|[[ningas]]-[[kugon]]|head2=[[ningas]]-[[kugón]]|b=+}}

# [[ephemeral]] [[enthusiasm]]
# [[activity]] or [[project]] that doesn't last

====Usage notes====
* This describes how an initially fiery excitement over a new endeavor loses steam very quickly.

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}

{{cln|tl|compound nouns}}
