Page 13872 -ng: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Etymology 1===

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|tl|-g||for roots ending in ([[n]])}}
* {{alt|tl|-ng-||for [[compound]]s with preceding [[stem]] ending in a [[vowel]].}}
* {{alt|tl|-m-||for [[compound]]s with initial [[stem]] ending in [[vowel]]s, but the next [[stem]] starts with ([[b]]) or ([[p]]).}}
* {{alt|tl|-n-||for [[compound]]s with preceding [[stem]] ending in a [[vowel]], but next [[stem]] starts with the letter ([[d]]), ([[s]]), or ([[t]]).}}
* {{alt|tl|-g-||for [[compound]]s with preceding [[stem]] ending with letter ([[n]]).}}

====Ligature====
<!-- "-ng", "-g", and "na" (those three exclusively) is a separate part of speech entirely, called "pang-angkop" (ligature). -->
{{tl-head|ligature|b=+|nosuffix=1}}

# {{n-g|[[enclitic|Enclitic]] [[suffix]], connecting [[adjective]]s to [[noun]]s and vice versa, after words ending in [[vowel]]s, except [[compound word]]s where the next [[stem]] starts with the letter ([[b]]) or ([[p]]).}}
#: {{syn|tl|na|-g|-ng-|-m-|-n-|-g-}}
#: {{ux|tl|Maganda'''ng''' bulaklak|Pretty flower}}
# {{n-g|[[enclitic|Enclitic]] [[suffix]], connecting [[adverb]]s to [[verb]]s and vice versa, after words ending in [[vowel]]s, except [[compound word]]s where the next [[stem]] starts with the letter ([[b]]) or ([[p]]).}}
#: {{syn|tl|na|-g}}
#: {{ux|tl|Bigla siya'''ng''' nagsalita.|S/he suddenly spoke.}}

===Etymology 2===
Possibly from {{der|tl|es|-ín}}. See {{m|tl|-ing}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|tl|-ing||for roots ending in consonants}}

====Suffix====
{{tl-proper noun|b=+}}

# {{n-g|[[diminutive|Diminutive]] [[suffix]], used to form [[diminutive]]s of [[given name]]s ending in [[vowel]]s, often one already shortened or with a diminutive suffix.}}
#: {{uxi|tl|Pepe'''ng'''|little Joseph}}
#: {{uxi|tl|Is'''ang'''|little Isabel}}

===Derived terms===
