===Etymology 1===
{{bor+|tl|es|o}}. Each pronunciation has a different source:
* Filipino alphabet pronunciation is influenced by {{der|tl|en|o}}.
* Abakada alphabet pronunciation is influenced by the [[Baybayin]] character {{m|tl|ᜂ}}.
* Abecedario pronunciation is from {{der|tl|es|o}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr
|ó<qq:letter name>
|ów<qq:letter name, Filipino alphabet alternative>
|-ó<qq:phoneme, stressed or unstressed>
|syll=o
}}

====Letter====
{{tl-letter|b=o}}

# {{tl-letter-def|17|o|alph=fil}}
# {{tl-letter-def|13|o|alph=abak}}
# {{lb|tl|historical}} {{tl-letter-def|18|o|alph=abec}}

=====See also=====
* {{list:Latin script letters/tl/simple}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# {{tl-letter name|O|o|alph=fil}}
# {{tl-letter name|O|o|alph=abak}}
# {{lb|tl|historical}} {{tl-letter name|O|o|alph=abec}}

=====Alternative forms=====
* {{alt|tl|ow||Filipino alphabet letter}}

=====See also=====
* {{list:Latin script letter names/tl/simple}}
* {{l|tl|uo}}

===Etymology 2===
{{bor+|tl|es|o||or}}, from {{der|tl|la|aut}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr}}

====Conjunction====
{{tl-head|conjunction|b=+}}

# [[or]]
#: {{syn|tl|o kaya|dili kaya|kung|q3=inclusive, obsolete}}
#: {{ux|tl|Sasama ka ba '''o''' dito ka lang?|Are you coming along '''or''' will you just be here?}}

=====See also=====
{{col3|tl|ni}}

===Etymology 3===
Compare {{cog|nan-hbl|乎|tr=hôⁿ / hô͘}}, {{cog|en|oh}} and {{cog|es|oh}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|tl|oh}}

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr}}

====Particle====
{{tl-head|particle|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|informal}} {{n-g|sentence-ending particle used to express warning or to catch someone's attention.}}
#: {{ux|tl|Nandiyan na naman siya '''o'''.|He's at it again, '''see?'''}}
#: {{ux|tl|Ganito kasi dapat 'yan '''o'''.|You're supposed to do it like this, '''you see?'''}}

=====See also=====
{{col3|tl|ay|oy}}

====Interjection====
{{tl-head|interjection|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|informal}}

# {{n-g|expression of surprise, wonder, amazement, or awe}}: [[oh]]!
#: {{ux|tl|Hayop naman '''oh'''!|Damn it, '''argh'''!}}
# {{n-g|used to catch someone's attention about a new topic, question, or story}}: [[so]]; [[oh]]!
# {{n-g|used to refer to something given or offered to someone}}: [[here you are]]! [[here you go]]!
#: {{syn|tl|heto}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''O''', ang regalo ko sa'yo.|'''Here''', my gift for you.}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|ows}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}

