Page 14048 onse: -------- begin text --------
{{number box|tl}}

===Etymology===
{{bor+|tl|es|once}}, from {{der|tl|osp|onze}}, {{m|osp|ondze}}, from {{der|tl|la|ūndecim}}. According to Zorc (1993), the colloquial sense is said to be related to the double line visuals of the written number 11, possibly about [[double-dealing]]. The sense can also be possibly about having a [[one up]] (an advantage) above a common arbitrary number 10. See also {{m|tl|maisahan||to be able to get one-upped}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Numeral===
{{tl-num|b=+}}

# [[eleven]]
#: {{syn|tl|labing-isa}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|onse-onse|onsehin|ikaonse}}

====Related terms====
{{rel3|tl|alas-onse|a-onse}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|colloquial}} [[cheating]]; [[duping]]; [[swindling]]; [[fooling]]
#: {{syn|tl|daya|panlalamang|gulang}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|onsehan|maonse|onsehin}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:Tagalog Slang Dictionary|103}}

{{C|tl|Eleven}}
