Page 14180 oy: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|uy}}

===Etymology===
Probably a natural expression, as may be inferred from its presence with similar meaning in many other unrelated languages: {{cog|en|hey}}, {{cog|cmn|哎|tr=āi}}, {{cog|la|eia}}, {{cog|cs|ahoj}}, and {{cog|yi|אוי||oh, oy}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Interjection===
{{tl-head|interjection|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|colloquial|informal}} {{alt form|tl|hoy}}: {{n-g|expression used to call the attention of somebody}}: [[hey]]!
#: {{ux|tl|'''Oy''', tingnan n'yo 'to!|'''Hey''', look at this!}}
# {{lb|tl|colloquial|informal}} {{alt form|tl|hoy}}: {{n-g|expression used as a warning or as a protest}}: [[hey]]!
#: {{ux|tl|'''Oy'''! 'Wag!|'''Hey'''! Don't!}}
# {{lb|tl|colloquial|informal}} {{n-g|an informal greeting}}: [[hey]]!
#: {{ux|tl|'''Oy'''! Kamusta?|'''Hey'''! How are you?}}
# {{lb|tl|colloquial|informal}} {{n-g|an expression of surprise}}: [[hey]]!
#: {{ux|tl|'''Oy'''! Bago 'to ah!|'''Hey'''! This is new!}}

-------- end text --------
