Page 14484 pagtripan: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{af|tl|trip|t1=slang: something liked|pag- -an}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|pagtripán}}

===Verb===
{{tl-verb|pagtripán|pinagtripan|pinagtitripan|pagtitripan|b=+}}  {{tlb|tl|slang}}

# to [[make fun of]]; to [[pick on]]; to [[poke fun]]
#: {{ux|tl|Sa lahat ng nakita mo sa bakuran ko, bakit pa ang mga halaman ko ang '''pinagtripan''' mo?|On everything you saw in my backyard, why would you '''poke fun''' of my plants?}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=2006|author=Victor Emmanuel Carmelo D. Nadera|title=(H)istoryador(a)|publisher=UP Press|isbn=9789715422574|page=83
|passage=May pagkakataong kasabay kong '''pinagtripan''' na sa dinig ko&#39;y isang misis ng pinaghihinalaang NPA kumander sa Quezon ang pinaglarolaro muna ng  Russian Roulette bago kinoryente ang mga utong at kinantot.
|t=There is an incident I also poked fun of that I heard that a wife of a suspected NPA commander in Quezon is forced to play Russian roulette before her nipples are electrified and she is forced to have sex.}}
#* {{quote-text|tl|year=2009|author=Alon Collective (Literary group); Vicente Garcia Groyon|title=Watershed: selected writings
|passage="'''Pinagtripan''' ka lang! Victim ka, kapatid,&quot; sagot ni Earl. Hindi nagalit si Carlos kay  Earl. Pero gustong umiyak ni Carlos dahil na-realize niyang totoo ang sinabi ni  Earl. Biktima lang talaga siya ng ego-tripping ni Zanjoe. &quot;O &#39;wag kang umiyak dito."
|translation="You're just been picked on! You're a victim, pal" Earl answered. Carlos isn't angry to Earl. But Carlos wanted to cry because he realized that what is said to Earl is true. He's just a victim of Zanjoe's ego-tripping. "Oh, don't cry here."}}

====Conjugation====
{{tl-infl-pag-an|tr|i|p|trip|locative}}
-------- end text --------
