From {{pre|tl|pa|kupya|t2=hat}}. Symbol use as diacritic is because of the similarity [[acute accent]] and a [[grave accent]] on the same vowel looks like a [[circumflex]].

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|pakupyâ}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|pakupyâ|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|orthography}}

# [[circumflex]]
#: {{syn|tl|kaputsa}}

====Usage notes====
* Used to indicate [[stress]] in the final [[syllable]] plus a [[glottal stop]] at the end in Tagalog words

