Page 14774 pamagat: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Extract from Inskripsyon sa Binatbat na Tanso ng Laguna.jpg|thumb|The [[w:Laguna Copperplate Inscription|Laguna Copperplate Inscription]], c. 900 AD]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|magat||clipping|obsolete}}
* {{alt|tl|gat||clipping|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
According to {{w|Antoon Postma|Postma}} (1991), it could be from {{der|tl|kaw|pamgat}} / {{m|kaw|pamagat}} / {{m|kaw|pamĕgĕt||a person invested with a high office or rank at court; leader; chief}} as found in the {{w|Laguna Copperplate Inscription}}, or possibly from {{cog|tl-old|-}}.<ref name="Postma"/> Alternatively, possibly conjugated through {{prefix|tl|pa|magat}} or {{prefix|tl|pam|bagat}}.<ref name="Potet"/> Compare {{cog|su|ᮕᮙᮨᮌᮨᮒ᮪||man; mister}}, {{cog|id|pameget||male; master}}, {{cog|ms|pamegat||lord; master; mister; sir}}. See also {{ncog|ms|megat}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|pamagát}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|pamagát|b=+}}

# [[title]] {{gl|[[name]] of a [[book]], [[writing]], [[paper]], [[film]], [[video]], [[musical]] [[piece]], [[painting]], [[sculpture]], or other [[work of art]]}}
#: {{syn|tl|titulo|engkabesamyento}}
#: {{ux|tl|Anong '''pamagat''' ng iyong isinulat na tula?|What is the '''title''' of your written poem?}}
# {{lb|tl|dated}} [[honorific]] [[prepend]]ed or [[post-nominal]] [[append]]ed to a person's [[name]] to signify either [[veneration]], official [[position]] or a professional or academic [[qualification]]
#: {{uxi|tl|may '''pamagat''' na Gobernador Heneral|with a '''title''' of Governor General}}
# {{lb|tl|obsolete}} [[cognomen]]; [[nickname]] <ref name="Pambansa"/><ref name="Vocabulario 1860" /><ref name="Vocabulario 1613" />
#: {{syn|tl|pamansag}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|magpamagat|pamagatan|ipamagat}}

====See also====
{{col3|tl|Gat|Magat|Gatmaitan|Gatchalian|Gatbonton|Gatdula}}

===References===
<references>
<ref name="Pambansa">{{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}</ref>
<ref name="Postma">{{cite-journal|year=1991|last=Postma|first=Antoon|title=The Laguna Copper-Plate Inscription: A Valuable Philippine Document|journal=Indo-Pacific Prehistory 1990 Assn. Bulletin 11|url=https://journals.lib.washington.edu/index.php/BIPPA/article/viewFile/11381/10020|format=PDF|volume=2|location=Mansalay, Oriental Mindoro, Philippines|publisher=Mangyan Assistance and Research Center|page=165}}.</ref>
<ref name="Potet">{{cite-book|author=Jean-Paul G. POTET|year=2016|title=Seventeenth-Century Events at Liliw|page=41|publisher=Jean-Paul G. POTET|url=https://books.google.com.ph/books?id=NiSVDAAAQBAJ&printsec=copyright&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q&f=false}}</ref>
