Page 14865 panaginip: Already saw {{tl-pr}}, skipping: {{tl-pr}}
Page 14865 panaginip: Skipped, no changes
Page 14865 panaginip: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|panaguinip||obsolete|Abecedario}}
* {{alt|tl|panag-inip||now|dialectal|Southern Tagalog}}

===Etymology===
From {{af|tl|pan-|alt2=*tag-inip}}, or analytically {{af|tl|panag-|inip}} (cf. {{m|tl|panag-araw}}, {{m|tl|panag-ulan}}), from {{inh|tl|phi-pro|*taʀa-qinəp}} (cf. {{cog|ilo| tagainep}}, {{cog|pam|tinap}}, {{cog|krj|panagin-up}}, {{cog|war|inop}} / {{m|war|unop}}, {{cog|mrw|taginep}}, {{cog|tsg|tagainup}}, {{cog|ivv|tayaynep}}), derived from {{der|tl|map-pro|*qinəp||lie down to sleep}}. Alternative etymologies include it being from the theoretical root word {{m|tl|ginip}} as attested in ''Vocabulario de lengua tagala'' (1613) and ''Vocabulario de la lengua tagala'' (1860). However, no prefix ''pana-'' exists in Tagalog.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# [[dream]] {{gl|imaginary events seen while sleeping}}
#: {{syn|tl|bungang-tulog}}

====Usage notes====
The word {{m-self|tl|panaginip}} is used for dreams that mean visions during sleep, while {{m-self|tl|pangarap}} is used on dreams that mean hopes and wishes.

====Related terms====
{{rel3|tl|managinip|mapanaginipan|panagimpan|ipanaginip}}

====See also====
{{col3|tl|idlip|inip}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1860}}

{{C|tl|Dreams|Sleep|Thinking}}
