Page 15051 pang-: Skipped, no changes
Page 15051 pang-: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|pam-||before initials /b/ and /p/, will sometimes remove initial /b/ and /p/}}
* {{alt|tl|pan-||before initials /d/, /s/, /l/ and /t/, will sometimes remove initial /d/, /s/, /l/ and /t/}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|tl|poz-pro|*paŋ-}} (cf. {{cog|ceb|pang-}}, {{cog|id|peng-}} and {{cog|ms|peng-}}).

===Prefix===
{{tl-head|prefix|b=+}}

# ({{n-g|instrumentative prefix}}) {{ngd|forms nouns indicating a tool or an instrument that is used to perform the action expressed by the root}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|tanggal|t1=remove, detach|pantanggal|t2=remover}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|takip|t1=a cover|pantakip|t2=an instrument used to cover something}}
# ({{n-g|adjectival prefix}}) {{ngd|forms relational adjectives indicating use or purpose}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|dalawa|t1=two|pandalawa|t2=for two}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|bahay|t1=house|pambahay|t2=for use at home}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|babae|t1=woman|pambabae|t2=for women}}

===Prefix===
{{tl-head|prefix|b=+}}

# ({{n-g|Ordinal prefix}}) {{ngd|Used to form ordinal numbers}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|dalawa|t1=two|pangalawa|t2=second}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|walo|t1=eight|pangwalo|t2=eighth}}

====Usage notes====
Tagalog ordinal numbers prefixed with ''pang-'' are usually more informal compared to those prefixed with ''[[ika-]]''

===Prefix===
{{tl-head|prefix|b=+}}

# {{q|with syllable reduplication}} {{ngd|an action or a practice associated with the thing or action expressed by the root}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|gamot|t1=medicine|panggagamot|t2=practice of medicine}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|anak|t1=child|panganganak|t2=giving birth, delivery}}

====Derived terms====
{{prefixsee|tl}}
-------- end text --------
