Page 15068 pangadyi: Already saw {{tl-pr}}, skipping: {{tl-pr|pangadyî}}
Page 15068 pangadyi: Skipped, no changes
Page 15068 pangadyi: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|pang̃aryi||obsolete|Abecedario orthography}}

===Etymology===
From {{af|tl|pang-|alt2=*kadyi}} (possibly related with {{cog|ms|kaji}}), with the root ultimately from {{der|tl|ar|حَجِّي||pilgrim to Mecca}}. According to Fr. San Buena Ventura (1613), the word is from Brunei. Compare {{cog|pam|pangadi}}, {{cog|bcl|pangadyi}}, {{cog|ceb|pangadyi}}, {{cog|hil|pangadi}}, {{cog|mrw|pangadi'}}, {{cog|tsg|pangadji'}}, {{cog|jv|ꦔꦗꦶ}}, and {{cog|ms|pengajian}}. See also {{m|tl|haj}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|pangadyî}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|pangadyî|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|obsolete}}

# [[prayer]] {{q|in general}}
#: {{syn|tl|dasal|panalangin}}
# {{lb|tl|Islam}} a [[Muslim]] [[prayer]] recited by a Muslim [[cleric]] called [[sheik]]
# [[supplicate|supplicating]] [[prayer]]s or [[incantation]]s of a {{l|tl|katalona}}
# {{lb|tl|Christianity}} [[Christian]] [[doctrine]]

