Page 15197 para: Replacing {{audio|tl|Tl-PH-para.ogg|Audio}} with argument part <audio:Tl-PH-para.ogg>
Page 15197 para: Removing explicit syllabification same as auto-syllabification: {{hyph|tl|pa|ra}}
Page 15197 para: Replaced {{tl-IPA}} with {{tl-pr|+<audio:Tl-PH-para.ogg>}}
Page 15197 para: Would save with comment = convert {{tl-IPA}} to {{tl-pr}}; incorporate {{audio|tl|Tl-PH-para.ogg|Audio}} into {{tl-pr}}; remove {{hyph}} same as respelling auto-syllabification
Page 15197 para: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|+<audio:Tl-PH-para.ogg>}}

===Etymology 1===
{{bor+|tl|es|para||for}}.

====Conjunction====
{{tl-head|conjunction|b=+}}

# [[for]]; [[so]]; [[in order to]]
#: {{syn-lite|tl|upang|nang}}
#: {{ux-lite|tl|'''Para''' makapasok sa eskuwelahan, kailangan mo ng valid ID.|'''In order to''' be able to go inside the school, you need a valid ID.}}

====Preposition====
{{tl-prep|b=+}}

# [[for]]
#: {{ux-lite|tl|Nagtatrabaho si Ate Virgie '''para''' sa kanyang pamilya.|Virgie works '''for''' her family.}}

===Etymology 2===
{{bor+|tl|es|para||stop}} (second person singular imperative), from {{m-lite|es|parar||stop}}.

====Interjection====
{{tl-head|interjection|b=+}}

# {{n-g|Said by any [[jeepney]] passenger to call onto the driver to [[halt]] the vehicle, with the intention of [[dismount]]ing.}}
#: {{syn-lite|tl|tigil|hinto}}

=====Usage notes=====
* The word is usually paired with {{m|tl|ho}} or {{m|tl|po}} for respect: {{m|tl||para ho}} / {{m|tl||para po}}.

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|pumara|parahin}}

=====Related terms=====
{{rel3|tl|parakaida|pararayos|paragwas|parasol|parakaidero|parakaydista|antipara}}

===Etymology 3===
From {{inh|tl|poz-pro|*pada||same, equal, like}}. Compare {{cog-lite|ilo|pada}}, {{cog-lite|ms|pada}}, {{cog-lite|mak|ᨄᨑ|tr={{l-lite|mak|para}}}}, {{cog-lite|kaw|paḍa}}. Also possibly borrowed from {{bor-lite|tl|es|comparar}}.

====Adjective====
{{tl-adj|b=+}}

# [[look like|looking like]]; [[seem]]
#: {{syn-lite|tl|mukha}}
#: {{ux-lite|tl|'''Para''' kang tanga...|You '''look like''' an idiot...}}
#: {{ux-lite|tl|'''Parang''' may gusto ka sa akin.|You '''seem to''' like me / have a crush on me.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* This word is now usually seen as {{m|tl|parang}}, except when an enclitic is used which separates ''para'' and {{m|tl|-ng}}, although this could be ignored also and have the enclitic after the word ''parang'' modifies.
*: {{ux-lite|tl|'''Parang'''... '''Parang''' aso siya.|It looks like... It looks like a dog.}} (instead of ''Para siyang aso.'')
* This word may appear as {{m|tl|parang}} alone. For example, when agreeing with someone that it actually looks like a dog, you reply with ''parang'' “It seems so”, or ''parang nga'' “It actually looks like one”.
* This word used to be used like {{m|tl|tulad}} or {{m|tl|gaya}}, it used genitive case ({{m|tl|ng}}, {{m|tl|mo}}, etc.) instead of the linker {{m|tl|-ng}}. Seen in the [[Lord's Prayer]] ({{m|tl|Ama Namin}}), which is still preserved today. The Lord's Prayer spells {{m|tl|ng}} as ''nang''.
*: {{ux-lite|tl|Dito sa lupa, '''para nang''' sa langit.|On earth '''as it is''' in heaven.}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|kapara|parang|magkapara|walang kapara|pumara|makipara|magpara|ipara|parahan|pagparahin|magkaparahan|magparahan|para-para|himara|parahin}}

=====See also=====
{{rel3|tl|tulad|gaya|tila}}

-------- end text --------
