Page 15259 paritaan: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Possibly from {{af|tl|pa-||alt2=*dita|-an}}. The root may be a lost stem according to Potet (2017). See also {{cog|ms|pelita||lamp}}, which ultimately came from {{ncog|fa-cls|پلیته|tr=palīta||candle wick}}. Compare {{cog|mrw|palita'an||lantern; lamp}}, {{cog|mdh|palitan||lamp}}, and {{cog|tsg|palitaan||lamp}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|parita7án}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|paritaán|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|obsolete}}

# [[oil lamp]]
#: {{syn|tl|lampara|sumbo|sumbuhan}}
# [[lantern]]
#: {{syn|tl|parol|linterna}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|magparitaan}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|pam|paritaan|bor=1}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1860}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1613|140|Candil) Paritaan [(pc)] cuelgan de en media vn palo y en las puntas ponen dos eſcudillas con açeyte y mecha, nagpaparitaan .2.c. tener candil deſtos, los pobres le haçen de ſola vnamecha y el palo de ſola vna punta de çierta hechura.}}
* {{R:tl:Potet|ABCT|page=267}}

{{C|tl|Light sources}}
