Page 15336 pasintabi: Removing explicit syllabification same as auto-syllabification: {{hyph|tl|pa|sin|ta|bi}}
Page 15336 pasintabi: Replaced {{tl-IPA|pasintabì}} with {{tl-pr|pasintabì}}
Page 15336 pasintabi: Would save with comment = convert {{tl-IPA}} to {{tl-pr}}; remove {{hyph}} same as respelling auto-syllabification
Page 15336 pasintabi: -------- begin text --------
{{phrasebook|tl}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|pasantabi}}
* {{alt|tl|pasangtabi}}
* {{alt|tl|pasingtabi}}

===Etymology===
From its variant {{m|tl|pasantabi}}, from {{prefix|tl|pa|santabi}} which is derived from {{der|tl|sa|क्षन्तव्य}}. See {{m|tl|tabi}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|pasintabì}}

===Phrase===
{{tl-head|phrase|pasintabì|b=+}}

# [[excuse me]]
#: {{syn|tl|patawad|pasensya}}
# {{lb|tl|obsolete}} [[goodbye]]
#: {{syn|tl|paalam}}

====Usage notes====
''Pasintabi'' is used to indicate when the speaker may do or discuss something that is deemed crude, vulgar or graphically sensitive, especially those related to toilet talk or depictions of violence. The honorific particle {{m|tl|po}} is added after when addressing people of higher status or of older age.
-------- end text --------
