Page 15413 patay: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{inh+|tl|poz-pro|*p-atay||kill}}, from {{inh|tl|map-pro|*pa-aCay||kill}}, from {{inh|tl|map-pro|*aCay||death}}. Compare {{cog|ilo|patay}}, {{cog|pag|patey}}, {{cog|xsb|pati}}, {{cog|pam|pate}}, {{cog|ceb|patay}}, {{cog|mrw|patay}}, and {{cog|jv|ꦥꦠꦶ}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|patáy}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|patáy|b=+}}

# [[cadaver]]; [[corpse]]; [[dead]] body of a person
#: {{syn|tl|bangkay}}
# [[carcass]]; the dead body of an animal
# state or condition of being dead
# the [[dead]]; those who have [[died]]
#: {{syn|tl|namatay|yumao|pumanaw|sumakabilang-buhay|nasawi|minatay|q6=obsolete}}
#: {{ux|tl|Idalangin natin ang mga '''patay'''.|Let's pray for '''those who have died'''.}}
# act of [[kill]]ing something or someone
# {{lb|tl|by extension}} act of [[shut off|shutting off]] something
#: {{ant|tl|bukas}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|patáy|b=+}}

# [[dead]]; [[lifeless]]; no longer living
#: {{syn|tl|walang-buhay|utas}}
# [[off]]; not on; [[unpowered]] {{q|as of a light, machine}}
#: {{syn|tl|nakasara|sarado}}
#: {{ant|tl|nakasindi}}
# [[dried]]; no longer growing {{q|as of plants}}
#: {{syn|tl|tuyo}}
# [[obsolete]]; [[extinct]]; no longer in use {{lb|tl|as of a word, language, or law}}
# {{lb|tl|colloquial}} [[smitten]]; [[in love]]; [[head over heels]]
#: {{ux|tl|'''patay na patay''' kay Rody|'''head over heels''' with Rody|inline=1}}

====Derived terms====
{{col-auto|tl|pumatay|mapatay|patayin|patay kang bata ka|patay-gutom|patay malisya|Araw ng mga Patay|Dagat Patay|pagpatay|mamamatay-tao|pamatay|himatay|himatayin|mahimatayin|pagkahimatayin|himamatayin|pagkahimatay|mahimatay|ipapatay|patay-dampot|patay-sindi}}

====Related terms====
