Page 15615 petsa de peligro: Would save with comment = convert {{tl-IPA}} to {{tl-pr}}; remove/incorporate {{hyph}} into {{tl-pr}}
Page 15615 petsa de peligro: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{bor+|tl|es|[[fecha]] [[de]] [[peligro]]|t=date of danger}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|petsa de peli.gro}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# the [[last]] [[stretch]] of [[days]] before [[pay day]]

====Usage notes====
* Used as a metaphor for the dwindling cash supply (and the corresponding implications) before the next pay day. The original Spanish phrase ''fecha de peligro'' simply means ''date of danger'' and never has the same connotation as used in the Philippines.

===Further reading===
* http://www.shellyviajeratravel.com/2017/08/filipino-phrases-borrowed-from-spanish.html
