Page 15717 pinklawan: Already saw {{tl-pr}}, skipping: {{tl-pr|pink.lawan}}
Page 15717 pinklawan: Skipped, no changes
Page 15717 pinklawan: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{blend|tl|en:pink|dilawan<t:Liberal Party supporter><lit:yellow-inclined>}}, with pink as {{w|Leni Robredo}}'s campaign color. Despite running as an independent candidate in 2022, Leni was still associated during the campaign with her former party, {{w|Liberal Party (Philippines)|Liberal Party}}, which is associated with the color [[yellow]].

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|pink.lawan}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|Philippine politics|slang|sometimes|derogatory}} 

# [[supporter]] of {{w|Leni Robredo}}'s campaign
#: {{syn|tl|kakampink}}

====Usage notes====
* Used by supporters of {{w|Bongbong Marcos}} or {{w|Rodrigo Duterte}} as a derogatory term for supporters of {{w|Leni Robredo}}.

===Further reading===
* {{cite-web|en|url=http://www.archipelagofiles.com/2021/10/pinklawan-meaning.html|title=Pinklawan Meaning|work=Archipelago Files|accessdate=2024-04-29|passage=Although the term is used (mostly by Marcos supporters) as a derogatory term meant to insult Robredo supporters, some Robredo supporters have embraced the term.}}
* {{cite-web|en-US|url=https://www.rappler.com/newsbreak/inside-track/bato-dela-rosa-stumps-for-sara-duterte-hits-pinklawans-catarman-northern-samar/|title=Bato stumps for Sara Duterte, hits ‘pinklawans’ in Catarman|work=RAPPLER|date=2022-04-08|accessdate=2024-04-29|author=Bea Cupin|passage=“'''Pinklawan'''” is a derogatory slang term for those who support the candidacy of Vice President Leni Robredo, a play on “pink” and “dilawan” (yellowish). Robredo’s campaign color is pink, while her party – although she is running as an independent now – is associated with the color yellow.}}
-------- end text --------
