Page 15724 Pinoy Henyo: Already saw {{tl-pr}}, skipping: {{tl-pr|Pinóy Henyo}}
Page 15724 Pinoy Henyo: Skipped, no changes
Page 15724 Pinoy Henyo: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|pinoy henyo||alternative letter-case}}

===Etymology===
{{lit|Pinoy Genius}}. From a segment of the same name since 2004, in the noontime show ''{{w|Eat Bulaga!}}'', the longest running variety show in the Philippines. The segment was later succeeded by ''Gimme 5: Laro ng Mga Henyo'' ({{lit|Gimme 5: Game of the Geniuses|nocap=1}}) and ''Word of the Rings'' by 2023 after the ''Eat Bulaga'' trademark dispute.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|Pinóy Henyo}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|[[Pinóy]] [[henyo|Henyo]]|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|game}} a [[guessing game]] where one player has to [[guess]] the word given (usually placed on the player's forehead) by asking questions and other players (one or more) can only answer the questions through [[yes]], [[no]], or [[maybe]] before the timer runs out
-------- end text --------
