===Etymology 1===
Early borrowing from {{bor|tl|es|fiesta}}. Compare {{cog|ms|pesta}}. {{doublet|tl|piyesta}}, a later borrowing.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|pistá}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|pistá|b=+}}

# [[feast day]]; [[festival]]; [[festivity]]
#: {{syn|tl|pagdiriwang}}
#: {{uxi|tl|Ika-16 ng Enero ang '''pista''' ng Santo Niño.|The '''feast''' of the Santo Niño is at January 16.}}
# [[feast]] or [[banquet]] associated with a feast day
#: {{syn|tl|piyesta|piging|handa}}
# {{lb|tl|obsolete}} [[feast]] [[keep|kept]] outside of a [[Sunday]] or a [[patron]] [[holiday]] {{defdate|16th|17th c.}}

=====Alternative forms=====
* {{alt|tl|piyasta||obsolete}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|kapistahan|pista opisyal|ipagpista|makipamista|mamista|pamista|magpista|mamimista|pagpistahan|Pista ng Tatlong Hari}}

===Etymology 2===

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|pistâ}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|pistâ|b=+}}

# act of [[undervalue|undervaluing]] or [[underrate|underrating]], in a [[mean]] [[manner]], the [[merit]]s of someone or something; [[faultfinding]]; [[belittlement]]
#: {{syn|tl|pintas|puna|pula|pagmamaliit}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|pagpista|pamimista|pamista|pumista|magpista|pistaan|ipista}}

===Etymology 3===
{{bor+|tl|es|pista||track; course}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|pistâ}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|pistâ|b=+}}

# [[lane]]
#: {{syn|tl|daan}}

===References===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:Diccionario de terminos comunes tagalo-castellano|110}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1860}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1613}}
** page 320: “Fieſta) Piſta ([pc]) C. que ſe guarda fuera del domingo ola fieſta del patron”
** page 417: “Menos preciar) Piſta (pc) C. teniẽdo [a otro] en poco”
