Page 15986 pots: Skipped, no changes
Page 15986 pots: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{clipping|tl|nocap=1}} of {{af|tl|en:potassium|-s}}. Potassium has the symbol {{m|mul|K}} after {{der|tl|NL.|kalium}}. {{m|mul|K}} is reinterpreted as {{ncog|en|k}}, short for {{m|en|okay}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|pot_s}}

===Interjection===
{{tl-head|interjection|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|slang|dated}}

# [[okay]]
#: {{syn|tl|okey|sige}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''Pots! Pots!''' Papunta na ako!|'''Okay! Okay!''' I'll be right there.}}

====Usage notes====
* Mostly used by young people belonging in the social upper class especially in Manila.
