Page 16346 Quezon: Already saw {{tl-pr}}, skipping: {{tl-pr|Queson|syll=+}}
Page 16346 Quezon: Skipped, no changes
Page 16346 Quezon: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Ultimately from {{der|tl|nan-hbl|-}}, possibly {{m|nan-hbl|雞孫|tr=koe-sun / ke-sun}}, via {{bor|tl|es|Quezon}}. The places in the Philippines are named after {{w|Manuel L. Quezon}}, the second president of the [[Philippines]]. See also {{m|tl|Tuazon}}, {{m|tl|Dizon}}, {{m|tl|Lacson}}, {{m|tl|Tiongson}}, {{m|tl|Singson}}, {{m|tl|Pecson}}, {{m|tl|Quiazon}}, etc.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|Queson|syll=+}}

===Proper noun===
{{tl-proper noun|b=+}}

# {{place|tl|province|c/Philippines|;|caplc=Lucena|former name: [[Tayabas]]|t=Quezon}}
# [[w:en:Manuel Quezon|Manuel Quezon]] {{gl|2nd president of the Philippines}}
# {{surname|tl|from=Spanish < Hokkien}}, originally of Chinese origin common with Filipinos of Chinese ancestry
# {{place|tl|several <<locations>> in the <<c/Philippines>>}}:
## {{place|tl|municipality|p/Quezon|c/Philippines|on the southern tip of [[Alabat]] island}}
## {{place|tl|municipality|p/Isabela|c/Philippines}}
## {{place|tl|municipality|p/Bukidnon|c/Philippines}}
## {{place|tl|municipality|p/Nueva Ecija|c/Philippines}}
## {{place|tl|municipality|p/Nueva Vizcaya|c/Philippines}}
## {{place|tl|municipality|p/Palawan|c/Philippines}}

====Derived terms====
