Page 16857 sablay: Removing explicit syllabification same as auto-syllabification: {{hyph|tl|sab|lay}}
Page 16857 sablay: Replaced {{tl-IPA|sabláy}} with {{tl-pr|sabláy}}
Page 16857 sablay: Would save with comment = convert {{tl-IPA}} to {{tl-pr}}; remove {{hyph}} same as respelling auto-syllabification
Page 16857 sablay: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Possibly from {{inh|tl|phi-pro|*sab(ə)lay|*sab(ə)láy|to hang, drape over something}}. Compare {{cog|ivb|sabhay}}, {{cog|ifb|habluy}}, {{cog|ifk|hable}}, {{cog|pam|sable}}, {{cog|bcl|sablay}}, {{cog|akl|sabeay}}, {{cog|ceb|sablay}}, {{cog|mrw|sablay}}, and {{cog|tsg|sablay}}.

The “sash” sense is from the ''sablay'' garment used by the University of the Philippines created by six professors from UP Diliman, as inspired by the {{m|en|malong}} of Muslim Mindanao, to be worn diagonally across the chest on formal occasions, perhaps named as such due to the sense of “to hang over” in other Philippine languages like Cebuano.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|sabláy}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|sabláy|b=+}}

# [[wide of the mark]]; not [[strike|striking]] the [[target]] aimed at
#: {{syn|tl|sala|lihis|nagmintis|mumintis}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|sablayan|sumablay|pagsablay|isablay}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|sabláy|b=+}}

# [[miss]]; [[failure]] {{q|to hit, guess, answer, etc.}}
#: {{syn|tl|mintis|pagmintis|pagmimintis|sala|pagsala|lihis|paglihis}}
# [[oblique]] or [[indirect]] [[hint]]; [[insinuation]]; [[innuendo]]
# [[hard]], [[quick]] but [[indirect]] [[blow]] with the [[fist]]
# [[swiftness]] due to [[lightness]] {{q|such as of a small boat}}
# {{w|academic regalia}} [[sash]] worn across the [[chest]] {{gl|especially used during [[graduation]]s of the {{w|University of the Philippines}}}}
# {{lb|tl|by extension}} any [[garment]] [[hang|hung]] over the [[shoulder]] for [[formal]] [[wear]]
# {{lb|tl|obsolete}} [[hit]] to the [[side]] {{q|with a fist or with a weapon}}
# {{lb|tl|obsolete|by extension}} act of [[affront]]ing or [[insult]]ing another with words as if one does not speak to the other
# {{lb|tl|obsolete|by extension}} act of [[say]]ing something to another so that the person who did something would [[understand]] it

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|pasablay|magsablay|pasablay|sumablay|masablay|sablayan|pasablayin}}

====See also====
{{col3|tl|salampay|alampay|panuwelo|sabit}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{cite-web|work=Sablay on UP’s shoulder|url=https://cebudailynews.inquirer.net/137340/sablay-ups-shoulder|date=June 24, 2017|publisher=Cebu Daily News|first=Madrileña|last=de la Cerna}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1860}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1613}}
** page 30: “Afrentar) Sablay [(pc)] de palabra a otro como que no habla con el”
** page 218: “Deçir) Sablay (pc) a otro algo [ꝑa] q̃ lo entienda el q̃ lo hiço”
** page 390: “Lijero) Sablay (pc) de como nauio”
** page 560: “Soſlayo) Sablay (pc) de lança rejõ o otra coſa”

{{C|tl|Clothing}}
