===Etymology===
Borrowed from (c. 16th-18th century) {{w|Early Modern Spanish|Early Modern}} {{bor|tl|es|jabón}}, from {{der|tl|osp|xabon}}, from {{der|tl|la|sāpōnem}}, singular accusative of {{der|tl|la|sāpō}}, from {{der|tl|gem-pro|*saipǭ}}. In {{w|Early Modern Spanish}}, Spanish {{angbr|j}} was pronounced {{IPAchar|/ʃ/}}; {{IPAchar|/ʃ/}} became {{IPAchar|/s/}} as common with other early borrowings (compare {{m|tl|singkamas}}, {{m|tl|sugal}}, {{m|tl|sugarol}}, {{m|tl|saro}}, and {{m|tl|tasa}}).

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|sabón<audio:Tl-PH-sabon.ogg>}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|sabón|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|chemistry}} [[soap]]
# {{lb|tl|by extension}} [[detergent]]
# [[washing]] with [[soap]]
# {{lb|tl|figurative}} [[severe]] [[rebuke]] {{q|against someone}}
#: {{syn|tl|mura|pagmura}}
# {{lb|tl|obsolete}} [[coconut oil]] [[soap]] {{defdate|16th|17th c.}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|pagsasabon|isabon|magsabon|masabon|sabunan|sabunin|tagasabon|tagapagsabon|sabong panlaba|hinahabol na ng sabon}}

