Page 17029 salaghati: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|salachati||obsolete|Abecedario orthography}}
* {{alt|tl|salakhati}}

===Etymology===
Possibly from either:
* {{glossary|Borrowed}} from a compound of {{compound|tl|salag|hati|t1=full and leveled|t2=emotions|lit2=liver|lang2=ms}}, according to Potet (2016). Compare {{m|tl|dalamhati}}, {{m|tl|luwalhati}}, {{m|tl|pighati}}, {{m|tl|ulohati}}, and {{m|tl|lunggati}}. Possibly also from {{noncog|ms|sedak||suffocate; choke}}.
* {{glossary|Borrowed}} from {{cog|es|zaragata||turmoil; scuffle; quarrel}}, according to Lopez (1965). Compare possible doublet {{m|tl|saragate}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|salaghatì}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|salaghatì|b=+}}

# [[resentment]]; [[displeasure]]; [[indignation]]
#: {{syn|tl|hinanakit|sama ng loob|sakahati|q3=obsolete}}
# [[affliction]]; [[suffering]]; [[melancholy]]
#: {{syn|tl|dalamhati|pighati|dusa|sakahati|q4=obsolete}}

====See also====
* {{l|tl|galit}}
* {{l|tl|yamot}}

===Further reading===
