Page 17065 salap: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{bor+|tl|ar|صَرْف||money exchange; expense; money}}. {{root|tl|ar|ص ر ف}} Compare {{cog|ar|صَرَّاف||[[money changer]]}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|colloquial}} [[tip]] {{gl|fee for a small service}} {{defdate|from 20th c.}}
#: {{syn|tl|pabuya|tip}}
# {{lb|tl|gambling|colloquial}} [[small]] [[goodwill]] [[share]] of [[money]] given away by the [[winner]] to [[companion]]s
#: {{syn|tl|balato}}
# {{lb|tl|fishing}} [[small]] [[fishing]] [[net]] {{q|used for catching fry and other tiny fishes}}
# {{lb|tl|fishing}} [[catching]] of [[fry]] and other [[tiny]] [[fish]]es using such a [[net]]
#: {{syn|tl|pagsalap|pananalap}}
# [[skimmer]] {{gl|utensil for skimming liquids}}
#: {{syn|tl|panagap}}
# [[skimming]] of [[liquid]]
#: {{syn|tl|sagap|pagsagap|halagap|paghalagap}}
# something [[skimmed]] on the [[surface]] of a [[liquid]]
#: {{syn|tl|sagap}}
# {{lb|tl|obsolete}} [[wage]]s; [[salary]] {{defdate|18th|19th c.}}
# {{lb|tl|obsolete}} [[judge]]'s [[fee]]s {{defdate|16th|17th c.}}
#* {{quote-text|tl|year=1752|author=Francisco de San José|title=Arte y reglas de la lengua Tagala
|passage=Magcano cayá ang quinoha mong '''salap''' sa caniya?}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|manalap|salapan|ipagsalap|pasalapan|magpasalap|magsalap}}

=====See also=====
* {{l|tl|sima}}
* {{l|tl|sakag}}

===Etymology 2===

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|saláp}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|saláp|b=+}}

# [[nearly]] [[missed]] [[strike]] or [[stab]]
# {{lb|tl|fishing}} a [[type]] of [[freshwater]] [[fishing]] [[net]]

===References===
* {{R:tl:Potet|APL|page=152}}
-------- end text --------
