===Etymology===
From {{m|tl|salap||judge's fees}} + {{m|tl|-i}}, from {{der|tl|ar|صَرْف|t=money exchange; change; [[money]]}} and possibly confused with {{der|tl|ar|أَشْرَفِيّ|t=gold coin; [[ducat]]}}, according to Potet (2013). Another etymology suggested is from {{der|tl|ms|se-}} + {{der|tl|ms|rupiah}}, according to Panganiban (1972).

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|salapî}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|salapî|b=+}}

# [[money]]
#: {{syn|tl|pera|kuwarta|Thesaurus:salapi}}
# [[currency]]
# {{lb|tl|archaic}} [[fifty]]-[[centavo]] [[coin]]
#: {{syn|tl|batngin}}
# {{lb|tl|historical}} [[tostón]] {{gl|coin worth four Spanish reales}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|salapiin|magkasalapi|manalapi|masalapi|pampananalapi|panalapian|pananalapi|gantimpalang-salapi|mukhang-salapi|Panalapiang Internasyonal|salaping-papel|mabigat ang salapi}}

===References===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:tl:Potet|APL|page=152}}

{{C|tl|Money}}

