===Etymology 1===
From Proto-Central Philippine ''*salú'' ({{m-g|catch in hand}}). Compare {{cog|bcl|salo}}, {{cog|ceb|salo}}, and {{cog|hil|salo}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|saló}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|saló|b=+}}

# [[catching]] with one's [[hand]] {{q|of a ball, etc.}}
#: {{syn|tl|sambot|pagsambot}}
# [[supporting]] from [[under]] an [[object]] {{q|especially with one's hand}}
#: {{syn|tl|sapo|pagsapo|sapupo|pagsapupo}}
# [[undersupport]]; [[prop]]
#: {{syn|tl|tukod|talukod|sapo}}
# [[take over|taking over]] of a [[task]] [[left]] by another

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|tagasalo|saluhin|sumalo|saluhan|pasaluhin|pasaluhan|pasalo|panalo|pansalo|pagsalo|masalo|magsaluhan|makasalo|ipasalo|salungkawit|salungguhit|salungguhitan|salumbaba|salumbabaan|salumpuwit}}

===Etymology 2===
From Proto-Central Philippine ''*sálu'' ({{m-g|to eat together}}). Compare {{cog|pam|salu}}, {{cog|bcl|salo}}, {{cog|akl|saeo}}, {{cog|ceb|salo}}, {{cog|hil|salo}}, {{cog|war|saro}}, and {{cog|tsg|sāw}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# [[eating]] with [[another]] or [[together]] {{q|especially on the same plate}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|kasalo|isalo|makasalo|makisalo|magkasalo|magsalo|pagsalo|pagsaluhan|saluhan|pagsasalo|pasalo|pagsaluhan|pasaluhin|sumalo|salo-salo|magsalo-salo|pagsasalo-salo|salo-saluhan|pagsalo-saluhan|salubayo}}

===Etymology 3===

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|salò}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|salò|b=+}}

# [[mechanical]] [[catch]] {{q|in necklaces, bracelets, etc.}}
