Page 17244 sampu: Already saw {{tl-pr}}, skipping: {{tl-pr|sampû<audio:TL-PH-sampu.ogg>}}
Page 17244 sampu: Skipped, no changes
Page 17244 sampu: -------- begin text --------
{{number box|tl}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|sampo||colloquial}}
* {{alt|tl|sampouo|sangpouo||obsolete|Abecedario orthography}}
* {{alt|tl|sampuo|sampuwo|sangpuo|sangpuwo||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{m|tl|sampuo}}, from {{m|tl|sampuwo}}, from older {{m|tl|sampulo}}, ultimately from {{der|tl|map-pro|*sa-ŋa-puluq||ten}}. Compare {{cog|ilo|sangapulo}}, {{cog|bcl|sampulo}}, {{cog|mrw|sapolo'}}, {{cog|ms|sepuluh}}, {{cog|bhp|sampuru}}, and {{cog|haw|anahulu||period of ten days}}. {{surf|tl|sam-|pu|lit=one ten}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|sampû<audio:TL-PH-sampu.ogg>}}

===Numeral===
{{tl-num|sampû|b=+}}

# {{cln|tl|cardinal numbers}} [[ten]]
#: {{syn|tl|diyes}}

====Usage notes====
* To describe the quantity of something, the number is placed before the noun and affixed with the ([[-ng]]) [[enclitic]] [[suffix]] when the word ends with a [[vowel]] or with the "[[na]]" [[preposition]] for those ending in a [[consonant]].
*: ''Isa'''ng''' saging, dalawa'''ng''' pinya''
*: ''Apat '''na''' mansanas, anim '''na''' mangga''

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|ikasampu|pansampu|makasampu|sampuan|sampuin|pasampu|kasampu|pagsampuin|tigsampu|panampu|sampung laksa|sampung libo|sampung daan|sasampuin|pansampu|Sampung Utos}}

====See also====
{{col3|tl|labing-}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:Diccionario tagálog-hispano|1156}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1860}}

{{C|tl|Ten}}
