Page 17274 sana: Would save with comment = convert {{tl-IPA}} to {{tl-pr}} (3); remove {{hyph}} same as respelling auto-syllabification (3)
Page 17274 sana: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr}}

====Adverb====
{{tl-adv|b=+}}

# {{n-g|used to express hope or wish in something unknown}}: [[hopefully]]; I [[wish]] that
#: {{syn|tl|kahimanawari|nawari|nawa}}
#: {{ux|tl|Masaya '''sana''' sila.|'''I hope''' they're happy.|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''Sana''' nakarating sila nang ligtas.|'''Hopefully''' they all arrived safely.|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''Sana''' sa ibang pamilya na lang ako ipinanganak.|'''I wish''' I was born in a different family instead.|inline=1}}
# {{n-g|used to express an unrealized intention or situation}}
#: {{ux|tl|Nanalo '''sana''' siya sa takbuhan, pero nadapa siya sa pinakadulo.|He '''would have''' won the race, but he tripped at the very end.|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|tl|Pupunta '''sana''' ako sa bahay mo, pero nagbago ang isip ko.|I '''originally intended to''' go to your house, but I changed my mind.|inline=1}}
# {{n-g|used to express disappointment in a desired but unrealized result, especially due to an unfulfilled condition}}
#: {{ux|tl|Nag-aaral na '''sana''' ako ngayon sa iskul, kung hindi ako nagkasakit.|I '''would have been''' studying in school right now, if only I hadn't gotten sick.|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|tl|Kung nahulog siya sa patibong, patay na '''sana''' siya.|If only he fell into the trap, he '''would be''' dead right now.|inline=1}}

=====Derived terms=====
