Page 17294 sando: Removing explicit syllabification same as auto-syllabification: {{hyph|tl|san|do}}
Page 17294 sando: Replaced {{tl-IPA}} with {{tl-pr}}
Page 17294 sando: Would save with comment = convert {{tl-IPA}} to {{tl-pr}}; remove {{hyph}} same as respelling auto-syllabification
Page 17294 sando: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Possibly of {{der|tl|ja|-}} origin, according to Potet (2016) and the Komisyon sa Wikang Filipino. Compare {{cog|bn|স্যান্ডো গেঞ্জি}}, {{w|Regional_differences_and_dialects_in_Indian_English#Assamese_English|Assamese}} {{cog|en|sando-ganji}}, {{cog|pam|sandu}} and {{cog|hi|सैंडो गंजी}}. Another theory says that the word is named after German vaudeville showman and bodybuilder {{w|Eugene Sandow}} (1867-1925) who wore a sleeveless shirt when showing off his muscles.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# [[sleeveless]] [[undershirt]]; [[tank top]]; [[singlet]]

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|magsando|nakasando|sando bag}}

====See also====
* {{l|tl|kamiseta}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:tl:Potet|TBC|page=344}}
* {{cite-web|title=S (Filipino Cultural Dictionary)|work=Living in the Philippines|url=http://www.livinginthephilippines.com/culture-and-people/philippine-culture/filipino-cultural-dictionary/1269-s-filipino-cultural-dictionary?fbclid=IwAR0iSyW0h0PhNFFhoAuR6ryI4lE9bFbH0BdH18q1F2TGxop9MnXpK6FNgT8|accessdate=5 November 2022|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20221105002112/http://www.livinginthephilippines.com/culture-and-people/philippine-culture/filipino-cultural-dictionary/1269-s-filipino-cultural-dictionary?fbclid=IwAR0iSyW0h0PhNFFhoAuR6ryI4lE9bFbH0BdH18q1F2TGxop9MnXpK6FNgT8|archivedate=5 November 2022}}

-------- end text --------
