{{bor+|tl|es|sardinas}}, plural form of {{m|es|sardina}}, from {{der|tl|la|sardina}}, from {{der|tl|grc|σαρδίνη}}. The figurative sense is from the analogy of a fully packed vehicle likened to a can of sardines.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# [[sardines]]
# [[canned]] [[sardines]]

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|figurative}} [[packed like sardines]]; [[filled]] to [[full]] [[capacity]] {{q|of vehicles}}
#: {{syn|tl|siksikan}}
#: {{ux|tl|Parang '''sardinas''' ang bus papuntang Cubao.|The bus heading to Cubao seems '''full'''.|lit=The bus heading to Cubao is like '''sardines'''.}}

