* {{l|tl|masasaan}}

===Etymology 4===

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|+|sasà<qq:obsolete>}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# [[cleaving]] in the [[middle]]
# [[cleave]] someone with a [[knife]] [[downwards]] {{defdate|16th|17th c.}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|sasahin|sumasa}}

===Etymology 5===

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|sasâ}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|sasâ|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|obsolete}} {{n-g|name of the Baybayin letter {{l|tl|{{tl-bay sc|sa}}|tr=-}}, corresponding to "sa"}}

====See also====
{{col3|tl|sa}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1860}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1613}}
** page 349: “Hender) Saſa (pp) de vna cuchillada a alguno de alto abajo”
** page 444: “Nipa) Saſa (pc) con q̃ cubren las caſas, ſacã vino della”
** page 461: “Palma) Saſa (pc) baja como mata, hecha vn tallo que cultiuado almodo de las palmas de cocos da vn licor de que ſe haçe mejor [y mas] ſano vino que de las de cocos.”
** page 538: “S) Saſa (pc) deſta lengua Tagala.{{!}}. ſaſa yaon .{{!}}. {{tl-bay sc|sa|disp=1}} . ygava mo aco dito nang iſang ſaſa, haz me aqui vna letra .S. di ſaſa, ang ypinaſulat co [ſa iyo]? note mande eſcriuir vna .S?”

