{{glossary|Borrowed}} from (c. 16th-18th century) {{w|Early Modern Spanish|Early Modern}} {{bor|tl|es|Jesucristo||Jesus Christ}}. In {{w|Early Modern Spanish}}, Spanish {{angbr|j}} was pronounced {{IPAchar|/ʃ/}}; {{IPAchar|/ʃ/}} became {{IPAchar|/s/}} as common with other early borrowings. {{doublet|tl|Hesukristo}}. Attested in ''{{w|Doctrina Christiana}}''.

