Page 18146 siya: Would save with comment = convert {{tl-IPA}} to {{tl-pr}} (3); remove {{hyph}} same as respelling auto-syllabification (3)
Page 18146 siya: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|tl|poz-pro|*(si-)ia}}, from {{inh|tl|map-pro|*(si-)ia}}. Compare {{cog|bcl|siya}}, {{cog|ceb|siya}}, {{cog|id|ia}}, {{cog|mi|ia}}, and {{cog|war|hiya}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|tl|sya||informal}}
* {{alt|tl|s'ya||contraction}}
* {{alt|tl|xa||text messaging}}

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|siyá}}

====Pronoun====
{{tl-pron|siyá|b=+}}

# [[he]]; [[she]] {{gl|third person singular animate personal pronoun}}
#: {{ux|tl|Pilipino '''siya'''.|'''S/he''' is a Filipino.}}
# {{lb|tl|colloquial}} [[it]] {{gl|third person singular inanimate personal pronoun}}

=====See also=====
{{tl-personal pronouns}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|siyá|b=+}}

# the [[one]]; the [[identical]] [[one]]; the [[very]] [[same]]
#: {{ux|tl|Ang belong ito ay '''siya'''ng ginawa ng kanyang lola.|This veil is the '''very same one''' which her grandmother made.}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|siyanga|siya nawa|siya na|siyang-siya|siyanga pala|siya ring|kung ano ang puno, siya ang bunga}}

====Interjection====
{{tl-head|interjection|siyá|b=+}}

# [[so]]! [[well]]!
#: {{syn|tl|aba}}
# {{lb|tl|dialectal|Quezon}} [[yes]]!

===Etymology 2===
Early {{glossary|borrowing}} of {{bor|tl|es|silla}}, from {{der|tl|osp|siella}}, from {{der|tl|la|sella}}. {{doublet|tl|silya}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|+|si..yá}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|+|head2=siyá|b=+}}

# [[saddle]]
#: {{syn|tl|montura|sintadera|q2=of a bicycle}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''siya''' ng kabayo|horse '''saddle'''|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''siya''' ng bisikleta|bicycle '''saddle'''|inline=1}}
#* {{quote-book|1=tl|year=1989|author=Pramoedya Ananta Toer|tlr=Thelma B. Kintanar|title=Daigdig ng Tao|publisher=Solidaridad Publishing House|page=30|text=Nakasabit sa dingding ang mga '''siya''' ng kabayo na may iba-ibang palawit na estribo.|t=The horse '''saddles''' with different stirrups are hanging on the wall.}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|magsiya|siyahan}}

===Etymology 3===
{{bor+|tl|nan-hbl|謝|tr=siā||regards to; thanks; gratefulness}}, according to Manuel (1948).

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|si..yá}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|siyá|b=+}}

# [[satisfaction]]; [[pleasure]]; [[contentment]]
#: {{syn|tl|lugod|kaluguran|kasiyahan}}
# {{lb|tl|obsolete}} [[decision]]; [[determination]] {{gl|only used in {{m|tl|pasiya}}}}
# {{lb|tl|obsolete}} [[sufficiency]]; [[adequacy]] {{gl|only used in {{m|tl|kasiya}}}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|kasiyahan|kasiya-siya|bigyang-kasiyahan|kawalang-kasiyahan|di-kasiyahan|di-kasiya-siya|magbigay-kasiyahan|makasiya|masiyahan|masiya|nakasisiya|pagbibigay-kasiyahan|walang-kasiyahan}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:tl:Manuel 1948|q=siya|page=107}}

