===Etymology===
Borrowed from (c. 16th–18th century) {{w|Early Modern Spanish|Early Modern}} {{bor|tl|es|jugar||to play}}, from {{der|tl|la|iocor|iocārī}}. In {{w|Early Modern Spanish}}, {{angbr|j}} was pronounced {{IPAchar|/ʃ/}}; this was adapted by Tagalog as {{IPAchar|/s/}}, in common with other early borrowings (compare {{m|tl|sabon}}, {{m|tl|singkamas}}, {{m|tl|sugarol}}, {{m|tl|saro}}, and {{m|tl|tasa}}). {{doublet|tl|huwego}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|sugál}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|sugál|b=+}}

# [[gambling]]
#: {{syn|tl|pagsusugal|huwego}}
# [[game]] of [[gambling]]
#: {{syn|tl|huwego}}
# [[risk-taking]]; [[act]] involving [[risk]]
#: {{syn|tl|sapalaran|pakikipagsapalaran}}
# {{lb|tl|figurative}} [[acceptance]] of a [[challenge]]
#: {{syn|tl|labanan|pakikipaglaban}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|kasugal|pasugal|magsusugal|sugalan|manunugal|magsugal|sumugal|pasugalan|sugalero|sugalera}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|tl|sugarol}}
-------- end text --------
