Page 18363 suki: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|sukì}}

===Etymology 1===
{{bor+|tl|nan-hbl|主客||tr=chú-kheh|t=regular customer or dealer}}, as per Chan-Yap (1980).<ref>{{R:tl:Chan-Yap 1980|page=145}}</ref> Cognates to {{cog|ilo|suki}}, {{cog|pag|suki}}, {{cog|bcl|suki}}, {{cog|ceb|suki}}, and {{cog|tsg|sukiꞌ}}. Compare {{ncog|tl|singki}}~{{ncog|nan-hbl|新客|tr=sin-kheh}}, {{ncog|tl|Singson}}~{{ncog|nan-hbl|曾孫|tr=cheng-sun/tsing-sun}}, {{ncog|tl|sili}}~{{ncog|es|chili}}, {{ncog|tl|sitsirya}}~{{m|tl|tsitsirya}}, {{ncog|tl|sinelas}}~{{m|tl|tsinelas}}.

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|sukì|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|business}}

# [[regular]] and [[long-standing]] [[customer]] or [[client]] {{gl|who may receive special treatment due to patronage}}
# {{lb|tl|dialectal}} [[regular]] [[vendor]] or [[dealer]] {{gl|which one buys from}}

=====Alternative forms=====
* {{alt|tl|suke}}
* {{alt|tl|suque|suqui||obsolete|Abecedario orthography}}

=====See also=====
* {{l|tl|parokyano}}

===Etymology 2===

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|sukì|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|obsolete}}

# [[cross]]-[[like]] [[support]] or [[prop]] placed inside [[house]]s
# [[act]] of [[prop up|propping up]] or [[shore up|shoring up]] (something)

=====Alternative forms=====
* {{alt|tl|soqui|suqui||obsolete|Abecedario orthography}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|magsuki|isuki|sukian}}

=====See also=====
* {{l|tl|suhay}}

===References===
<references/>

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
