===Etymology===
Possibly a {{metathesis|tl||nocap=1}} of {{der|tl|nan-hbl|仇敵|tr=siû-te̍k|t=enemy}}.<ref>{{R:tl:Chan-Yap 1980|page=133}}</ref><ref>{{cite-book|last=Agoncillo|first=Teodoro A.|authorlink=Teodoro Agoncillo|title=History of the Filipino People|url=https://archive.org/details/historyoffilipin00teod|year=1960|edition=8th|year_published=1990|publisher=Garotech Publishing|location=Quezon City|isbn=978-971-8711-06-4|page=53}}</ref><ref>{{R:tl:Manuel 1948|q=Suwitik|page=58}}</ref><ref>{{R:nan:tdj|54518|e=仇敵}}</ref><ref>{{cite-web|year=2002+|title=台華線頂對照典|work=台華對應綜合大辭典查詢|url=https://taigi.fhl.net/dic_un/|section=編號: 71159|sectionurl=https://taigi.fhl.net/dic_un/search.php?DETAIL=1&LIMIT=id=71159&dbname=tunion&graph=2}}</ref> Unrelated to {{ncog|en|Jesuitic}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|b=+}}

# [[cunning]]; [[sly]]; [[tricky]]; [[artful]]
#: {{syn|tl|tuso|madaya|mapanlinlang|sukaron}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|tl|suwitikin}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# [[swindler]]; [[cheat]]
#: {{syn|tl|manlilinlang|mangagantso|mandaraya}}

===References===
<references/>

