Page 18897 tala: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{unc|tl}}. Possibly from either:
* From {{inh|tl|poz-pro|*talaq}}.
* From {{der|tl|sa|तारा|t=star}}. Possible {{doublet|tl|estrelya|nocap=1}}.

Compare {{cog|ban|ᬢᬭᬵ|tr=tala}} and {{cog|pam|tala}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|talà}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|talà|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|star|strictly}} [[morning star]]; any [[bright]] [[star]] (except the [[Sun]])
#: {{syn|tl|lusero}}
# {{lb|tl|astronomy}} [[star]]
#: {{syn|tl|bituin|estrelya}}
# {{lb|tl|astronomy|loosely}} any [[astronomical]] [[body]] {{q|such as a star, a planet, or a comet}}
# {{lb|tl|figurative}} [[beautiful]] [[woman]]
#: {{syn|tl|paraluman}}
# {{lb|tl|figurative}} [[celebrity]] {{gl|artist, actor, etc.}}
#: {{syn|tl|bituin}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|dalubtala|dalubtalaan|dalubtalain|buntala|malatala|malabuntala|Talang Batugan|talang-bulo|talang-gubat|talumpok|talanyo|talumpon|buntalain|kabuntalaan|kabuntalaanin|alat|Bulak Tala|Tala|Talang Bakero}}

=====See also=====
{{col3|tl|Benus|Tanglaw-Daga<t:evening star>|Ilaw-Daga<t:evening star>|kometa|bulalakaw|buntala}}

===Etymology 2===
Derived from {{der|tl|sa|ताल||palmyra or fan palm tree}} whose leaves were used to write on, according to Potet (2016). Compare {{cog|ceb|mantala}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|talâ}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|talâ|b=+}}

# [[record]]; [[notes]]
#: {{syn|tl|listahan|talaan|lista|nota}}
# [[listing]]; [[jotting]] down on a [[list]]
#: {{syn|tl|pagtatala}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|talaan|aklat-talaan|ipatala|magpatala|itala|nakatala|magtala|pagpapatala|pagtatala|patalaan|tagapagtala|tagatala|talaarawan|talaangkanan|talahanayan|talahuluganan|talasalitaan|talambuhay|talabulanan|talamayawan|talababa|talababaan|talaaklatan|talaang-aklat|talaang-itim|talatauhan}}

===Etymology 3===

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# {{taxlink|Limnophila rugosa|species}} {{gl|a type of marshweed used for cooking as an aromatic}}

