Page 19131 tanim: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|tl|poz-pro|*tanəm||to plant}}, from {{inh|tl|map-pro|*CaNəm||to plant, to bury}}. Compare {{cog|akl|tanom}}, {{cog|bcl|tanom}}, {{cog|ceb|tanom}}, {{cog|ch|tanom}}, {{cog|haw|kanu||to bury; to plant}}, {{cog|pam|tanam}}, {{cog|ms|tanam}}, {{cog|sm|tanu||to bury}}, and {{cog|tsg|tanum}}.<br>Compare {{ncog|ja|-}} {{ja-r|種|た​ね|t=seed}}.<ref>{{R:tl:Potet|TBC|page=344}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|taním}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|taním|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|botany}} [[plant]]
#: {{syn|tl|halaman}}
# [[act]] of [[plant]]ing
#: {{syn|tl|pagtatanim|pagkakatanim}}
# {{lb|tl|figurative}} [[act]] of [[harbor]]ing a [[grudge]] or [[ill]] [[feeling]]
#: {{syn|tl|pagtatanim}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|itanim|makatanim|magpatanim|magtanim|magtatanim|manananim|mapatanim|matamnan|matanim|matanimin|pananim|nakatanim|pantanim|patanim|pataniman|patamnan|tagatanim|tagapagtanim|tagtanim|tamnan|taniman|panananim}}

====Related terms====
{{rel3|tl|tanaman}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|taním|b=+}}

# [[planted]] by someone {{q|of a plant, as opposed to a plant that sprouted on its own}}
#: {{syn|tl|itinanim}}

===References===
<references/>

