Page 19137 tansan: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{der|tl|ja|-}} {{ja-r|炭酸|たんさん|t=carbonated; carbonic acid}} (a {{glossary|clipping}} of {{ja-r|炭酸飲料|たんさん いんりょう|t=carbonated drink}}), a {{gentrade|tl|nocap=1}} by Clifford-Wilkinson Tansan Mineral Water Co., Ltd. popular in the Philippines in the early 20th century, initially romanized and introduced as ''"TANSAN"'' on metal bottlecaps and on {{bor|tl|en|-}} marketing material.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|+|tansán}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|+|head2=tansán|b=+}}

# [[bottlecap]] {{q|especially of soft drink bottles}}
#: {{syn|tl|takip-tansan|kitse|q2=dialectal}}
# {{lb|tl|colloquial}} [[soda]] [[water]]

====See also====
* {{l|tl|lapaw}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
