===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|tapapecho}}
* {{alt|tl|tapa pecho}}

===Etymology===
{{bor+|tl|es|[[tapa]] [[pecho]]|lit=breast cover}}. Compare [[w:Chilean Spanish|Chilean]] {{cog|es|tapapecho||beef [[brisket]]}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|archaic}}

# [[covering]] of a woman's [[breast]]
#* {{quote-book|tl|author=Modesto de Castro|title=Pag susulatan nang dalauang binibini na si Urbana at ni Feliza na nagtuturo ng̃ mabuting kaugalian|year=1902|publisher=J. Martinez|url=https://books.google.com.ph/books?id=2C1BAQAAMAAJ&pg=PP61&dq=tapapecho&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwiIjN6x8M_7AhVlpFYBHTNtDJIQ6AF6BAgFEAI#v=onepage&q=tapapecho&f=false|text=Cum magsoot ang isang babaye nang barong nang̃ang̃aninag, ualang '''tapapecho''' ó panaquip sa dibdib, ay nacasusuclam tingnan...|t=If a woman wears a transparent clothing, without ['''covering for the chest'''], it is loathing to see...}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|author=Gémino H. Abad|title=Memories, Visions, and Scholarship, and Other Essays|year=2001|publisher=University of the Philippines, Center for Integrative and Development Studies|url=https://books.google.com.ph/books?id=e_5uAAAAMAAJ&q=tapapecho&dq=tapapecho&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwjo5r_68s_7AhUWr1YBHU5-DpQ4ChDoAXoECAgQAg|isbn=978-971-742-069-1|text=Sa pananamit, di dapat magsuot ang babae ng barong nanganganinag at kailangang laging may '''tapapecho''' o takip sa suso.|t=In clothing, a woman should not wear transparent clothes and always needed to have ['''breast covering'''].}}
#* {{quote-av|tl|year=2022|writer=w:Suzette Doctolero; et al.|director=Zig Dulay|actor=Julie Anne San Jose|role=Maria Clara|episode=Noli yarn?!|number=2|title=Maria Clara at Ibarra|network=GMA Network|text=Ipagpaumanhin mo kung aming tiningnan ang iyong '''tapa pecho'''. Ngayon lamang kami nakakita ng ganyan.|t=Please excuse us if we looked at your '''breast cover'''. We have only seen that today.}}

====Related terms====
{{rel3|tl|pitso|tapaboka|tapon}}

====See also====
{{col3|tl|salungso|bra}}

===Further reading===
* {{cite-book|author=Maneepin Phromsuthirak|title=Costumes in ASEAN|year=2000|publisher=National ASEAN Committee on Culture and Information of Thailand|url=https://books.google.com.ph/books?id=CfyBAAAAMAAJ&dq=tapapecho+filipinas&focus=searchwithinvolume&q=tapa+pecho|isbn=978-974-7102-83-3}}
* {{cite-book|author=Eric V. Cruz|title=The Terno: Its Development and Identity as the Filipino Women's National Costume|year=1982|publisher=U.P. College of Home Economics|url=https://books.google.com.ph/books?id=t7jfAAAAMAAJ&dq=tapapecho+filipinas&focus=searchwithinvolume&q=tapa+pecho}}
-------- end text --------
