Page 19368 tayo: Would save with comment = convert {{tl-IPA}} to {{tl-pr}} (2); incorporate {{audio|tl|Tl-PH-tayo.ogg|Audio}} into {{tl-pr}}; remove {{hyph}} same as respelling auto-syllabification (2)
Page 19368 tayo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
Possibly from {{m|tl|kata}} + ''*-yo'' (from {{m|tl|kayo}}/{{m|tl|ninyo}}), with omission of the initial ''ka''. Compare {{cog|tsg|taniyu}} ({{m|tsg|ta}} + {{m|tsg|niyu}}), {{cog|pag|tayo}} ({{m|pag|ta}} + {{m|pag|yo}}), and {{cog|pam|tamu}} ({{m|pam|ta}} + {{m|pam|mu}}).<ref>Liao, Hsiu-chuan. (2006) ''A Typology of First Person Dual Pronouns in Philippine Languages and Their Reconstructibility'', The Tenth International Conference on Austronesian Linguistics. [https://sil-philippines-languages.org/ical/handouts/liao_Phil_pronoun_recon.pdf]</ref> May also be borrowed from {{cog|ilo|-tayo}} with stress shift.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|+<audio:Tl-PH-tayo.ogg>}}

====Pronoun====
{{tl-pron|b=+}}

# [[we]]; [[us]] {{n-g|(inclusive of the person spoken to)}}
#: {{uxi|tl|Kain '''tayo'''!|Let '''us''' eat!}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|tayo-tayo|pantayo-tayo|tana|tayo na|tara}}

=====See also=====
{{tl-personal pronouns}}

===Etymology 2===

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|tayô}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|tayô|b=+}}

# [[act]] of [[stand]]ing {{q|on one's feet}}
#: {{syn|tl|pagtayo|tindig|pagtindig}}
# [[standing]] [[position]] {{q|of a person}}
#: {{syn|tl|pagkakatayo}}
# [[act]] of [[erect]]ing something {{gl|a building, statue, etc.}}
#: {{syn|tl|pagtatayo|tirik|pagtitirik}}
# [[act]] of [[organize|organizing]] or [[found]]ing
#: {{syn|tl|tatag|pagtatatag}}
# [[status]]; [[condition]] {{q|of one's project, health, etc.}}
#: {{syn|tl|lagay|kalagayan}}
# [[position]]; [[duty]] {{q|in an office}}
#: {{syn|tl|tungkulin|trabaho}}
# [[rank]]; [[state]]
#: {{syn|tl|estado|kalagayan}}
# [[site]]; [[location]]; [[position]]
#: {{syn|tl|puwesto|lagay|posisyon|lugar|kinatatayuan}}
# [[standpoint]]; [[stand]] {{q|on an issue}}
#: {{syn|tl|kinatatayuan|kinaroroonan}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|katayuan|kinatatayuan|ipagpatayo|itayo|magpatayo|magtayo|nakatayo|pagtatayo|pagtayo|patayo|patayuan|tayuan|tumayo|tumayo-tayo|magpatayo-tayo}}

====Verb====
{{tl-head|verb form|tayô|b=+}}

# {{inflection of|tl|tumayo||immediate imperative|mood}}

