===Etymology===
{{bor+|tl|en|ticket}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# [[ticket]] {{gl|pass entitling the holder to admission or boarding}}
#: {{syn|tl|bilyete}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=1965|author=Philippine Center for Language Study; Jean Donald Bowen|title=Beginning Tagalog: A Course for Speakers of English|publisher=Univ of California Press|page=501
|passage=Para mabili ang '''tiket''' niya C. i. Sina Antonia at Aurora 2. Noong Linggo 3. Petsa  otso 4 Si Antonia 5. Idinuldol sa kanilang mukha ang tiket 6. May tationg otso 7.  Kasi, petsa otso ang kaarawan ni Antonia 8. Para matuto ng liksiyon ang  mamang&nbsp;...}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=2014|author=Joi Barrios|title=Tagalog for Beginners: An Introduction to Filipino, the National Language of the Philippines (Downloadable MP3 Audio Included)|publisher=Tuttle Publishing|isbn=9781462910397
|passage=Sasakay siya sa Pasay Bus Terminal. Bababa siya sa Crossing ng U.P. Los  Baños. Halimbawa 2 Bibili ako ng '''tiket''' papuntang Bohol. Alas-dos ng hapon ang  alis ng eroplano. Alas-tres ang dating sa Bohol. Dalawang libong piso ang tiket.}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=2015|author=Joi Barrios; Julia Camagong|title=Easy Tagalog: Learn to Speak Tagalog Quickly (Downloadable CD-ROM)|publisher=Tuttle Publishing|isbn=9781462916771|page=222
|passage=YOU : Bakit po mahal ang '''tiket'''? TICKET AGENT : . Situation 2 You are buying  five bus tickets for a trip with your friends to go north to Banuae. You want to take  the very last bus. The bus leaves at 11:45 in the evening. The fare is usually two&nbsp;...}}
# [[ticket]] {{gl|list of candidates for an election}}
# [[ticket]] {{gl|citation for a violation, especially in traffic}}
# [[pass]]; [[free]] [[ticket]]
#: {{syn|tl|pases}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|tikitan|mantiket}}

-------- end text --------
