Page 19606 timawa: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|timaua|timagua||obsolete|Abecedario}}
* {{alt|tl|timagwa}}

===Etymology===
Possibly related to {{noncog|ms-cla|istimewa||special; privilege}}, which is said to have come from {{noncog|sa|आस्तामेव|lit=May it keep on being so.}}.

Compare {{cog|pam|timaua}}, {{cog|ceb|timawa}}, {{cog|hil|timawa}}, and {{cog|ilo|timmawa}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|timawà}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|timawà|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|colloquial}} [[glutton]]; [[voracious]] [[eater]]
#: {{syn|tl|patay-gutom}}
# {{lb|tl|colloquial}} [[mean]] or [[despicable]] [[person]]
# {{lb|tl|colloquial}} [[stupid]] [[person]]; [[fool]]
#: {{syn|tl|bobo|tanga}}
# {{lb|tl|colloquial|rare}} [[poor]] or [[destitute]] [[person]]
#: {{syn|tl|dukha|hampaslupa|busabos}}
# {{lb|tl|historical}} [[privileged]] [[intermediate]] [[class]]
# {{lb|tl|historical}} [[freeman]]; [[emancipated]] [[slave]]
# {{lb|tl|obsolete}} act of [[free]]ing oneself from [[danger]] or [[calamity]]
#: {{syn|tl|paglaya}}
# {{lb|tl|obsolete}} [[act]] of [[manumission]]

====Usage notes====
* The word '''''timawa''''' used to refer to privileged middle classes but during the Spanish period, the sense demoted to “[[freemen]]”. The meaning further evolved to its modern meaning to be “a [[poor]] person”.

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|timawain|matimawa|magtimawa|pagtimawaan|katimawaan|pagkatimawa|pagtimawa|tumimawa}}

====See also====
{{col3|tl|maharlika}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|timawà|b=+}}

# [[vile]]; [[abject]]
#: {{syn|tl|imbi|hamak|bulisik|bulisiksik}}
# {{lb|tl|colloquial}} [[poor]]
#: {{syn|tl|mahirap|dukha}}
# {{lb|tl|colloquial}} [[gluttonous]]
#: {{syn|tl|matakaw|masiba}}
# {{lb|tl|obsolete}} [[ignoble]]; [[plebeian]]
#: {{syn|tl|karaniwan|polista}}
# {{lb|tl|obsolete}} [[free]]; [[emancipated]] {{q|of a former slave}}
#: {{syn|tl|malaya}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1613|389|Libre) Timava (pp) ſin eſclauonia, ni rrico ni pobre, mang̃a timava, los libres, la jente comun del pueblo deſpues delos magnates}}
