===Etymology===
From {{inh|tl|phi-pro|*timuʀ||southeast monsoon}} (compare {{cog|ceb|timog||southeasterly wind}}, {{cog|cyo|timog}}, {{cog|ivv|timoy||rain}},  {{cog|msb|timog||north}}, and {{cog|tao|cimoy||rain}}), from {{inh|tl|poz-pro|*timuʀ||southeast monsoon}} (compare {{cog|mrw|timor||wind}}, {{cog|tsg|timul||northeast}}, {{cog|ace|timu||east}}, {{cog|haw|kimu||precipitation}}, {{cog|ms|timur||east}}, and {{cog|sm|timu||rain}}), from {{inh|tl|map-pro|*timuʀ||south or east wind}} (compare {{cog|ami|timol}}).

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|hmp=Timog}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# [[south]]
#: {{syn|tl|sur|q1=uncommon}}
#: {{ux|tl|Patungong '''timog''' ang mga manlalakbay.|The travellers are going towards the '''south'''.}}

====Coordinate terms====
* {{list:compass points/tl}}

