Page 19946 tsa: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|sa||obsolete}}
* {{alt|tl|cha}}
* {{alt|tl|saa|tsaa|chaa}}

===Etymology===
Ultimately from {{der|tl|zh|-}}, either through:
* {{der|tl|yue|茶}}, possibly via {{w|Macau Portuguese|Macau}} {{der|tl|pt|chá}} and next via {{w|Philippine Spanish|Philippine}} {{cog|es|cha}} as recorded in Abella (1874). 
* {{der|tl|cmn-wadegiles|-}} [[romanization]] of {{der|tl|cmn|茶|tr=chʻa<sup>2</sup>}} according to Manuel (1948)
The sense "gossip" is a {{semantic loan|tl|en|tea|t=information; gossip|nocap=1}} as in {{m|en|spill the tea}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# [[tea]] {{q|plant, leaves, and drink}}
# {{lb|tl|slang}} [[tea]] {{gl|information, especially [[gossip]]}}
#: {{ux|tl|Anong '''tsa''', mare?|What's the '''tea''', girl?}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|magtsa|pagtsatsa|tsaang-gubat|tsaang-parang|tsarera|eladong tsa}}

