===Etymology===
From {{af|tl|tubig|-an}}. The game of [[patintero]] is called as such, because one informally prepares the [[playing field]] via drawing lines on the ground ([[sand]] or [[soil]]) that look like tiny [[depression]]s on the [[ground]] [[reminiscent]] of [[irrigate]]d [[field]]s on [[farm]]s.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|+<n^fertile land; rice paddy; body of water><v^to water>|tubigán<n^[[patintero]] {{q|game}}; water container><a^aquatic, watery; fed up; water-filled>}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# [[fertile]] [[irrigated]] [[land]]; [[watery]] [[land]]; [[paddy]]; [[paddy field]]; [[rice paddy]]
# a [[body]] of [[water]] {{q|such as [[river]]s, [[lake]]s, [[sea]]s, [[water]] [[reservoir]]s, [[oases]], [[watering hole]]s}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|tubigan sa disyerto}}

===Verb===
{{tl-verb|+|tinubigan|tinutubigan|tutubigan|b=+}}

# to [[water]]; to [[add]] [[water]]
#: {{ux|tl|'''Tubigan''' mo itong halaman bago ito mamatay.|'''Water''' this plant before it dies.}}

===Related terms===
{{der3|tl|matubigan|pantubigan|patubigan}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|tubigán|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|playground games}} [[patintero]] {{gl|traditional Filipino children's game}}
# [[water]] [[container]]

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|tubigán|b=+}}

# [[aquatic]]; [[watery]]
# {{clipping of|tl|natubigan}}: [[fed up]]; [[burned out]]
# {{clipping of|tl|natubigan}}: [[filled]] with [[water]]

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|halamang tubigan}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:KWF Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1860}}

