Page 20379 ulianin: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|olianin||obsolete|Abecedario orthography}}
* {{alt|tl|uliyanin}}
* {{alt|tl|ulyanin}}

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|tl|ulian|in}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|uli7anin|+<qq:colloquial>}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|sometimes|offensive}}

# [[senile]]
#: {{syn|tl|ulian}}
# [[forgetful]] {{q|due to old age}}
#: {{syn|tl|ulian|malimutin|makalimutin}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|sometimes|offensive}}

# [[dotard]]
#: {{syn|tl|ulian}}

====Usage notes====
* As persons with mental disorders, including elderlies, are socially stigmatized in the Philippines, this is sometimes considered offensive if the condition has not been diagnosed with certainty.

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|pagkaulianin|mag-ulianin}}
-------- end text --------
