Page 20625 utot: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|otot||obsolete|Abecedario orthography}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|tl|poz-pro|*qutut||flatulence; to fart}}, from {{inh|tl|map-pro|*qətut||fart; flatulence}}. Cognate with {{cog|akl|utot}}, {{cog|bno|utot}}, {{cog|ceb|utut}}/''{{l|ceb|utut}}'', {{cog|mrw|tot}}, {{cog|war|tot}}. Compare {{cog|ms|kentut}} and {{cog|th|ตด}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|utót}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|utót|b=+}}

# [[fart]]; [[flatulence]]
#: {{ux|tl|Narinig ng lahat ang kanyang '''utot'''.|translation=Everyone heard his fart.}}
# [[act]] of [[fart]]ing
#: {{syn|tl|pag-utot}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|umutot|ututan|ututin|pag-utot}}

-------- end text --------
Page 20626 utoy: Removing explicit syllabification same as auto-syllabification: {{hyph|tl|u|toy}}
Page 20626 utoy: Replaced {{tl-IPA}} with {{tl-pr}}
Page 20626 utoy: Would save with comment = convert {{tl-IPA}} to {{tl-pr}}; remove {{hyph}} same as respelling auto-syllabification
Page 20626 utoy: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|otoy}}

===Etymology===
From {{suf|tl|utol|oy|t1=brother, comrade}}. Compare {{m|tl|totoy}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|chiefly|_|Batangas|affectionate}} {{n-g|term of address to a boy}}
#: {{syn|tl|totoy|toto|ito|ato|anak}}
#: {{coord|tl|neneng|ineng}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''Utoy''', kumusta ka na ga?|How are you, '''boy'''? {{gl|when addressing a young person}}}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=2014|author=Baldwin G. Gutierrez|title=I Survive: A Filipino Teacher's Journey to Teaching In the United States|publisher=Lulu Press, Inc|isbn=9781312275584
|passage=“'''Utoy''', ano gang kurso ang kukunin mo sa college (Brother, what course are you  going to take in college)?” I asked my brother once. “Hindi ko pa alam, ... Alamin  mo kung saan ka pwede magaral at pagtutulungan naminyan. Maganda nga&nbsp;...}}
#* {{quote-text|tl|year=2005|title=Gawad Ka Amado, 1999-2005
|passage=Patuloy na makikipagtalakayan kay Ka Mayo sina Rosa at Bert, samantalang  nilalaro ni Jun ang gitara ... Welga? [Hindi makakakibo sina Rosa at Bert, lalapit si Jun at hahabol si Mayo] TANDA: [Kay Jun] Welga ba ito, '''utoy'''? ... Pa-saan po  sila?}}

====Usage notes====
''Utoy'' is primarily used when addressing a young boy (usually by parents) or a person of lower status (by superiors), and usually comes first in sentences, but may come last. The term also entered mainstream Tagalog.
-------- end text --------
