Page 20699 Vigan: Already saw {{tl-pr}}, skipping: {{tl-pr}}
Page 20699 Vigan: Skipped, no changes
Page 20699 Vigan: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{bor+|tl|es|Vigan}}, also spelled as {{m|es|Bigan}} in early maps like the {{w|Velarde map}} (1734), originally from {{der|tl|ilo|Bigan}}. A common theory is that this word derived from {{cog|ilo|biga|t={{vern|giant taro}} / Biga'a ({{taxfmt|Alocasia macrorrhizos|species}})}} + {{m|ilo|-an|t=locative suffix}} where {{taxfmt|Alocasia macrorrhizos|species}} plants once grew abundantly along the banks of the [[Mestizo River]], from which Captain {{w|Juan de Salcedo}} derived the city's name, after a misunderstanding with the locals, thinking he was asking the name of the plants. The other theory derives this word from {{der|tl|nan-hbl|美岸|tr=Bí-gān|lit=beautiful coast}}, possibly by Chinese settlers in the area.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Proper noun===
{{tl-proper noun|b=+}}

# {{place|tl|t=Vigan|city/capital city|province/Ilocos Sur|c/Philippines}}
-------- end text --------
