===Etymology===
{{bor+|tl|es|Zamboanga}}, from {{der|tl|sml|Samboangan|t=mooring place}} from {{suffix|sml|samboang|an|t1=mooring pole|t2=place marker suffix|nocat=1}}, as attested in the [[w:Velarde map|Velarde Map]] (1734). A popular folk etymology may also attribute it to either {{cog|id|jambangan|t=flower garden}} or {{cog|ms|jambangan|t=flower garden}} or {{cog|tsg|jambangan|t=flower garden}} from {{suffix|ms|jambang|an|t1=flower pot|t2=place marker suffix}}, but this name has never been attested in any historical records prior to the 1960s with the place being attested usually instead as "Samboangan".<ref>{{cite-web|last=Enriquez|first=A.R.|title=Jambangan: the "Garden of Flowers" never was!|url=http://arenriquez.over-blog.com/article-jambangan-the-garden-of-flowers-never-was-83440368.html|site=Antonio Enriquez's name|date=September 5, 2011|accessdate=13 September 2016}}</ref>

