===Prefix===
{{tl-head|prefix form|b=+}}

# {{alternative form of|tl|pang-|nodot=1}}{{n-g|, if the [[root]] starts with [[bilabial]] [[consonant]]s, such as ''{{angbr|b}}'' or ''{{angbr|p}}'', which gets [[nasal]]ly [[assimilate]]d to the [[prefix]] [[ending]], especially with ''{{angbr|p}}'' or sometimes ''{{angbr|b}}''.}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|bati|t1=beat|pambati|t2=whisk}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|bahay|t1=house|pambahay|t2=for use at home}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|bura|t1=erasure|pambura|t2=eraser}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|palo|t1=spank|pamalo|t2=spanker}}

====Usage notes====
* When used before root initials {{IPAchar|/b/}} or {{IPAchar|/p/}}, the said initials sometimes undergo [[nasal]] [[assimilation]] to the [[prefix]] [[ending]].
*: {{prefixusex|tl|baril|t1=gun|[[pamamaril]]|t2=shooting}}
*: {{prefixusex|tl|bakod|t1=fence|[[pamakod]]|t2=[[fencing]] {{gl|material used to make fence}}}}
*: {{prefixusex|tl|punas|t1=wipe|[[pamunas]]|t2=rag; wiper}}
*: {{prefixusex|tl|paypay|t1=flap of air|[[pamaypay]]|t2=hand fan}}
* Native speakers sometimes use the prefix {{m|tl|pang-}} by default, instead of {{m|tl|pam-}} without any [[morpheme]] [[change]] to the word.
*: {{prefixusex|tl|altaff=pang-|punas|t1=wipe|[[pangpunas]]|t2=wiper|lit2=for wiping}}
*: {{prefixusex|tl|altaff=pang-|paypay|t1=flap of air|[[pangpaypay]]|lit2=for fanning}}
*: {{prefixusex|tl|altaff=pang-|bahay|t1=house|[[pangbahay]]|lit2=for use at home}}

====Derived terms====
{{prefixsee|tl}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
