Page 286 pan-: Skipped, no changes
Page 286 pan-: -------- begin text --------

===Prefix===
{{tl-head|prefix form|b=+}}

# {{alt form|tl|pang-|nodot=1}}{{n-g|, if the [[root]] starts with [[alveolar]] [[consonant]]s, such as ''{{angbr|d}}'', ''{{angbr|l}}'', ''{{angbr|n}}'', ''{{angbr|r}}'', ''{{angbr|s}}'', or ''{{angbr|t}}'', which [[sometimes]] gets [[nasal]]ly [[assimilate]]d to the [[prefix]] [[ending]] when starts with [[alveolar]] [[consonant]]s, ''{{angbr|s}}'', ''{{angbr|t}}'', or ''{{angbr|d}}''.}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|digma|t1=war|pandigma|t2=meant for war}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|diwa|t1=gist|pandiwa|t2=verb}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|lasa|t1=flavor|panlasa|t2=taste}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|samantala|t1=while|pansamantala|t2=temporary}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|sampalataya|t1=belief|pananampalataya|t2=faith}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|takip|t1=cover|pantakip|t2=an instrument used to cover something}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|talo|t1=defeat|panalo|t2=victory}}

====Usage notes====
* When used before root initials {{IPAchar|/d/}}, {{IPAchar|/s/}}, or {{IPAchar|/t/}}, the said initials sometimes undergo [[nasal]] [[assimilation]] to the [[prefix]] [[ending]].
*: {{prefixusex|tl|damit|t1=clothing|pananamit|t2=act of wearing clothes}}
*: {{prefixusex|tl|sulat|t1=writing|panulat|t2=writing instrument}}
*: {{prefixusex|tl|tinda|t1=sale|paninda|t2=merchandise}}
* Native speakers sometimes use the prefix {{m|tl|pang-}} by default, instead of {{m|tl|pan-}} without any [[morpheme]] [[change]] to the word.
*: {{prefixusex|tl|altaff=pang-|sulat|t1=writing|pangsulat|lit2=for writing}}
*: {{prefixusex|tl|altaff=pang-|takip|t1=cover|pangtakip|lit2=for covering}}

====Derived terms====
{{prefixsee|tl}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* https://learningtagalog.com/grammar/nouns/noun_affixes/pang.html
